    {
      "@id": "concept:crimes-legislation-amendment-serious-and-organised-crime-act-2010-sch-1-sec-4-2-ss-3",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "4(3) Crimes Legislation Amendment (Serious and Organised Crime) Act",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/crimes-legislation-amendment-serious-and-organised-crime-act-2010#sch-1-sec-4-2-ss-3"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "crimes-legislation-amendment-serious-and-organised-crime-act-2010.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "crimes-legislation-amendment-serious-and-organised-crime-act-2010.pdf, p.8",
      "values:originalText": "(3) The application for the order must be supported by an affidavit of\nan *authorised officer stating:\nComLaw Authoritative Act C2012C00115\n\nUnexplained wealth  Schedule 1\nMain amendments  Part 1\n\nCrimes Legislation Amendment (Serious and Organised Crime) Act 2010\n\n(a) that the authorised officer suspects that the *total wealth of\nthe *suspect exceeds the value of the suspect’s *wealth that\nwas *lawfully acquired; and\n\n(b) if the application is to restrain property of a person other than\nthe suspect but not to restrain *bankruptcy property of the\n*suspect—that the authorised officer suspects that the\nproperty is subject to the *effective control of the suspect;\nand\n\n(c) that the authorised officer suspects either or both of the\nfollowing:\n\n(i) that the suspect has committed an offence against a law\nof the Commonwealth, a *foreign indictable offence or a\n*State offence that has a federal aspect;\n\n(ii) that the whole or any part of the suspect’s wealth was\nderived from an offence against a law of the\nCommonwealth, a foreign indictable offence or a State\noffence that has a federal aspect.\nThe affidavit must include the grounds on which the authorised\nofficer holds those suspicions.\nLegal expenses",
      "skos:definition": "(3) The application for the order must be supported by an affidavit of\nan *authorised officer stating:\nComLaw Authoritative Act C2012C00115\n\nUnexplained wealth  Schedule 1\nMain amendments  Part 1\n\nCrimes Legislation Amendment (Serious and Organised Crime) Act 2010\n\n(a) that the authorised officer suspects that the *total wealth of\nthe *suspect exceeds the value of the suspect’s *wealth that\nwas *lawfully acquired; and\n\n(b) if the application is to restrain property of a person other than\nthe suspect but not to restrain *bankruptcy property of the\n*suspect—that the authorised officer suspects that the\nproperty is subject to the *effective control of the suspect;\nand\n\n(c) that the authorised officer suspects either or both of the\nfollowing:\n\n(i) that the suspect has committed an offence against a law\nof the Commonwealth, a *foreign indictable offence or a\n*State offence that has a federal aspect;\n\n(ii) that the whole or any part of the suspect’s wealth was\nderived from an offence against a law of the\nCommonwealth, a foreign indictable offence or a State\noffence that has a federal aspect.\nThe affidavit must include the grounds on which the authorised\nofficer holds those suspicions.\nLegal expenses",
      "values:partOf": {
        "@id": "concept:crimes-legislation-amendment-serious-and-organised-crime-act-2010-sch-1-sec-4-2"
      },
      "cml:asserts": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:crimes-legislation-amendment-serious-and-organised-crime-act-2010-sch-1-sec-4-2-ss-3-norm"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:crimes-legislation-amendment-serious-and-organised-crime-act-2010-sch-1-sec-4-2-ss-3-logic-deontic-1"
        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "090bd1220e7892fd057e70195ccb32c12c2ac415e8c476355aef2c842857fe33",
      "skos:note": "Affidavit must include grounds for suspicions about suspect's wealth and suspected offences.",
      "dc:description": "grounds for suspicions"
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/crimes-legislation-amendment-serious-and-organised-crime-act-2010#sch-1-sec-4-2-ss-3",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "4(3) Crimes Legislation Amendment (Serious and Organised Crime) Act",
      "values:kind": "subsection",
      "cof:pageNumber": 8,
      "values:originalText": "(3) The application for the order must be supported by an affidavit of\nan *authorised officer stating:\nComLaw Authoritative Act C2012C00115\n\nUnexplained wealth  Schedule 1\nMain amendments  Part 1\n\nCrimes Legislation Amendment (Serious and Organised Crime) Act 2010\n\n(a) that the authorised officer suspects that the *total wealth of\nthe *suspect exceeds the value of the suspect’s *wealth that\nwas *lawfully acquired; and\n\n(b) if the application is to restrain property of a person other than\nthe suspect but not to restrain *bankruptcy property of the\n*suspect—that the authorised officer suspects that the\nproperty is subject to the *effective control of the suspect;\nand\n\n(c) that the authorised officer suspects either or both of the\nfollowing:\n\n(i) that the suspect has committed an offence against a law\nof the Commonwealth, a *foreign indictable offence or a\n*State offence that has a federal aspect;\n\n(ii) that the whole or any part of the suspect’s wealth was\nderived from an offence against a law of the\nCommonwealth, a foreign indictable offence or a State\noffence that has a federal aspect.\nThe affidavit must include the grounds on which the authorised\nofficer holds those suspicions.\nLegal expenses"
    },
