      },
      "dc:source": "crimes-legislation-amendment-serious-and-organised-crime-act-2010.pdf, p.8",
      "values:originalText": "(4) Despite subsection (1), the court may refuse to make a *restraining\norder if the court is satisfied that it is not in the public interest to\nmake the order.\nComLaw Authoritative Act C2012C00115\n\nSchedule 1  Unexplained wealth",
      "skos:definition": "(4) Despite subsection (1), the court may refuse to make a *restraining\norder if the court is satisfied that it is not in the public interest to\nmake the order.\nComLaw Authoritative Act C2012C00115\n\nSchedule 1  Unexplained wealth",
      "values:partOf": {
        "@id": "concept:crimes-legislation-amendment-serious-and-organised-crime-act-2010-sch-1-sec-4-2"
      },
      "cml:asserts": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:crimes-legislation-amendment-serious-and-organised-crime-act-2010-sch-1-sec-4-2-ss-4-norm"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:crimes-legislation-amendment-serious-and-organised-crime-act-2010-sch-1-sec-4-2-ss-4-logic-deontic-1"
        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "b50778d77faf632c00c790476a9c5dc3ff41393abaafd422464e1d9a4e1d6244",
      "skos:note": "Court may refuse restraining order if not in public interest."
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/crimes-legislation-amendment-serious-and-organised-crime-act-2010#sch-1-sec-4-2-ss-4",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "4(4) Crimes Legislation Amendment (Serious and Organised Crime) Act",
      "values:kind": "subsection",
      "cof:pageNumber": 8,
      "values:originalText": "(4) Despite subsection (1), the court may refuse to make a *restraining\norder if the court is satisfied that it is not in the public interest to\nmake the order.\nComLaw Authoritative Act C2012C00115\n\nSchedule 1  Unexplained wealth"
    },
    {
      "@id": "concept:crimes-legislation-amendment-serious-and-organised-crime-act-2010-sch-1-sec-4-2-ss-4-norm",
