      "cml:confidence": {
        "@value": 1.0,
        "@type": "xsd:decimal"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      }
    },
    {
      "@id": "concept:crimes-legislation-amendment-serious-and-organised-crime-act-2010-sch-1-sec-6",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "6 Crimes Legislation Amendment (Serious and Organised Crime) Act",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/crimes-legislation-amendment-serious-and-organised-crime-act-2010#sch-1-sec-6"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "crimes-legislation-amendment-serious-and-organised-crime-act-2010.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "crimes-legislation-amendment-serious-and-organised-crime-act-2010.pdf, p.10",
      "values:originalText": "Note:\nA court can also refuse to make a restraining order if the\nCommonwealth refuses to give an undertaking: see section 21.\n\n(4A) If the court refuses to make a *restraining order under\nsubsection (1), it may make any order as to costs it considers\nappropriate, including costs on an indemnity basis.\nRisk of property being disposed of etc.\n\n(5) The court may make a *restraining order even if there is no risk of\nthe property being disposed of or otherwise dealt with.\nLater acquisitions of property\n\n(6) The court may specify that a *restraining order covers property that\nis acquired by the *suspect after the court makes the order.\nOtherwise, no property that is acquired after a court makes a\nrestraining order is covered by the order.",
      "skos:definition": "Note:\nA court can also refuse to make a restraining order if the\nCommonwealth refuses to give an undertaking: see section 21.\n\n(4A) If the court refuses to make a *restraining order under\nsubsection (1), it may make any order as to costs it considers\nappropriate, including costs on an indemnity basis.\nRisk of property being disposed of etc.\n\n(5) The court may make a *restraining order even if there is no risk of\nthe property being disposed of or otherwise dealt with.\nLater acquisitions of property\n\n(6) The court may specify that a *restraining order covers property that\nis acquired by the *suspect after the court makes the order.\nOtherwise, no property that is acquired after a court makes a\nrestraining order is covered by the order.",
      "cml:hasPart": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:crimes-legislation-amendment-serious-and-organised-crime-act-2010-sch-1-sec-6-ss-4a"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:crimes-legislation-amendment-serious-and-organised-crime-act-2010-sch-1-sec-6-ss-5"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:crimes-legislation-amendment-serious-and-organised-crime-act-2010-sch-1-sec-6-ss-6"
        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "8cbd13c684c4552c7a42518501abff97afd514eac420593a8c737a9a0c9f26be"
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/crimes-legislation-amendment-serious-and-organised-crime-act-2010#sch-1-sec-6",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "6 Crimes Legislation Amendment (Serious and Organised Crime) Act",
      "values:kind": "section",
      "cof:pageNumber": 10,
      "values:originalText": "Note:\nA court can also refuse to make a restraining order if the\nCommonwealth refuses to give an undertaking: see section 21.\n\n(4A) If the court refuses to make a *restraining order under\nsubsection (1), it may make any order as to costs it considers\nappropriate, including costs on an indemnity basis.\nRisk of property being disposed of etc.\n\n(5) The court may make a *restraining order even if there is no risk of\nthe property being disposed of or otherwise dealt with.\nLater acquisitions of property\n\n(6) The court may specify that a *restraining order covers property that\nis acquired by the *suspect after the court makes the order.\nOtherwise, no property that is acquired after a court makes a\nrestraining order is covered by the order."
    },
    {
