    {
      "@id": "concept:crimes-legislation-amendment-serious-and-organised-crime-act-2010-sch-1-sec-29a",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "29A Court may exclude property from a restraining order made",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/crimes-legislation-amendment-serious-and-organised-crime-act-2010#sch-1-sec-29a"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "crimes-legislation-amendment-serious-and-organised-crime-act-2010.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "crimes-legislation-amendment-serious-and-organised-crime-act-2010.pdf, p.10",
      "values:originalText": "under section 20A\n\nThe court to which an application for a *restraining order under\nsection 20A was made may, when the order is made or at a later\ntime, exclude specified property from the order if:\n\n(a) an application is made under section 30 or 31; and\n\n(b) the court is satisfied that:\n\n(i) the property is property of a person other than the\n*suspect; and\n\n(ii) the property is not subject to the *effective control of the\nsuspect.\nNote:\nSection 32 may prevent the court from hearing the application until\nthe DPP has had a reasonable opportunity to conduct an examination\nof the applicant.\nComLaw Authoritative Act C2012C00115\n\nUnexplained wealth  Schedule 1\nMain amendments  Part 1\n\nCrimes Legislation Amendment (Serious and Organised Crime) Act 2010",
      "skos:definition": "under section 20A\n\nThe court to which an application for a *restraining order under\nsection 20A was made may, when the order is made or at a later\ntime, exclude specified property from the order if:\n\n(a) an application is made under section 30 or 31; and\n\n(b) the court is satisfied that:\n\n(i) the property is property of a person other than the\n*suspect; and\n\n(ii) the property is not subject to the *effective control of the\nsuspect.\nNote:\nSection 32 may prevent the court from hearing the application until\nthe DPP has had a reasonable opportunity to conduct an examination\nof the applicant.\nComLaw Authoritative Act C2012C00115\n\nUnexplained wealth  Schedule 1\nMain amendments  Part 1\n\nCrimes Legislation Amendment (Serious and Organised Crime) Act 2010",
      "cml:asserts": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:crimes-legislation-amendment-serious-and-organised-crime-act-2010-sch-1-sec-29a-norm"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:crimes-legislation-amendment-serious-and-organised-crime-act-2010-sch-1-sec-29a-logic-deontic-1"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:crimes-legislation-amendment-serious-and-organised-crime-act-2010-sch-1-sec-29a-logic-alleninterval-2"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:crimes-legislation-amendment-serious-and-organised-crime-act-2010-sch-1-sec-29a-logic-ltl-3"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:crimes-legislation-amendment-serious-and-organised-crime-act-2010-sch-1-sec-29a-logic-deontic-4"
        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "44a86eb857b6719023565c0cc8194d56e77185515902923eebf1e694f399377c",
      "skos:note": "Court may exclude property from a restraining order made under section 20A."
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/crimes-legislation-amendment-serious-and-organised-crime-act-2010#sch-1-sec-29a",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "29A Court may exclude property from a restraining order made",
      "values:kind": "section",
      "cof:pageNumber": 10,
      "values:originalText": "under section 20A\n\nThe court to which an application for a *restraining order under\nsection 20A was made may, when the order is made or at a later\ntime, exclude specified property from the order if:\n\n(a) an application is made under section 30 or 31; and\n\n(b) the court is satisfied that:\n\n(i) the property is property of a person other than the\n*suspect; and\n\n(ii) the property is not subject to the *effective control of the\nsuspect.\nNote:\nSection 32 may prevent the court from hearing the application until\nthe DPP has had a reasonable opportunity to conduct an examination\nof the applicant.\nComLaw Authoritative Act C2012C00115\n\nUnexplained wealth  Schedule 1\nMain amendments  Part 1\n\nCrimes Legislation Amendment (Serious and Organised Crime) Act 2010"
    },
