    {
      "@id": "concept:crimes-legislation-amendment-serious-and-organised-crime-act-2010-sch-1-sec-45a",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "45A Cessation of restraining orders relating to unexplained wealth",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/crimes-legislation-amendment-serious-and-organised-crime-act-2010#sch-1-sec-45a"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "crimes-legislation-amendment-serious-and-organised-crime-act-2010.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "crimes-legislation-amendment-serious-and-organised-crime-act-2010.pdf, p.11",
      "values:originalText": "(1) A *restraining order made under section 20A ceases to be in force\nif, within 28 days after the order was made, no application for an\n*unexplained wealth order has been made in relation to the *suspect\nto whom the restraining order relates.\n\n(2) A *restraining order made under section 20A ceases to be in force\nif:\n\n(a) an application for an *unexplained wealth order is made in\nrelation to the *suspect to whom the restraining order relates;\nand\n\n(b) the application is made within 28 days after the making of\nthe restraining order; and\n\n(c) the court refuses to make the unexplained wealth order; and\n\n(d) one of the following applies:\nComLaw Authoritative Act C2012C00115\n\nSchedule 1  Unexplained wealth",
      "skos:definition": "(1) A *restraining order made under section 20A ceases to be in force\nif, within 28 days after the order was made, no application for an\n*unexplained wealth order has been made in relation to the *suspect\nto whom the restraining order relates.\n\n(2) A *restraining order made under section 20A ceases to be in force\nif:\n\n(a) an application for an *unexplained wealth order is made in\nrelation to the *suspect to whom the restraining order relates;\nand\n\n(b) the application is made within 28 days after the making of\nthe restraining order; and\n\n(c) the court refuses to make the unexplained wealth order; and\n\n(d) one of the following applies:\nComLaw Authoritative Act C2012C00115\n\nSchedule 1  Unexplained wealth",
      "cml:hasPart": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:crimes-legislation-amendment-serious-and-organised-crime-act-2010-sch-1-sec-45a-ss-1"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:crimes-legislation-amendment-serious-and-organised-crime-act-2010-sch-1-sec-45a-ss-2"
        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "ae540fe17ee928092399a3fed1e1351a969dc20918eab02e3aa30925e6e01963"
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/crimes-legislation-amendment-serious-and-organised-crime-act-2010#sch-1-sec-45a",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "45A Cessation of restraining orders relating to unexplained wealth",
      "values:kind": "section",
      "cof:pageNumber": 11,
      "values:originalText": "(1) A *restraining order made under section 20A ceases to be in force\nif, within 28 days after the order was made, no application for an\n*unexplained wealth order has been made in relation to the *suspect\nto whom the restraining order relates.\n\n(2) A *restraining order made under section 20A ceases to be in force\nif:\n\n(a) an application for an *unexplained wealth order is made in\nrelation to the *suspect to whom the restraining order relates;\nand\n\n(b) the application is made within 28 days after the making of\nthe restraining order; and\n\n(c) the court refuses to make the unexplained wealth order; and\n\n(d) one of the following applies:\nComLaw Authoritative Act C2012C00115\n\nSchedule 1  Unexplained wealth"
    },
