    },
    {
      "@id": "concept:crimes-legislation-amendment-serious-and-organised-crime-act-2010-sch-1-sec-8-2",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "8 Crimes Legislation Amendment (Serious and Organised Crime) Act",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/crimes-legislation-amendment-serious-and-organised-crime-act-2010#sch-1-sec-8-2"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "crimes-legislation-amendment-serious-and-organised-crime-act-2010.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "crimes-legislation-amendment-serious-and-organised-crime-act-2010.pdf, p.12",
      "values:originalText": "(i) the time for an appeal against the refusal has expired\nwithout an appeal being lodged;\n\n(ii) an appeal against the refusal has lapsed;\n\n(iii) an appeal against the refusal has been dismissed and\nfinally disposed of.\n\n(3) A *restraining order made under section 20A ceases to be in force\nif:\n\n(a) an application for an *unexplained wealth order is made in\nrelation to the *suspect to whom the restraining order relates;\nand\n\n(b) the application is made within 28 days after the making of\nthe restraining order; and\n\n(c) the court makes the unexplained wealth order; and\n\n(d) either:\n\n(i) the unexplained wealth order is complied with; or\n\n(ii) an appeal against the unexplained wealth order has been\nupheld and finally disposed of.\n\n(4) If a *restraining order ceases under subsection (1) or (2), the court\nmay, on application by a person with an *interest in the property\ncovered by the restraining order, make any order as to costs it\nconsiders appropriate, including costs on an indemnity basis.",
      "skos:definition": "(i) the time for an appeal against the refusal has expired\nwithout an appeal being lodged;\n\n(ii) an appeal against the refusal has lapsed;\n\n(iii) an appeal against the refusal has been dismissed and\nfinally disposed of.\n\n(3) A *restraining order made under section 20A ceases to be in force\nif:\n\n(a) an application for an *unexplained wealth order is made in\nrelation to the *suspect to whom the restraining order relates;\nand\n\n(b) the application is made within 28 days after the making of\nthe restraining order; and\n\n(c) the court makes the unexplained wealth order; and\n\n(d) either:\n\n(i) the unexplained wealth order is complied with; or\n\n(ii) an appeal against the unexplained wealth order has been\nupheld and finally disposed of.\n\n(4) If a *restraining order ceases under subsection (1) or (2), the court\nmay, on application by a person with an *interest in the property\ncovered by the restraining order, make any order as to costs it\nconsiders appropriate, including costs on an indemnity basis.",
      "cml:hasPart": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:crimes-legislation-amendment-serious-and-organised-crime-act-2010-sch-1-sec-8-2-ss-3"
        },
