      "cml:confidence": {
        "@value": 1.0,
        "@type": "xsd:decimal"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      }
    },
    {
      "@id": "concept:crimes-legislation-amendment-serious-and-organised-crime-act-2010-sch-1-sec-179b",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "179B Making an order requiring a person to appear",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/crimes-legislation-amendment-serious-and-organised-crime-act-2010#sch-1-sec-179b"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "crimes-legislation-amendment-serious-and-organised-crime-act-2010.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "crimes-legislation-amendment-serious-and-organised-crime-act-2010.pdf, p.13",
      "values:originalText": "(1) A court with *proceeds jurisdiction may make an order (a\npreliminary unexplained wealth order) requiring a person to\nappear before the court for the purpose of enabling the court to\ndecide whether or not to make an *unexplained wealth order in\nrelation to the person if:\n\n(a) the *DPP applies for an unexplained wealth order in relation\nto the person; and\n\n(b) the court is satisfied that an *authorised officer has\nreasonable grounds to suspect that the person’s *total wealth\nexceeds the value of the person’s *wealth that was *lawfully\nacquired; and\n\n(c) any affidavit requirements in subsection (2) for the\napplication have been met.\nAffidavit requirements\n\n(2) An application for an *unexplained wealth order in relation to a\nperson must be supported by an affidavit of an *authorised officer\nstating:\n\n(a) the identity of the person; and\n\n(b) that the authorised officer suspects that the person’s *total\nwealth exceeds the value of the person’s *wealth that was\n*lawfully acquired; and\n\n(c) the following:\n\n(i) the property the authorised officer knows or reasonably\nsuspects was lawfully acquired by the person;\n\n(ii) the property the authorised officer knows or reasonably\nsuspects is owned by the person or is under the\n*effective control of the person.\nThe affidavit must include the grounds on which the authorised\nofficer holds the suspicions referred to in paragraphs (b) and (c).\nComLaw Authoritative Act C2012C00115\n\nSchedule 1  Unexplained wealth",
      "skos:definition": "(1) A court with *proceeds jurisdiction may make an order (a\npreliminary unexplained wealth order) requiring a person to\nappear before the court for the purpose of enabling the court to\ndecide whether or not to make an *unexplained wealth order in\nrelation to the person if:\n\n(a) the *DPP applies for an unexplained wealth order in relation\nto the person; and\n\n(b) the court is satisfied that an *authorised officer has\nreasonable grounds to suspect that the person’s *total wealth\nexceeds the value of the person’s *wealth that was *lawfully\nacquired; and\n\n(c) any affidavit requirements in subsection (2) for the\napplication have been met.\nAffidavit requirements\n\n(2) An application for an *unexplained wealth order in relation to a\nperson must be supported by an affidavit of an *authorised officer\nstating:\n\n(a) the identity of the person; and\n\n(b) that the authorised officer suspects that the person’s *total\nwealth exceeds the value of the person’s *wealth that was\n*lawfully acquired; and\n\n(c) the following:\n\n(i) the property the authorised officer knows or reasonably\nsuspects was lawfully acquired by the person;\n\n(ii) the property the authorised officer knows or reasonably\nsuspects is owned by the person or is under the\n*effective control of the person.\nThe affidavit must include the grounds on which the authorised\nofficer holds the suspicions referred to in paragraphs (b) and (c).\nComLaw Authoritative Act C2012C00115\n\nSchedule 1  Unexplained wealth",
      "cml:hasPart": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:crimes-legislation-amendment-serious-and-organised-crime-act-2010-sch-1-sec-179b-ss-1"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:crimes-legislation-amendment-serious-and-organised-crime-act-2010-sch-1-sec-179b-ss-2"
        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "683dab7f8df56fe0d9eb6eb5c1a1d48e0162ddd4506fb28a3007a8effbc5a5a4"
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/crimes-legislation-amendment-serious-and-organised-crime-act-2010#sch-1-sec-179b",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "179B Making an order requiring a person to appear",
      "values:kind": "section",
      "cof:pageNumber": 13,
      "values:originalText": "(1) A court with *proceeds jurisdiction may make an order (a\npreliminary unexplained wealth order) requiring a person to\nappear before the court for the purpose of enabling the court to\ndecide whether or not to make an *unexplained wealth order in\nrelation to the person if:\n\n(a) the *DPP applies for an unexplained wealth order in relation\nto the person; and\n\n(b) the court is satisfied that an *authorised officer has\nreasonable grounds to suspect that the person’s *total wealth\nexceeds the value of the person’s *wealth that was *lawfully\nacquired; and\n\n(c) any affidavit requirements in subsection (2) for the\napplication have been met.\nAffidavit requirements\n\n(2) An application for an *unexplained wealth order in relation to a\nperson must be supported by an affidavit of an *authorised officer\nstating:\n\n(a) the identity of the person; and\n\n(b) that the authorised officer suspects that the person’s *total\nwealth exceeds the value of the person’s *wealth that was\n*lawfully acquired; and\n\n(c) the following:\n\n(i) the property the authorised officer knows or reasonably\nsuspects was lawfully acquired by the person;\n\n(ii) the property the authorised officer knows or reasonably\nsuspects is owned by the person or is under the\n*effective control of the person.\nThe affidavit must include the grounds on which the authorised\nofficer holds the suspicions referred to in paragraphs (b) and (c).\nComLaw Authoritative Act C2012C00115\n\nSchedule 1  Unexplained wealth"
    },
