    {
      "@id": "concept:crimes-legislation-amendment-serious-and-organised-crime-act-2010-sch-1-sec-179e",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "179E Making an unexplained wealth order",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/crimes-legislation-amendment-serious-and-organised-crime-act-2010#sch-1-sec-179e"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "crimes-legislation-amendment-serious-and-organised-crime-act-2010.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "crimes-legislation-amendment-serious-and-organised-crime-act-2010.pdf, p.15",
      "values:originalText": "(1) A court with *proceeds jurisdiction may make an order (an\nunexplained wealth order) requiring a person to pay an amount to\nthe Commonwealth if:\n\n(a) the court has made a *preliminary unexplained wealth order\nin relation to the person; and\n\n(b) the court is not satisfied that the whole or any part of the\nperson’s *wealth was not derived from one or more of the\nfollowing:\n\n(i) an offence against a law of the Commonwealth;\n\n(ii) a *foreign indictable offence;\n\n(iii) a *State offence that has a federal aspect.\n\n(2) The court must specify in the order that the person is liable to pay\nto the Commonwealth an amount (the person’s unexplained\nwealth amount) equal to the amount that, in the opinion of the\ncourt, is the difference between:\n\n(a) the person’s *total wealth; and\n\n(b) the sum of the values of the property that the court is satisfied\nwas not derived from one or more of the following:\n\n(i) an offence against a law of the Commonwealth;\n\n(ii) a *foreign indictable offence;\n\n(iii) a *State offence that has a federal aspect;\nComLaw Authoritative Act C2012C00115\n\nSchedule 1  Unexplained wealth",
      "skos:definition": "(1) A court with *proceeds jurisdiction may make an order (an\nunexplained wealth order) requiring a person to pay an amount to\nthe Commonwealth if:\n\n(a) the court has made a *preliminary unexplained wealth order\nin relation to the person; and\n\n(b) the court is not satisfied that the whole or any part of the\nperson’s *wealth was not derived from one or more of the\nfollowing:\n\n(i) an offence against a law of the Commonwealth;\n\n(ii) a *foreign indictable offence;\n\n(iii) a *State offence that has a federal aspect.\n\n(2) The court must specify in the order that the person is liable to pay\nto the Commonwealth an amount (the person’s unexplained\nwealth amount) equal to the amount that, in the opinion of the\ncourt, is the difference between:\n\n(a) the person’s *total wealth; and\n\n(b) the sum of the values of the property that the court is satisfied\nwas not derived from one or more of the following:\n\n(i) an offence against a law of the Commonwealth;\n\n(ii) a *foreign indictable offence;\n\n(iii) a *State offence that has a federal aspect;\nComLaw Authoritative Act C2012C00115\n\nSchedule 1  Unexplained wealth",
      "cml:hasPart": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:crimes-legislation-amendment-serious-and-organised-crime-act-2010-sch-1-sec-179e-ss-1"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:crimes-legislation-amendment-serious-and-organised-crime-act-2010-sch-1-sec-179e-ss-2"
        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "0f42f1f3d22f4329c88013ff66270720f8aec36059313eb3c6f49f4c8f8c7cc5"
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/crimes-legislation-amendment-serious-and-organised-crime-act-2010#sch-1-sec-179e",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "179E Making an unexplained wealth order",
      "values:kind": "section",
      "cof:pageNumber": 15,
      "values:originalText": "(1) A court with *proceeds jurisdiction may make an order (an\nunexplained wealth order) requiring a person to pay an amount to\nthe Commonwealth if:\n\n(a) the court has made a *preliminary unexplained wealth order\nin relation to the person; and\n\n(b) the court is not satisfied that the whole or any part of the\nperson’s *wealth was not derived from one or more of the\nfollowing:\n\n(i) an offence against a law of the Commonwealth;\n\n(ii) a *foreign indictable offence;\n\n(iii) a *State offence that has a federal aspect.\n\n(2) The court must specify in the order that the person is liable to pay\nto the Commonwealth an amount (the person’s unexplained\nwealth amount) equal to the amount that, in the opinion of the\ncourt, is the difference between:\n\n(a) the person’s *total wealth; and\n\n(b) the sum of the values of the property that the court is satisfied\nwas not derived from one or more of the following:\n\n(i) an offence against a law of the Commonwealth;\n\n(ii) a *foreign indictable offence;\n\n(iii) a *State offence that has a federal aspect;\nComLaw Authoritative Act C2012C00115\n\nSchedule 1  Unexplained wealth"
    },
