    {
      "@id": "concept:crimes-legislation-amendment-serious-and-organised-crime-act-2010-sch-1-sec-179f",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "179F Ancillary orders",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/crimes-legislation-amendment-serious-and-organised-crime-act-2010#sch-1-sec-179f"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "crimes-legislation-amendment-serious-and-organised-crime-act-2010.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "crimes-legislation-amendment-serious-and-organised-crime-act-2010.pdf, p.16",
      "values:originalText": "(1) A court that makes an *unexplained wealth order, or any other\ncourt that could have made the unexplained wealth order, may\nmake orders ancillary to the order, either when the order is made or\nat a later time.\nComLaw Authoritative Act C2012C00115\n\nUnexplained wealth  Schedule 1\nMain amendments  Part 1\n\nCrimes Legislation Amendment (Serious and Organised Crime) Act 2010\n\n(2) A court that makes a *preliminary unexplained wealth order, or any\nother court that could have made the order, may make orders\nancillary to the order, either when the order is made or at a later\ntime.",
      "skos:definition": "(1) A court that makes an *unexplained wealth order, or any other\ncourt that could have made the unexplained wealth order, may\nmake orders ancillary to the order, either when the order is made or\nat a later time.\nComLaw Authoritative Act C2012C00115\n\nUnexplained wealth  Schedule 1\nMain amendments  Part 1\n\nCrimes Legislation Amendment (Serious and Organised Crime) Act 2010\n\n(2) A court that makes a *preliminary unexplained wealth order, or any\nother court that could have made the order, may make orders\nancillary to the order, either when the order is made or at a later\ntime.",
      "cml:hasPart": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:crimes-legislation-amendment-serious-and-organised-crime-act-2010-sch-1-sec-179f-ss-1"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:crimes-legislation-amendment-serious-and-organised-crime-act-2010-sch-1-sec-179f-ss-2"
        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "368473828daa97dc0f9a7e24e3004e57416eaf32150c72cba3a2d3f41847426e"
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/crimes-legislation-amendment-serious-and-organised-crime-act-2010#sch-1-sec-179f",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "179F Ancillary orders",
      "values:kind": "section",
      "cof:pageNumber": 16,
      "values:originalText": "(1) A court that makes an *unexplained wealth order, or any other\ncourt that could have made the unexplained wealth order, may\nmake orders ancillary to the order, either when the order is made or\nat a later time.\nComLaw Authoritative Act C2012C00115\n\nUnexplained wealth  Schedule 1\nMain amendments  Part 1\n\nCrimes Legislation Amendment (Serious and Organised Crime) Act 2010\n\n(2) A court that makes a *preliminary unexplained wealth order, or any\nother court that could have made the order, may make orders\nancillary to the order, either when the order is made or at a later\ntime."
    },
