    {
      "@id": "concept:crimes-legislation-amendment-serious-and-organised-crime-act-2010-sch-1-sec-179l",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "179L Relieving certain dependants from hardship",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/crimes-legislation-amendment-serious-and-organised-crime-act-2010#sch-1-sec-179l"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "crimes-legislation-amendment-serious-and-organised-crime-act-2010.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "crimes-legislation-amendment-serious-and-organised-crime-act-2010.pdf, p.19",
      "values:originalText": "(1) The court making an *unexplained wealth order in relation to a\nperson must make another order directing the Commonwealth,\nonce the unexplained wealth order is satisfied, to pay a specified\namount to a *dependant of the person if the court is satisfied that:\n\n(a) the unexplained wealth order would cause hardship to the\ndependant; and\n\n(b) the specified amount would relieve that hardship; and\n\n(c) if the dependant is aged at least 18 years—the dependant had\nno knowledge of the person’s conduct that is the subject of\nthe unexplained wealth order.\n\n(2) The specified amount must not exceed the person’s *unexplained\nwealth amount.\nComLaw Authoritative Act C2012C00115\n\nSchedule 1  Unexplained wealth",
      "skos:definition": "(1) The court making an *unexplained wealth order in relation to a\nperson must make another order directing the Commonwealth,\nonce the unexplained wealth order is satisfied, to pay a specified\namount to a *dependant of the person if the court is satisfied that:\n\n(a) the unexplained wealth order would cause hardship to the\ndependant; and\n\n(b) the specified amount would relieve that hardship; and\n\n(c) if the dependant is aged at least 18 years—the dependant had\nno knowledge of the person’s conduct that is the subject of\nthe unexplained wealth order.\n\n(2) The specified amount must not exceed the person’s *unexplained\nwealth amount.\nComLaw Authoritative Act C2012C00115\n\nSchedule 1  Unexplained wealth",
      "cml:hasPart": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:crimes-legislation-amendment-serious-and-organised-crime-act-2010-sch-1-sec-179l-ss-1"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:crimes-legislation-amendment-serious-and-organised-crime-act-2010-sch-1-sec-179l-ss-2"
        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "e92748386ee421104401a97dbfc7f73de711d671f53de930d47ca550dc223edb"
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/crimes-legislation-amendment-serious-and-organised-crime-act-2010#sch-1-sec-179l",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "179L Relieving certain dependants from hardship",
      "values:kind": "section",
      "cof:pageNumber": 19,
      "values:originalText": "(1) The court making an *unexplained wealth order in relation to a\nperson must make another order directing the Commonwealth,\nonce the unexplained wealth order is satisfied, to pay a specified\namount to a *dependant of the person if the court is satisfied that:\n\n(a) the unexplained wealth order would cause hardship to the\ndependant; and\n\n(b) the specified amount would relieve that hardship; and\n\n(c) if the dependant is aged at least 18 years—the dependant had\nno knowledge of the person’s conduct that is the subject of\nthe unexplained wealth order.\n\n(2) The specified amount must not exceed the person’s *unexplained\nwealth amount.\nComLaw Authoritative Act C2012C00115\n\nSchedule 1  Unexplained wealth"
    },
