      "cml:integrityHash": "9643596455b3fe679f08c37e4427e5753dea4c8e35d398d9e09612e5038c1173",
      "skos:note": "Provide written notice and a copy of the application to the person subject to the unexplained wealth order.",
      "dc:description": "true"
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/crimes-legislation-amendment-serious-and-organised-crime-act-2010#sch-1-sec-179n-ss-2",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "179N(2) Notice of application",
      "values:kind": "subsection",
      "cof:pageNumber": 20,
      "values:originalText": "(2) If a court with *proceeds jurisdiction makes a *preliminary\nunexplained wealth order in relation to the person, the *DPP must,\nwithin 7 days of the making of the order:\n\n(a) give written notice of the order to the person who would be\nsubject to the *unexplained wealth order if it were made; and\n\n(b) provide to the person a copy of the application for the\nunexplained wealth order, and the affidavit referred to in\nsubsection 179B(2)."
    },
