    {
      "@id": "concept:crimes-legislation-amendment-serious-and-organised-crime-act-2010-sch-1-sec-179p",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "179P Additional application for an unexplained wealth order",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/crimes-legislation-amendment-serious-and-organised-crime-act-2010#sch-1-sec-179p"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "crimes-legislation-amendment-serious-and-organised-crime-act-2010.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "crimes-legislation-amendment-serious-and-organised-crime-act-2010.pdf, p.20",
      "values:originalText": "(1) The *DPP cannot, unless the court gives leave, apply for an\n*unexplained wealth order against a person if:\n\n(a) an application has previously been made for an unexplained\nwealth order in relation to the person; and\n\n(b) the application has been finally determined on the merits.\n\n(2) The court must not give leave unless it is satisfied that:\n\n(a) the *wealth to which the new application relates was\nidentified only after the first application was determined; or\nComLaw Authoritative Act C2012C00115\n\nUnexplained wealth  Schedule 1\nMain amendments  Part 1\n\nCrimes Legislation Amendment (Serious and Organised Crime) Act 2010\n\n(b) necessary evidence became available only after the first\napplication was determined; or\n\n(c) it is in the interests of justice to give the leave.",
      "skos:definition": "(1) The *DPP cannot, unless the court gives leave, apply for an\n*unexplained wealth order against a person if:\n\n(a) an application has previously been made for an unexplained\nwealth order in relation to the person; and\n\n(b) the application has been finally determined on the merits.\n\n(2) The court must not give leave unless it is satisfied that:\n\n(a) the *wealth to which the new application relates was\nidentified only after the first application was determined; or\nComLaw Authoritative Act C2012C00115\n\nUnexplained wealth  Schedule 1\nMain amendments  Part 1\n\nCrimes Legislation Amendment (Serious and Organised Crime) Act 2010\n\n(b) necessary evidence became available only after the first\napplication was determined; or\n\n(c) it is in the interests of justice to give the leave.",
      "cml:hasPart": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:crimes-legislation-amendment-serious-and-organised-crime-act-2010-sch-1-sec-179p-ss-1"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:crimes-legislation-amendment-serious-and-organised-crime-act-2010-sch-1-sec-179p-ss-2"
        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "24ca5523d85f2e6722117423f5bb4476da9ce5216de4b1239ed69bd7f739e02d"
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/crimes-legislation-amendment-serious-and-organised-crime-act-2010#sch-1-sec-179p",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "179P Additional application for an unexplained wealth order",
      "values:kind": "section",
      "cof:pageNumber": 20,
      "values:originalText": "(1) The *DPP cannot, unless the court gives leave, apply for an\n*unexplained wealth order against a person if:\n\n(a) an application has previously been made for an unexplained\nwealth order in relation to the person; and\n\n(b) the application has been finally determined on the merits.\n\n(2) The court must not give leave unless it is satisfied that:\n\n(a) the *wealth to which the new application relates was\nidentified only after the first application was determined; or\nComLaw Authoritative Act C2012C00115\n\nUnexplained wealth  Schedule 1\nMain amendments  Part 1\n\nCrimes Legislation Amendment (Serious and Organised Crime) Act 2010\n\n(b) necessary evidence became available only after the first\napplication was determined; or\n\n(c) it is in the interests of justice to give the leave."
    },
