    {
      "@id": "concept:crimes-legislation-amendment-serious-and-organised-crime-act-2010-sch-1-sec-18-ss-3",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "18(3) Crimes Legislation Amendment (Serious and Organised Crime) Act",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/crimes-legislation-amendment-serious-and-organised-crime-act-2010#sch-1-sec-18-ss-3"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "crimes-legislation-amendment-serious-and-organised-crime-act-2010.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "crimes-legislation-amendment-serious-and-organised-crime-act-2010.pdf, p.22",
      "values:originalText": "(3) A *restraining order may be made in respect of the property as if:\n\n(a) the property were the *person’s property; and\n\n(b) there were reasonable grounds to suspect that:\n\n(i) the person had committed an offence against a law of\nthe Commonwealth, a *foreign indictable offence or a\n*State offence that has a federal aspect;\n\n(ii) the whole or any part of the person’s wealth was derived\nfrom an offence against a law of the Commonwealth, a\nforeign indictable offence or a State offence that has a\nfederal aspect.",
      "skos:definition": "(3) A *restraining order may be made in respect of the property as if:\n\n(a) the property were the *person’s property; and\n\n(b) there were reasonable grounds to suspect that:\n\n(i) the person had committed an offence against a law of\nthe Commonwealth, a *foreign indictable offence or a\n*State offence that has a federal aspect;\n\n(ii) the whole or any part of the person’s wealth was derived\nfrom an offence against a law of the Commonwealth, a\nforeign indictable offence or a State offence that has a\nfederal aspect.",
      "values:partOf": {
        "@id": "concept:crimes-legislation-amendment-serious-and-organised-crime-act-2010-sch-1-sec-18"
      },
      "cml:asserts": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:crimes-legislation-amendment-serious-and-organised-crime-act-2010-sch-1-sec-18-ss-3-norm"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:crimes-legislation-amendment-serious-and-organised-crime-act-2010-sch-1-sec-18-ss-3-logic-deontic-1"
        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "bcec77ced84cd6ce73a940b099dbe405b6b071ca389d67e83bc23403374bf48d",
      "skos:note": "Granting of restraining order in respect of property"
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/crimes-legislation-amendment-serious-and-organised-crime-act-2010#sch-1-sec-18-ss-3",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "18(3) Crimes Legislation Amendment (Serious and Organised Crime) Act",
      "values:kind": "subsection",
      "cof:pageNumber": 22,
      "values:originalText": "(3) A *restraining order may be made in respect of the property as if:\n\n(a) the property were the *person’s property; and\n\n(b) there were reasonable grounds to suspect that:\n\n(i) the person had committed an offence against a law of\nthe Commonwealth, a *foreign indictable offence or a\n*State offence that has a federal aspect;\n\n(ii) the whole or any part of the person’s wealth was derived\nfrom an offence against a law of the Commonwealth, a\nforeign indictable offence or a State offence that has a\nfederal aspect."
    },
