    {
      "@id": "concept:crimes-legislation-amendment-serious-and-organised-crime-act-2010-sch-1-sec-179sa",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "179SA Legal expenses",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/crimes-legislation-amendment-serious-and-organised-crime-act-2010#sch-1-sec-179sa"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "crimes-legislation-amendment-serious-and-organised-crime-act-2010.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "crimes-legislation-amendment-serious-and-organised-crime-act-2010.pdf, p.22",
      "values:originalText": "(1) If the court considers that it is appropriate to do so, it may order\nthat the whole, or a specified part, of specified property covered by\nan order under subsection 179S(1) is not available to satisfy the\n*unexplained wealth order and may instead be disposed of or\notherwise dealt with for the purposes of meeting a person’s\nreasonable legal expenses arising from an application under this\nAct.\nComLaw Authoritative Act C2012C00115\n\nUnexplained wealth  Schedule 1\nMain amendments  Part 1\n\nCrimes Legislation Amendment (Serious and Organised Crime) Act 2010\n\n(2) The court may require that a costs assessor certify that legal\nexpenses have been properly incurred before permitting the\npayment of expenses from the disposal of any property covered by\nan order under subsection (1) and may make any further or\nancillary orders it considers appropriate.",
      "skos:definition": "(1) If the court considers that it is appropriate to do so, it may order\nthat the whole, or a specified part, of specified property covered by\nan order under subsection 179S(1) is not available to satisfy the\n*unexplained wealth order and may instead be disposed of or\notherwise dealt with for the purposes of meeting a person’s\nreasonable legal expenses arising from an application under this\nAct.\nComLaw Authoritative Act C2012C00115\n\nUnexplained wealth  Schedule 1\nMain amendments  Part 1\n\nCrimes Legislation Amendment (Serious and Organised Crime) Act 2010\n\n(2) The court may require that a costs assessor certify that legal\nexpenses have been properly incurred before permitting the\npayment of expenses from the disposal of any property covered by\nan order under subsection (1) and may make any further or\nancillary orders it considers appropriate.",
      "cml:hasPart": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:crimes-legislation-amendment-serious-and-organised-crime-act-2010-sch-1-sec-179sa-ss-1"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:crimes-legislation-amendment-serious-and-organised-crime-act-2010-sch-1-sec-179sa-ss-2"
        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "b5f6bc525fed2c8dad7ac550b555cc09e80a9e8cb40994b7b7d1b235373b112f"
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/crimes-legislation-amendment-serious-and-organised-crime-act-2010#sch-1-sec-179sa",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "179SA Legal expenses",
      "values:kind": "section",
      "cof:pageNumber": 22,
      "values:originalText": "(1) If the court considers that it is appropriate to do so, it may order\nthat the whole, or a specified part, of specified property covered by\nan order under subsection 179S(1) is not available to satisfy the\n*unexplained wealth order and may instead be disposed of or\notherwise dealt with for the purposes of meeting a person’s\nreasonable legal expenses arising from an application under this\nAct.\nComLaw Authoritative Act C2012C00115\n\nUnexplained wealth  Schedule 1\nMain amendments  Part 1\n\nCrimes Legislation Amendment (Serious and Organised Crime) Act 2010\n\n(2) The court may require that a costs assessor certify that legal\nexpenses have been properly incurred before permitting the\npayment of expenses from the disposal of any property covered by\nan order under subsection (1) and may make any further or\nancillary orders it considers appropriate."
    },
