          "@id": "concept:crimes-legislation-amendment-serious-and-organised-crime-act-2010-sch-1-sec-179sa-ss-1-logic-deontic-1"
        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "b0638b92046fdeea8a3bfc1ca80a1dc0ea5cae4f6251ef7b27bd0e8ca90cfd33",
      "skos:note": "Court may order specified property not available to satisfy unexplained wealth order for legal expenses."
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/crimes-legislation-amendment-serious-and-organised-crime-act-2010#sch-1-sec-179sa-ss-1",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "179SA(1) Legal expenses",
      "values:kind": "subsection",
      "cof:pageNumber": 22,
      "values:originalText": "(1) If the court considers that it is appropriate to do so, it may order\nthat the whole, or a specified part, of specified property covered by\nan order under subsection 179S(1) is not available to satisfy the\n*unexplained wealth order and may instead be disposed of or\notherwise dealt with for the purposes of meeting a person’s\nreasonable legal expenses arising from an application under this\nAct.\nComLaw Authoritative Act C2012C00115\n\nUnexplained wealth  Schedule 1\nMain amendments  Part 1\n\nCrimes Legislation Amendment (Serious and Organised Crime) Act 2010"
    },
    {
      "@id": "concept:crimes-legislation-amendment-serious-and-organised-crime-act-2010-sch-1-sec-179sa-ss-1-norm",
      "@type": "values:Permission",
