    {
      "@id": "concept:crimes-legislation-amendment-serious-and-organised-crime-act-2010-sch-1-sec-179t",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "179T Amounts exceeding the court’s jurisdiction",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/crimes-legislation-amendment-serious-and-organised-crime-act-2010#sch-1-sec-179t"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "crimes-legislation-amendment-serious-and-organised-crime-act-2010.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "crimes-legislation-amendment-serious-and-organised-crime-act-2010.pdf, p.23",
      "values:originalText": "(1) If:\n\n(a) a court makes an *unexplained wealth order of a particular\namount; and\n\n(b) the court does not have jurisdiction with respect to the\nrecovery of debts of an amount equal to that amount;\nthe registrar of the court must issue a certificate containing the\nparticulars specified in the regulations.\n\n(2) The certificate may be registered, in accordance with the\nregulations, in a court having jurisdiction with respect to the\nrecovery of debts of an amount equal to the amount of the relevant\norder.\n\n(3) Upon registration in a court, the certificate is enforceable in all\nrespects as a final judgment of the court in favour of the\nCommonwealth.",
      "skos:definition": "(1) If:\n\n(a) a court makes an *unexplained wealth order of a particular\namount; and\n\n(b) the court does not have jurisdiction with respect to the\nrecovery of debts of an amount equal to that amount;\nthe registrar of the court must issue a certificate containing the\nparticulars specified in the regulations.\n\n(2) The certificate may be registered, in accordance with the\nregulations, in a court having jurisdiction with respect to the\nrecovery of debts of an amount equal to the amount of the relevant\norder.\n\n(3) Upon registration in a court, the certificate is enforceable in all\nrespects as a final judgment of the court in favour of the\nCommonwealth.",
      "cml:hasPart": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:crimes-legislation-amendment-serious-and-organised-crime-act-2010-sch-1-sec-179t-ss-1"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:crimes-legislation-amendment-serious-and-organised-crime-act-2010-sch-1-sec-179t-ss-2"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:crimes-legislation-amendment-serious-and-organised-crime-act-2010-sch-1-sec-179t-ss-3"
        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "85c39a3821f66df1144a0fce7a598f710f7f0c5cc757d1a8171c0d438cfb3347"
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/crimes-legislation-amendment-serious-and-organised-crime-act-2010#sch-1-sec-179t",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "179T Amounts exceeding the court’s jurisdiction",
      "values:kind": "section",
      "cof:pageNumber": 23,
      "values:originalText": "(1) If:\n\n(a) a court makes an *unexplained wealth order of a particular\namount; and\n\n(b) the court does not have jurisdiction with respect to the\nrecovery of debts of an amount equal to that amount;\nthe registrar of the court must issue a certificate containing the\nparticulars specified in the regulations.\n\n(2) The certificate may be registered, in accordance with the\nregulations, in a court having jurisdiction with respect to the\nrecovery of debts of an amount equal to the amount of the relevant\norder.\n\n(3) Upon registration in a court, the certificate is enforceable in all\nrespects as a final judgment of the court in favour of the\nCommonwealth."
    },
