      "dc:source": "crimes-legislation-amendment-serious-and-organised-crime-act-2010.pdf, p.24",
      "values:originalText": "(4) The court that made the *unexplained wealth order or the\n*restraining order may, on application by the *DPP, make the\ndirection if:\nComLaw Authoritative Act C2012C00115\n\nUnexplained wealth  Schedule 1\nMain amendments  Part 1\n\nCrimes Legislation Amendment (Serious and Organised Crime) Act 2010\n\n(a) the unexplained wealth order has been made against the\nperson; and\n\n(b) the restraining order has been made:\n\n(i) against the person under section 20A; or\n\n(ii) against property of another person in relation to which\nan order is in force under section 179S in relation to the\nunexplained wealth order.\nNote:\nThe heading to section 282 is altered by adding at the end “in relation to certain\nrestraining orders”.",
      "skos:definition": "(4) The court that made the *unexplained wealth order or the\n*restraining order may, on application by the *DPP, make the\ndirection if:\nComLaw Authoritative Act C2012C00115\n\nUnexplained wealth  Schedule 1\nMain amendments  Part 1\n\nCrimes Legislation Amendment (Serious and Organised Crime) Act 2010\n\n(a) the unexplained wealth order has been made against the\nperson; and\n\n(b) the restraining order has been made:\n\n(i) against the person under section 20A; or\n\n(ii) against property of another person in relation to which\nan order is in force under section 179S in relation to the\nunexplained wealth order.\nNote:\nThe heading to section 282 is altered by adding at the end “in relation to certain\nrestraining orders”.",
      "values:partOf": {
        "@id": "concept:crimes-legislation-amendment-serious-and-organised-crime-act-2010-sch-1-sec-282a"
      },
      "cml:asserts": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:crimes-legislation-amendment-serious-and-organised-crime-act-2010-sch-1-sec-282a-ss-4-norm"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:crimes-legislation-amendment-serious-and-organised-crime-act-2010-sch-1-sec-282a-ss-4-logic-deontic-1"
        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "2d5f454d9c02f4bb146bc091152916c0d433a050705306e96bc73f1f8ba97c71",
      "skos:note": "Court direction to Official Trustee on unexplained wealth order or restraining order application"
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/crimes-legislation-amendment-serious-and-organised-crime-act-2010#sch-1-sec-282a-ss-4",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "282A(4) Direction by a court to the Official Trustee in relation to",
      "values:kind": "subsection",
      "cof:pageNumber": 24,
      "values:originalText": "(4) The court that made the *unexplained wealth order or the\n*restraining order may, on application by the *DPP, make the\ndirection if:\nComLaw Authoritative Act C2012C00115\n\nUnexplained wealth  Schedule 1\nMain amendments  Part 1\n\nCrimes Legislation Amendment (Serious and Organised Crime) Act 2010\n\n(a) the unexplained wealth order has been made against the\nperson; and\n\n(b) the restraining order has been made:\n\n(i) against the person under section 20A; or\n\n(ii) against property of another person in relation to which\nan order is in force under section 179S in relation to the\nunexplained wealth order.\nNote:\nThe heading to section 282 is altered by adding at the end “in relation to certain\nrestraining orders”."
    },
