    },
    {
      "@id": "concept:crimes-legislation-amendment-serious-and-organised-crime-act-2010-sch-2-sec-15b",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "15B Making freezing orders",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/crimes-legislation-amendment-serious-and-organised-crime-act-2010#sch-2-sec-15b"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "crimes-legislation-amendment-serious-and-organised-crime-act-2010.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "crimes-legislation-amendment-serious-and-organised-crime-act-2010.pdf, p.32",
      "values:originalText": "(1) A magistrate must order that a *financial institution not allow a\nwithdrawal from an *account with the institution, except in the\nmanner and circumstances specified in the order, if:\n\n(a) an *authorised officer described in paragraph (a), (aa), (b) or\n(c) of the definition of authorised officer in section 338\napplies for the order in accordance with Division 2; and\n\n(b) there are reasonable grounds to suspect that the balance of\nthe account:\n\n(i) is *proceeds of an *indictable offence, a *foreign\nindictable offence or an *indictable offence of\nCommonwealth concern (whether or not the identity of\nthe person who committed the offence is known); or\n\n(ii) is wholly or partly an *instrument of a *serious offence;\nand\n\n(c) the magistrate is satisfied that, unless an order is made under\nthis section, there is a risk that the balance of the account will\nbe reduced so that a person will not be deprived of all or\nsome of such proceeds or such an instrument.\nNote 1:\nParagraphs (a), (aa), (b) and (c) of the definition of authorised officer\nin section 338 cover certain AFP members, certain members of the\nAustralian Commission for Law Enforcement Integrity, certain\nmembers of the Australian Crime Commission and certain officers of\nCustoms.\nNote 2:\nThe balance of the account may be proceeds of an offence even\nthough the balance is only partly derived from the offence: see\nsection 329.\n\n(2) An order made under subsection (1) covers the balance of the\n*account from time to time.\nComLaw Authoritative Act C2012C00115\n\nOther amendments relating to proceeds of crime  Schedule 2\nFreezing orders  Part 1\n\nCrimes Legislation Amendment (Serious and Organised Crime) Act 2010\nOrder need not be based on commission of particular offence\n\n(3) The reasonable grounds referred to in paragraph (1)(b), and the\nsatisfaction referred to in paragraph (1)(c), need not be based on a\nfinding as to the commission of a particular offence.",
      "skos:definition": "(1) A magistrate must order that a *financial institution not allow a\nwithdrawal from an *account with the institution, except in the\nmanner and circumstances specified in the order, if:\n\n(a) an *authorised officer described in paragraph (a), (aa), (b) or\n(c) of the definition of authorised officer in section 338\napplies for the order in accordance with Division 2; and\n\n(b) there are reasonable grounds to suspect that the balance of\nthe account:\n\n(i) is *proceeds of an *indictable offence, a *foreign\nindictable offence or an *indictable offence of\nCommonwealth concern (whether or not the identity of\nthe person who committed the offence is known); or\n\n(ii) is wholly or partly an *instrument of a *serious offence;\nand\n\n(c) the magistrate is satisfied that, unless an order is made under\nthis section, there is a risk that the balance of the account will\nbe reduced so that a person will not be deprived of all or\nsome of such proceeds or such an instrument.\nNote 1:\nParagraphs (a), (aa), (b) and (c) of the definition of authorised officer\nin section 338 cover certain AFP members, certain members of the\nAustralian Commission for Law Enforcement Integrity, certain\nmembers of the Australian Crime Commission and certain officers of\nCustoms.\nNote 2:\nThe balance of the account may be proceeds of an offence even\nthough the balance is only partly derived from the offence: see\nsection 329.\n\n(2) An order made under subsection (1) covers the balance of the\n*account from time to time.\nComLaw Authoritative Act C2012C00115\n\nOther amendments relating to proceeds of crime  Schedule 2\nFreezing orders  Part 1\n\nCrimes Legislation Amendment (Serious and Organised Crime) Act 2010\nOrder need not be based on commission of particular offence\n\n(3) The reasonable grounds referred to in paragraph (1)(b), and the\nsatisfaction referred to in paragraph (1)(c), need not be based on a\nfinding as to the commission of a particular offence.",
      "cml:hasPart": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:crimes-legislation-amendment-serious-and-organised-crime-act-2010-sch-2-sec-15b-ss-1"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:crimes-legislation-amendment-serious-and-organised-crime-act-2010-sch-2-sec-15b-ss-2"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:crimes-legislation-amendment-serious-and-organised-crime-act-2010-sch-2-sec-15b-ss-3"
        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "5eef84e64a5bbe3c9cba2140721ec4b83bd5df46261df1fe9055b202cd7782ed"
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/crimes-legislation-amendment-serious-and-organised-crime-act-2010#sch-2-sec-15b",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "15B Making freezing orders",
      "values:kind": "section",
      "cof:pageNumber": 32,
      "values:originalText": "(1) A magistrate must order that a *financial institution not allow a\nwithdrawal from an *account with the institution, except in the\nmanner and circumstances specified in the order, if:\n\n(a) an *authorised officer described in paragraph (a), (aa), (b) or\n(c) of the definition of authorised officer in section 338\napplies for the order in accordance with Division 2; and\n\n(b) there are reasonable grounds to suspect that the balance of\nthe account:\n\n(i) is *proceeds of an *indictable offence, a *foreign\nindictable offence or an *indictable offence of\nCommonwealth concern (whether or not the identity of\nthe person who committed the offence is known); or\n\n(ii) is wholly or partly an *instrument of a *serious offence;\nand\n\n(c) the magistrate is satisfied that, unless an order is made under\nthis section, there is a risk that the balance of the account will\nbe reduced so that a person will not be deprived of all or\nsome of such proceeds or such an instrument.\nNote 1:\nParagraphs (a), (aa), (b) and (c) of the definition of authorised officer\nin section 338 cover certain AFP members, certain members of the\nAustralian Commission for Law Enforcement Integrity, certain\nmembers of the Australian Crime Commission and certain officers of\nCustoms.\nNote 2:\nThe balance of the account may be proceeds of an offence even\nthough the balance is only partly derived from the offence: see\nsection 329.\n\n(2) An order made under subsection (1) covers the balance of the\n*account from time to time.\nComLaw Authoritative Act C2012C00115\n\nOther amendments relating to proceeds of crime  Schedule 2\nFreezing orders  Part 1\n\nCrimes Legislation Amendment (Serious and Organised Crime) Act 2010\nOrder need not be based on commission of particular offence\n\n(3) The reasonable grounds referred to in paragraph (1)(b), and the\nsatisfaction referred to in paragraph (1)(c), need not be based on a\nfinding as to the commission of a particular offence."
    },
