    {
      "@id": "concept:crimes-legislation-amendment-serious-and-organised-crime-act-2010-sch-2-sec-15c",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "15C Affidavit supporting application made in person",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/crimes-legislation-amendment-serious-and-organised-crime-act-2010#sch-2-sec-15c"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "crimes-legislation-amendment-serious-and-organised-crime-act-2010.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "crimes-legislation-amendment-serious-and-organised-crime-act-2010.pdf, p.33",
      "values:originalText": "If an *authorised officer applies in person to a magistrate for a\n*freezing order relating to an *account with a *financial institution,\nthe application must be supported by an affidavit of an authorised\nofficer described in paragraph (a), (aa), (b) or (c) of the definition\nof authorised officer in section 338:\n\n(a) setting out sufficient information to identify the account (for\nexample, the account number); and\n\n(b) identifying the financial institution; and\n\n(c) setting out the grounds to suspect that the balance of the\naccount:\n\n(i) is *proceeds of an *indictable offence, a *foreign\nindictable offence or an *indictable offence of\nCommonwealth concern; or\n\n(ii) is wholly or partly an *instrument of a *serious offence;\nand\n\n(d) setting out the grounds on which a person could be satisfied\nthat, unless the order is made, there is a risk that the balance\nof the account will be reduced so that a person will not be\ndeprived of all or some of such proceeds or of such an\ninstrument.\nNote:\nParagraphs (a), (aa), (b) and (c) of the definition of authorised officer\nin section 338 cover certain AFP members, certain members of the\nAustralian Commission for Law Enforcement Integrity, certain\nmembers of the Australian Crime Commission and certain officers of\nCustoms.",
      "skos:definition": "If an *authorised officer applies in person to a magistrate for a\n*freezing order relating to an *account with a *financial institution,\nthe application must be supported by an affidavit of an authorised\nofficer described in paragraph (a), (aa), (b) or (c) of the definition\nof authorised officer in section 338:\n\n(a) setting out sufficient information to identify the account (for\nexample, the account number); and\n\n(b) identifying the financial institution; and\n\n(c) setting out the grounds to suspect that the balance of the\naccount:\n\n(i) is *proceeds of an *indictable offence, a *foreign\nindictable offence or an *indictable offence of\nCommonwealth concern; or\n\n(ii) is wholly or partly an *instrument of a *serious offence;\nand\n\n(d) setting out the grounds on which a person could be satisfied\nthat, unless the order is made, there is a risk that the balance\nof the account will be reduced so that a person will not be\ndeprived of all or some of such proceeds or of such an\ninstrument.\nNote:\nParagraphs (a), (aa), (b) and (c) of the definition of authorised officer\nin section 338 cover certain AFP members, certain members of the\nAustralian Commission for Law Enforcement Integrity, certain\nmembers of the Australian Crime Commission and certain officers of\nCustoms.",
      "cml:asserts": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:crimes-legislation-amendment-serious-and-organised-crime-act-2010-sch-2-sec-15c-norm"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:crimes-legislation-amendment-serious-and-organised-crime-act-2010-sch-2-sec-15c-logic-deontic-1"
        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "715e5662b824648ca72b61ef2e69983fc7c44cebe43e2b592a350fdd1013b4ed",
      "skos:note": "Application for freezing order must be supported by affidavit of authorised officer",
      "dc:description": "affidavit supporting application made in person"
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/crimes-legislation-amendment-serious-and-organised-crime-act-2010#sch-2-sec-15c",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "15C Affidavit supporting application made in person",
      "values:kind": "section",
      "cof:pageNumber": 33,
      "values:originalText": "If an *authorised officer applies in person to a magistrate for a\n*freezing order relating to an *account with a *financial institution,\nthe application must be supported by an affidavit of an authorised\nofficer described in paragraph (a), (aa), (b) or (c) of the definition\nof authorised officer in section 338:\n\n(a) setting out sufficient information to identify the account (for\nexample, the account number); and\n\n(b) identifying the financial institution; and\n\n(c) setting out the grounds to suspect that the balance of the\naccount:\n\n(i) is *proceeds of an *indictable offence, a *foreign\nindictable offence or an *indictable offence of\nCommonwealth concern; or\n\n(ii) is wholly or partly an *instrument of a *serious offence;\nand\n\n(d) setting out the grounds on which a person could be satisfied\nthat, unless the order is made, there is a risk that the balance\nof the account will be reduced so that a person will not be\ndeprived of all or some of such proceeds or of such an\ninstrument.\nNote:\nParagraphs (a), (aa), (b) and (c) of the definition of authorised officer\nin section 338 cover certain AFP members, certain members of the\nAustralian Commission for Law Enforcement Integrity, certain\nmembers of the Australian Crime Commission and certain officers of\nCustoms."
    },
