      "dc:source": "crimes-legislation-amendment-serious-and-organised-crime-act-2010.pdf, p.34",
      "values:originalText": "(1) The magistrate may complete and sign the same form of *freezing\norder that would be made under section 15B if satisfied that:\n\n(a) a freezing order should be issued urgently; or\n\n(b) the delay that would occur if an application were made in\nperson would frustrate the effectiveness of the order.",
      "skos:definition": "(1) The magistrate may complete and sign the same form of *freezing\norder that would be made under section 15B if satisfied that:\n\n(a) a freezing order should be issued urgently; or\n\n(b) the delay that would occur if an application were made in\nperson would frustrate the effectiveness of the order.",
      "values:partOf": {
        "@id": "concept:crimes-legislation-amendment-serious-and-organised-crime-act-2010-sch-2-sec-30"
      },
      "cml:asserts": [
