      },
      "dc:source": "crimes-legislation-amendment-serious-and-organised-crime-act-2010.pdf, p.34",
      "values:originalText": "(3) The applicant must then:\n\n(a) complete a form of *freezing order in terms substantially\ncorresponding to those given by the magistrate; and\n\n(b) state on the form:\n\n(i) the name of the magistrate; and\n\n(ii) the day on which the order was signed; and\nComLaw Authoritative Act C2012C00115\n\nOther amendments relating to proceeds of crime  Schedule 2\nFreezing orders  Part 1\n\nCrimes Legislation Amendment (Serious and Organised Crime) Act 2010\n\n(iii) the time at which the order was signed.",
      "skos:definition": "(3) The applicant must then:\n\n(a) complete a form of *freezing order in terms substantially\ncorresponding to those given by the magistrate; and\n\n(b) state on the form:\n\n(i) the name of the magistrate; and\n\n(ii) the day on which the order was signed; and\nComLaw Authoritative Act C2012C00115\n\nOther amendments relating to proceeds of crime  Schedule 2\nFreezing orders  Part 1\n\nCrimes Legislation Amendment (Serious and Organised Crime) Act 2010\n\n(iii) the time at which the order was signed.",
      "values:partOf": {
        "@id": "concept:crimes-legislation-amendment-serious-and-organised-crime-act-2010-sch-2-sec-30"
      },
      "cml:asserts": [
