          "@id": "concept:crimes-legislation-amendment-serious-and-organised-crime-act-2010-sch-2-sec-15h-ss-4-logic-deontic-1"
        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "24f25abd1964b97f2cebd359cb2461327069b273d3a3afc643ca548691f184ef",
      "skos:note": "Giving a false document to a financial institution after obtaining a freezing order is an offence."
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/crimes-legislation-amendment-serious-and-organised-crime-act-2010#sch-2-sec-15h-ss-4",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "15H(4) Offences relating to orders made under section 15E",
      "values:kind": "subsection",
      "cof:pageNumber": 36,
      "values:originalText": "(4) A person commits an offence if:\n\n(a) the person gives a magistrate a form of *freezing order under\nsection 15E relating to a *financial institution; and\n\n(b) the person does so after presenting to the financial institution\na document purporting to be a form of the freezing order; and\n\n(c) the form given to the magistrate is not in the same form as\nthe document presented to the financial institution.\nPenalty: Imprisonment for 2 years or 120 penalty units, or both."
    },
    {
      "@id": "concept:crimes-legislation-amendment-serious-and-organised-crime-act-2010-sch-2-sec-15h-ss-4-norm",
