    {
      "@id": "concept:crimes-legislation-amendment-serious-and-organised-crime-act-2010-sch-2-sec-15j",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "15J Service of freezing order etc. on financial institution and",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/crimes-legislation-amendment-serious-and-organised-crime-act-2010#sch-2-sec-15j"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "crimes-legislation-amendment-serious-and-organised-crime-act-2010.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "crimes-legislation-amendment-serious-and-organised-crime-act-2010.pdf, p.37",
      "values:originalText": "account-holder\n\n(1) If a magistrate makes a *freezing order relating to an *account with\na *financial institution, the applicant for the order must cause the\nthings described in subsection (2) to be given to:\n\n(a) the financial institution; and\n\n(b) each person in whose name the account is held.\n\n(2) The things are as follows:\n\n(a) a copy of the order (or of a form of the order under\nsection 15E);\n\n(b) a written statement of the name and contact details of the\n*enforcement agency mentioned in the paragraph of the\ndefinition of authorised officer in section 338 that describes\nthe applicant.\nNote:\nIf the copy of the order is given to the financial institution after the\nend of the first working day after the order is made, the order does not\ncome into force: see subsection 15N(1).",
      "skos:definition": "account-holder\n\n(1) If a magistrate makes a *freezing order relating to an *account with\na *financial institution, the applicant for the order must cause the\nthings described in subsection (2) to be given to:\n\n(a) the financial institution; and\n\n(b) each person in whose name the account is held.\n\n(2) The things are as follows:\n\n(a) a copy of the order (or of a form of the order under\nsection 15E);\n\n(b) a written statement of the name and contact details of the\n*enforcement agency mentioned in the paragraph of the\ndefinition of authorised officer in section 338 that describes\nthe applicant.\nNote:\nIf the copy of the order is given to the financial institution after the\nend of the first working day after the order is made, the order does not\ncome into force: see subsection 15N(1).",
      "cml:hasPart": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:crimes-legislation-amendment-serious-and-organised-crime-act-2010-sch-2-sec-15j-ss-1"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:crimes-legislation-amendment-serious-and-organised-crime-act-2010-sch-2-sec-15j-ss-2"
        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "8ad60c8d10a33eab307c352cecbba17cea3ca580d25a7e407e05c0572fc3fedb"
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/crimes-legislation-amendment-serious-and-organised-crime-act-2010#sch-2-sec-15j",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "15J Service of freezing order etc. on financial institution and",
      "values:kind": "section",
      "cof:pageNumber": 37,
      "values:originalText": "account-holder\n\n(1) If a magistrate makes a *freezing order relating to an *account with\na *financial institution, the applicant for the order must cause the\nthings described in subsection (2) to be given to:\n\n(a) the financial institution; and\n\n(b) each person in whose name the account is held.\n\n(2) The things are as follows:\n\n(a) a copy of the order (or of a form of the order under\nsection 15E);\n\n(b) a written statement of the name and contact details of the\n*enforcement agency mentioned in the paragraph of the\ndefinition of authorised officer in section 338 that describes\nthe applicant.\nNote:\nIf the copy of the order is given to the financial institution after the\nend of the first working day after the order is made, the order does not\ncome into force: see subsection 15N(1)."
    },
