      }
    },
    {
      "@id": "concept:crimes-legislation-amendment-serious-and-organised-crime-act-2010-sch-2-sec-15m",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "15M Protection from suits etc. for those complying with orders",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/crimes-legislation-amendment-serious-and-organised-crime-act-2010#sch-2-sec-15m"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "crimes-legislation-amendment-serious-and-organised-crime-act-2010.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "crimes-legislation-amendment-serious-and-organised-crime-act-2010.pdf, p.38",
      "values:originalText": "No action, suit or proceeding lies against:\n\n(a) a *financial institution; or\n\n(b) an *officer or *agent of the institution acting in the course of\nthat person’s employment or agency;\nin relation to any action taken by the institution or person in\ncomplying with a *freezing order or in the mistaken belief that\naction was required under a freezing order.\nNote:\nThis section does not affect any action that may lie against anyone\nelse for the making or operation of a freezing order.",
      "skos:definition": "No action, suit or proceeding lies against:\n\n(a) a *financial institution; or\n\n(b) an *officer or *agent of the institution acting in the course of\nthat person’s employment or agency;\nin relation to any action taken by the institution or person in\ncomplying with a *freezing order or in the mistaken belief that\naction was required under a freezing order.\nNote:\nThis section does not affect any action that may lie against anyone\nelse for the making or operation of a freezing order.",
      "cml:asserts": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:crimes-legislation-amendment-serious-and-organised-crime-act-2010-sch-2-sec-15m-norm"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:crimes-legislation-amendment-serious-and-organised-crime-act-2010-sch-2-sec-15m-logic-deontic-1"
        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "b10302a473c60e287529031eb8ef0ecccc4524e6319a8705947d56c73ea08b78",
      "skos:note": "Protection from suits for those complying with orders"
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/crimes-legislation-amendment-serious-and-organised-crime-act-2010#sch-2-sec-15m",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "15M Protection from suits etc. for those complying with orders",
      "values:kind": "section",
      "cof:pageNumber": 38,
      "values:originalText": "No action, suit or proceeding lies against:\n\n(a) a *financial institution; or\n\n(b) an *officer or *agent of the institution acting in the course of\nthat person’s employment or agency;\nin relation to any action taken by the institution or person in\ncomplying with a *freezing order or in the mistaken belief that\naction was required under a freezing order.\nNote:\nThis section does not affect any action that may lie against anyone\nelse for the making or operation of a freezing order."
    },
    {
      "@id": "concept:crimes-legislation-amendment-serious-and-organised-crime-act-2010-sch-2-sec-15m-norm",
      "@type": "values:Obligation",
      "cml:modality": {
        "@id": "cml:Deontic"
      },
      "values:partOf": {
        "@id": "concept:crimes-legislation-amendment-serious-and-organised-crime-act-2010-sch-2-sec-15m"
      },
      "values:deonticStatus": {
        "@id": "values:HeuristicDerived"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "values:borneBy": {
        "@id": "values:State"
      },
      "skos:scopeNote": "borne by: State"
    },
    {
      "@id": "concept:crimes-legislation-amendment-serious-and-organised-crime-act-2010-sch-2-sec-15m-logic-deontic-1",
      "@type": "cml:LogicApplication",
      "cml:modality": {
        "@id": "cml:Deontic"
      },
      "cml:operator": "Obligation",
      "cml:logicSummary": "Obligation to comply with orders",
      "cml:executionSurface": "modalities::logic::deontic",
      "cml:confidence": {
        "@value": 1.0,
        "@type": "xsd:decimal"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      }
    },
    {
      "@id": "concept:crimes-legislation-amendment-serious-and-organised-crime-act-2010-sch-2-sec-15p",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "15P Order extending a freezing order",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/crimes-legislation-amendment-serious-and-organised-crime-act-2010#sch-2-sec-15p"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "crimes-legislation-amendment-serious-and-organised-crime-act-2010.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "crimes-legislation-amendment-serious-and-organised-crime-act-2010.pdf, p.39",
      "values:originalText": "(1) A magistrate may make an order extending the period specified in\na *freezing order made in relation to an *account with a *financial\ninstitution if:\n\n(a) an *authorised officer described in paragraph (a), (aa), (b) or\n(c) of the definition of authorised officer in section 338\napplies for the extension; and\n\n(b) the magistrate is satisfied that an application has been made\nto a court (but not decided by the court) for a *restraining\norder to cover the account (whether or not the restraining\norder is also to cover other property).\n\n(2) The extension may be for:\n\n(a) a specified number of *working days; or\n\n(b) the period ending when the court decides the application for\nthe *restraining order.\n\n(3) The extension does not have effect unless a copy of the order for\nthe extension is given to the *financial institution before the time\nthe *freezing order would cease to be in force apart from the\nextension.\n\n(4) The following provisions apply in relation to an order extending a\n*freezing order in a way corresponding to the way in which they\napply in relation to a freezing order:\n\n(a) Division 2 (except paragraphs 15C(c) and (d));\n\n(b) section 15J (except the note to that section).\n\n(5) Division 2 applies because of subsection (4) as if:\n\n(a) section 15C also required that an affidavit supporting an\napplication:\n\n(i) identify the *freezing order; and\nComLaw Authoritative Act C2012C00115\n\nSchedule 2  Other amendments relating to proceeds of crime",
      "skos:definition": "(1) A magistrate may make an order extending the period specified in\na *freezing order made in relation to an *account with a *financial\ninstitution if:\n\n(a) an *authorised officer described in paragraph (a), (aa), (b) or\n(c) of the definition of authorised officer in section 338\napplies for the extension; and\n\n(b) the magistrate is satisfied that an application has been made\nto a court (but not decided by the court) for a *restraining\norder to cover the account (whether or not the restraining\norder is also to cover other property).\n\n(2) The extension may be for:\n\n(a) a specified number of *working days; or\n\n(b) the period ending when the court decides the application for\nthe *restraining order.\n\n(3) The extension does not have effect unless a copy of the order for\nthe extension is given to the *financial institution before the time\nthe *freezing order would cease to be in force apart from the\nextension.\n\n(4) The following provisions apply in relation to an order extending a\n*freezing order in a way corresponding to the way in which they\napply in relation to a freezing order:\n\n(a) Division 2 (except paragraphs 15C(c) and (d));\n\n(b) section 15J (except the note to that section).\n\n(5) Division 2 applies because of subsection (4) as if:\n\n(a) section 15C also required that an affidavit supporting an\napplication:\n\n(i) identify the *freezing order; and\nComLaw Authoritative Act C2012C00115\n\nSchedule 2  Other amendments relating to proceeds of crime",
      "cml:hasPart": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:crimes-legislation-amendment-serious-and-organised-crime-act-2010-sch-2-sec-15p-ss-1"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:crimes-legislation-amendment-serious-and-organised-crime-act-2010-sch-2-sec-15p-ss-2"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:crimes-legislation-amendment-serious-and-organised-crime-act-2010-sch-2-sec-15p-ss-3"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:crimes-legislation-amendment-serious-and-organised-crime-act-2010-sch-2-sec-15p-ss-4"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:crimes-legislation-amendment-serious-and-organised-crime-act-2010-sch-2-sec-15p-ss-5"
        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "3fce5c6aa4faa74f10e590448a9338101e57050a72b3b4f27a82293fd8afba94"
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/crimes-legislation-amendment-serious-and-organised-crime-act-2010#sch-2-sec-15p",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "15P Order extending a freezing order",
      "values:kind": "section",
      "cof:pageNumber": 39,
      "values:originalText": "(1) A magistrate may make an order extending the period specified in\na *freezing order made in relation to an *account with a *financial\ninstitution if:\n\n(a) an *authorised officer described in paragraph (a), (aa), (b) or\n(c) of the definition of authorised officer in section 338\napplies for the extension; and\n\n(b) the magistrate is satisfied that an application has been made\nto a court (but not decided by the court) for a *restraining\norder to cover the account (whether or not the restraining\norder is also to cover other property).\n\n(2) The extension may be for:\n\n(a) a specified number of *working days; or\n\n(b) the period ending when the court decides the application for\nthe *restraining order.\n\n(3) The extension does not have effect unless a copy of the order for\nthe extension is given to the *financial institution before the time\nthe *freezing order would cease to be in force apart from the\nextension.\n\n(4) The following provisions apply in relation to an order extending a\n*freezing order in a way corresponding to the way in which they\napply in relation to a freezing order:\n\n(a) Division 2 (except paragraphs 15C(c) and (d));\n\n(b) section 15J (except the note to that section).\n\n(5) Division 2 applies because of subsection (4) as if:\n\n(a) section 15C also required that an affidavit supporting an\napplication:\n\n(i) identify the *freezing order; and\nComLaw Authoritative Act C2012C00115\n\nSchedule 2  Other amendments relating to proceeds of crime"
    },
