    },
    {
      "@id": "concept:crimes-legislation-amendment-serious-and-organised-crime-act-2010-sch-2-sec-36",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "36 Crimes Legislation Amendment (Serious and Organised Crime) Act",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/crimes-legislation-amendment-serious-and-organised-crime-act-2010#sch-2-sec-36"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "crimes-legislation-amendment-serious-and-organised-crime-act-2010.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "crimes-legislation-amendment-serious-and-organised-crime-act-2010.pdf, p.40",
      "values:originalText": "(ii) state that an application has been made for a *restraining\norder to cover the *account; and\n\n(b) the reference in subsection 15E(1) to section 15B were a\nreference to subsection (1) of this section.",
      "skos:definition": "(ii) state that an application has been made for a *restraining\norder to cover the *account; and\n\n(b) the reference in subsection 15E(1) to section 15B were a\nreference to subsection (1) of this section.",
      "cml:asserts": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:crimes-legislation-amendment-serious-and-organised-crime-act-2010-sch-2-sec-36-norm"
        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "ffe1886a0f0d8a9d40b54fbded6bdb0db725f0cb46bf617f429021865be24216",
      "skos:note": "Mention of subsection 15B(1) in section 15E(1)"
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/crimes-legislation-amendment-serious-and-organised-crime-act-2010#sch-2-sec-36",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "36 Crimes Legislation Amendment (Serious and Organised Crime) Act",
      "values:kind": "section",
      "cof:pageNumber": 40,
      "values:originalText": "(ii) state that an application has been made for a *restraining\norder to cover the *account; and\n\n(b) the reference in subsection 15E(1) to section 15B were a\nreference to subsection (1) of this section."
    },
    {
      "@id": "concept:crimes-legislation-amendment-serious-and-organised-crime-act-2010-sch-2-sec-36-norm",
      "@type": "values:Obligation",
      "cml:modality": {
        "@id": "cml:Deontic"
      },
      "values:partOf": {
        "@id": "concept:crimes-legislation-amendment-serious-and-organised-crime-act-2010-sch-2-sec-36"
      },
      "values:deonticStatus": {
        "@id": "values:HeuristicDerived"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "values:borneBy": {
        "@id": "values:State"
      },
      "skos:scopeNote": "borne by: State"
    },
    {
      "@id": "concept:crimes-legislation-amendment-serious-and-organised-crime-act-2010-sch-2-sec-15q",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "15Q Magistrate may vary freezing order to allow withdrawal to",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/crimes-legislation-amendment-serious-and-organised-crime-act-2010#sch-2-sec-15q"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "crimes-legislation-amendment-serious-and-organised-crime-act-2010.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "crimes-legislation-amendment-serious-and-organised-crime-act-2010.pdf, p.40",
      "values:originalText": "meet reasonable expenses\n\n(1) A magistrate may vary a *freezing order relating to an *account\nwith a *financial institution so that the institution may allow a\nwithdrawal from the account to meet one or more of the following\nrelating to a person in whose name the account is held:\n\n(a) the reasonable living expenses of the person;\n\n(b) the reasonable living expenses of any of the *dependants of\nthe person;\n\n(c) the reasonable business expenses of the person;\n\n(d) a specified debt incurred in good faith by the person.\n\n(2) The magistrate may vary the *freezing order only if:\n\n(a) a person in whose name the *account is held has applied for\nthe variation; and\n\n(b) the person has notified the *DPP in writing of the application\nand the grounds for the application; and\n\n(c) the magistrate is satisfied that the expense or debt does not,\nor will not, relate to legal costs that the person has incurred,\nor will incur, in connection with:\n\n(i) proceedings under this Act; or\n\n(ii) proceedings for an offence against a law of the\nCommonwealth, a State or a Territory; and\n\n(d) the magistrate is satisfied that the person cannot meet the\nexpense or debt out of property that is not covered by:\n\n(i) a freezing order; or\n\n(ii) a *restraining order; or\n\n(iii) an *interstate restraining order; or\n\n(iv) a *foreign restraining order that is registered under the\n*Mutual Assistance Act.\nComLaw Authoritative Act C2012C00115\n\nOther amendments relating to proceeds of crime  Schedule 2\nFreezing orders  Part 1\n\nCrimes Legislation Amendment (Serious and Organised Crime) Act 2010\n\n(3) The variation does not take effect until written notice of it is given\nto the *financial institution.",
      "skos:definition": "meet reasonable expenses\n\n(1) A magistrate may vary a *freezing order relating to an *account\nwith a *financial institution so that the institution may allow a\nwithdrawal from the account to meet one or more of the following\nrelating to a person in whose name the account is held:\n\n(a) the reasonable living expenses of the person;\n\n(b) the reasonable living expenses of any of the *dependants of\nthe person;\n\n(c) the reasonable business expenses of the person;\n\n(d) a specified debt incurred in good faith by the person.\n\n(2) The magistrate may vary the *freezing order only if:\n\n(a) a person in whose name the *account is held has applied for\nthe variation; and\n\n(b) the person has notified the *DPP in writing of the application\nand the grounds for the application; and\n\n(c) the magistrate is satisfied that the expense or debt does not,\nor will not, relate to legal costs that the person has incurred,\nor will incur, in connection with:\n\n(i) proceedings under this Act; or\n\n(ii) proceedings for an offence against a law of the\nCommonwealth, a State or a Territory; and\n\n(d) the magistrate is satisfied that the person cannot meet the\nexpense or debt out of property that is not covered by:\n\n(i) a freezing order; or\n\n(ii) a *restraining order; or\n\n(iii) an *interstate restraining order; or\n\n(iv) a *foreign restraining order that is registered under the\n*Mutual Assistance Act.\nComLaw Authoritative Act C2012C00115\n\nOther amendments relating to proceeds of crime  Schedule 2\nFreezing orders  Part 1\n\nCrimes Legislation Amendment (Serious and Organised Crime) Act 2010\n\n(3) The variation does not take effect until written notice of it is given\nto the *financial institution.",
      "cml:hasPart": [
