    {
      "@id": "concept:crimes-legislation-amendment-serious-and-organised-crime-act-2010-sch-2-sec-15r",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "15R Application to revoke a freezing order",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/crimes-legislation-amendment-serious-and-organised-crime-act-2010#sch-2-sec-15r"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "crimes-legislation-amendment-serious-and-organised-crime-act-2010.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "crimes-legislation-amendment-serious-and-organised-crime-act-2010.pdf, p.41",
      "values:originalText": "(1) A person may apply to a magistrate to revoke a *freezing order.\n\n(2) The applicant for the revocation must give written notice of the\napplication and the grounds on which the revocation is sought to\nthe *enforcement agency mentioned in the paragraph of the\ndefinition of authorised officer in section 338 that describes the\n*authorised officer who applied for the *freezing order.\n\n(3) One or more of the following may adduce additional material to\nthe magistrate relating to the application to revoke the *freezing\norder:\n\n(a) the *authorised officer who applied for the freezing order;\n\n(b) the authorised officer whose affidavit supported the\napplication for the freezing order;\n\n(c) another authorised officer described in the paragraph of the\ndefinition of authorised officer in section 338 that describes\nthe authorised officer mentioned in paragraph (a) or (b) of\nthis subsection.\n\n(4) The magistrate may revoke the *freezing order if satisfied that it is\nin the interests of justice to do so.",
      "skos:definition": "(1) A person may apply to a magistrate to revoke a *freezing order.\n\n(2) The applicant for the revocation must give written notice of the\napplication and the grounds on which the revocation is sought to\nthe *enforcement agency mentioned in the paragraph of the\ndefinition of authorised officer in section 338 that describes the\n*authorised officer who applied for the *freezing order.\n\n(3) One or more of the following may adduce additional material to\nthe magistrate relating to the application to revoke the *freezing\norder:\n\n(a) the *authorised officer who applied for the freezing order;\n\n(b) the authorised officer whose affidavit supported the\napplication for the freezing order;\n\n(c) another authorised officer described in the paragraph of the\ndefinition of authorised officer in section 338 that describes\nthe authorised officer mentioned in paragraph (a) or (b) of\nthis subsection.\n\n(4) The magistrate may revoke the *freezing order if satisfied that it is\nin the interests of justice to do so.",
      "cml:hasPart": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:crimes-legislation-amendment-serious-and-organised-crime-act-2010-sch-2-sec-15r-ss-1"
        },
        {
