    {
      "@id": "concept:crimes-legislation-amendment-serious-and-organised-crime-act-2010-sch-2-sec-15s",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "15S Notice of revocation of a freezing order",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/crimes-legislation-amendment-serious-and-organised-crime-act-2010#sch-2-sec-15s"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "crimes-legislation-amendment-serious-and-organised-crime-act-2010.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "crimes-legislation-amendment-serious-and-organised-crime-act-2010.pdf, p.41",
      "values:originalText": "(1) If a *freezing order relating to an *account with a *financial\ninstitution is revoked under section 15R, an *authorised officer (the\nnotifying officer) described in the paragraph of the definition of\nauthorised officer in section 338 that describes the authorised\nofficer who applied for the freezing order must cause written notice\nof the revocation to be given to:\n\n(a) the financial institution; and\n\n(b) each person in whose name the account is held.\n\n(2) However, the notifying officer need not give notice to the applicant\nfor the revocation.\nComLaw Authoritative Act C2012C00115\n\nSchedule 2  Other amendments relating to proceeds of crime",
      "skos:definition": "(1) If a *freezing order relating to an *account with a *financial\ninstitution is revoked under section 15R, an *authorised officer (the\nnotifying officer) described in the paragraph of the definition of\nauthorised officer in section 338 that describes the authorised\nofficer who applied for the freezing order must cause written notice\nof the revocation to be given to:\n\n(a) the financial institution; and\n\n(b) each person in whose name the account is held.\n\n(2) However, the notifying officer need not give notice to the applicant\nfor the revocation.\nComLaw Authoritative Act C2012C00115\n\nSchedule 2  Other amendments relating to proceeds of crime",
      "cml:hasPart": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:crimes-legislation-amendment-serious-and-organised-crime-act-2010-sch-2-sec-15s-ss-1"
        },
