    {
      "@id": "concept:crimes-legislation-amendment-serious-and-organised-crime-act-2010-sch-2-sec-69",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "69 Subsections 293(1), (2) and (3)",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/crimes-legislation-amendment-serious-and-organised-crime-act-2010#sch-2-sec-69"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "crimes-legislation-amendment-serious-and-organised-crime-act-2010.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "crimes-legislation-amendment-serious-and-organised-crime-act-2010.pdf, p.55",
      "values:originalText": "Repeal the subsections, substitute:\n\n(1) This section applies if:\n\n(a) a *legal aid commission incurred (before, on or after the\ncommencement of this subsection) legal costs for:\n\n(i) representing a person whose property was, at the time of\nthe representation, covered by a *restraining order in\nproceedings under this Act; or\n\n(ii) representing a person, who was a *suspect at the time of\nthe representation and whose property was at that time\ncovered by a restraining order, in proceedings for\ndefending any criminal charge against the person; and\n\n(b) the commission has given (before, on or after the\ncommencement of this subsection) the *Official Trustee a bill\nfor the costs; and\n\n(c) the Official Trustee is satisfied that the bill is true and\ncorrect.\n\n(2) The *Official Trustee must pay the legal costs (according to the\nbill) to the *legal aid commission out of the *Confiscated Assets\nAccount, subject to subsection (2A).\n\n(2A) If the *Official Trustee is satisfied that:\n\n(a) the balance of the *Confiscated Assets Account is insufficient\nto pay the legal costs; and\n\n(b) property of the person is covered by the *restraining order;\nthe Official Trustee must pay the legal costs (according to the bill)\nto the *legal aid commission out of that property covered by the\norder, to the extent possible.\nComLaw Authoritative Act C2012C00115\n\nSchedule 2  Other amendments relating to proceeds of crime",
      "skos:definition": "Repeal the subsections, substitute:\n\n(1) This section applies if:\n\n(a) a *legal aid commission incurred (before, on or after the\ncommencement of this subsection) legal costs for:\n\n(i) representing a person whose property was, at the time of\nthe representation, covered by a *restraining order in\nproceedings under this Act; or\n\n(ii) representing a person, who was a *suspect at the time of\nthe representation and whose property was at that time\ncovered by a restraining order, in proceedings for\ndefending any criminal charge against the person; and\n\n(b) the commission has given (before, on or after the\ncommencement of this subsection) the *Official Trustee a bill\nfor the costs; and\n\n(c) the Official Trustee is satisfied that the bill is true and\ncorrect.\n\n(2) The *Official Trustee must pay the legal costs (according to the\nbill) to the *legal aid commission out of the *Confiscated Assets\nAccount, subject to subsection (2A).\n\n(2A) If the *Official Trustee is satisfied that:\n\n(a) the balance of the *Confiscated Assets Account is insufficient\nto pay the legal costs; and\n\n(b) property of the person is covered by the *restraining order;\nthe Official Trustee must pay the legal costs (according to the bill)\nto the *legal aid commission out of that property covered by the\norder, to the extent possible.\nComLaw Authoritative Act C2012C00115\n\nSchedule 2  Other amendments relating to proceeds of crime",
      "cml:hasPart": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:crimes-legislation-amendment-serious-and-organised-crime-act-2010-sch-2-sec-69-ss-1"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:crimes-legislation-amendment-serious-and-organised-crime-act-2010-sch-2-sec-69-ss-2"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:crimes-legislation-amendment-serious-and-organised-crime-act-2010-sch-2-sec-69-ss-2a"
        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "45006b563b2fa2182b7ea81cca2aac16faa404d7946d1c0f51f91fbff6cf069d"
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/crimes-legislation-amendment-serious-and-organised-crime-act-2010#sch-2-sec-69",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "69 Subsections 293(1), (2) and (3)",
      "values:kind": "section",
      "cof:pageNumber": 55,
      "values:originalText": "Repeal the subsections, substitute:\n\n(1) This section applies if:\n\n(a) a *legal aid commission incurred (before, on or after the\ncommencement of this subsection) legal costs for:\n\n(i) representing a person whose property was, at the time of\nthe representation, covered by a *restraining order in\nproceedings under this Act; or\n\n(ii) representing a person, who was a *suspect at the time of\nthe representation and whose property was at that time\ncovered by a restraining order, in proceedings for\ndefending any criminal charge against the person; and\n\n(b) the commission has given (before, on or after the\ncommencement of this subsection) the *Official Trustee a bill\nfor the costs; and\n\n(c) the Official Trustee is satisfied that the bill is true and\ncorrect.\n\n(2) The *Official Trustee must pay the legal costs (according to the\nbill) to the *legal aid commission out of the *Confiscated Assets\nAccount, subject to subsection (2A).\n\n(2A) If the *Official Trustee is satisfied that:\n\n(a) the balance of the *Confiscated Assets Account is insufficient\nto pay the legal costs; and\n\n(b) property of the person is covered by the *restraining order;\nthe Official Trustee must pay the legal costs (according to the bill)\nto the *legal aid commission out of that property covered by the\norder, to the extent possible.\nComLaw Authoritative Act C2012C00115\n\nSchedule 2  Other amendments relating to proceeds of crime"
    },
