    {
      "@id": "concept:crimes-legislation-amendment-serious-and-organised-crime-act-2010-sch-2-sec-52-2",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "52 Crimes Legislation Amendment (Serious and Organised Crime) Act",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/crimes-legislation-amendment-serious-and-organised-crime-act-2010#sch-2-sec-52-2"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "crimes-legislation-amendment-serious-and-organised-crime-act-2010.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "crimes-legislation-amendment-serious-and-organised-crime-act-2010.pdf, p.56",
      "values:originalText": "(3) If the *Official Trustee pays an amount to the *legal aid\ncommission under this section and property of the person is\ncovered by a *restraining order, the person must pay the\nCommonwealth an amount equal to the lesser of the following (or\neither of them if they are the same):\n\n(a) the amount paid to the legal aid commission;\n\n(b) the value of the person’s property covered by the restraining\norder.\nNote:\nThe heading to section 293 is replaced by the heading “Payments to legal aid\ncommissions for representing suspects and other persons”.",
      "skos:definition": "(3) If the *Official Trustee pays an amount to the *legal aid\ncommission under this section and property of the person is\ncovered by a *restraining order, the person must pay the\nCommonwealth an amount equal to the lesser of the following (or\neither of them if they are the same):\n\n(a) the amount paid to the legal aid commission;\n\n(b) the value of the person’s property covered by the restraining\norder.\nNote:\nThe heading to section 293 is replaced by the heading “Payments to legal aid\ncommissions for representing suspects and other persons”.",
      "cml:asserts": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:crimes-legislation-amendment-serious-and-organised-crime-act-2010-sch-2-sec-52-2-norm"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:crimes-legislation-amendment-serious-and-organised-crime-act-2010-sch-2-sec-52-2-logic-deontic-1"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:crimes-legislation-amendment-serious-and-organised-crime-act-2010-sch-2-sec-52-2-logic-alleninterval-2"
        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "b365cafad2e5f3ce32846b9afa4e731974b1cbb966e9a2b1d3fe66645b394663",
      "skos:note": "Pay Commonwealth an amount equal to the lesser of the amount paid to legal aid commission or value of property covered by restraining order."
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/crimes-legislation-amendment-serious-and-organised-crime-act-2010#sch-2-sec-52-2",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "52 Crimes Legislation Amendment (Serious and Organised Crime) Act",
      "values:kind": "section",
      "cof:pageNumber": 56,
      "values:originalText": "(3) If the *Official Trustee pays an amount to the *legal aid\ncommission under this section and property of the person is\ncovered by a *restraining order, the person must pay the\nCommonwealth an amount equal to the lesser of the following (or\neither of them if they are the same):\n\n(a) the amount paid to the legal aid commission;\n\n(b) the value of the person’s property covered by the restraining\norder.\nNote:\nThe heading to section 293 is replaced by the heading “Payments to legal aid\ncommissions for representing suspects and other persons”."
    },
