    },
    {
      "@id": "concept:crimes-legislation-amendment-serious-and-organised-crime-act-2010-sch-2-sec-107",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "107 Application and transitional",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/crimes-legislation-amendment-serious-and-organised-crime-act-2010#sch-2-sec-107"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "crimes-legislation-amendment-serious-and-organised-crime-act-2010.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "crimes-legislation-amendment-serious-and-organised-crime-act-2010.pdf, p.60",
      "values:originalText": "(1)\nThe amendment of section 42 of the Proceeds of Crime Act 2002 made\nby this Part applies in relation to the revocation of a restraining order on\nor after commencement, whether the application for that revocation was\nmade before, on or after commencement.\n(2)\nIf an application under section 42 of the Proceeds of Crime Act 2002 for\nthe revocation of a restraining order has been made but not determined\nas at commencement:\n\n(a) the applicant may vary the application to take account of\nparagraph 42(5)(b) of the Proceeds of Crime Act 2002 as in\nforce at commencement; and\n\n(b) if the application is varied under paragraph (a) of this\nsubitem—the applicant must give a copy of the application as\nvaried, and written notice of any additional grounds that he\nor she proposes to rely on in seeking that revocation, to the\nresponsible authority and the Official Trustee; and\n\n(c) the responsible authority may adduce additional material to\nthe court relating to those additional grounds.\n(3)\nIn this item:\ncommencement means the commencement of this item.\nComLaw Authoritative Act C2012C00115\n\nAmendments relating to controlled operations, assumed identities and witness identity\nprotection  Schedule 3\nMain amendments  Part 1\n\nCrimes Legislation Amendment (Serious and Organised Crime) Act 2010",
      "skos:definition": "(1)\nThe amendment of section 42 of the Proceeds of Crime Act 2002 made\nby this Part applies in relation to the revocation of a restraining order on\nor after commencement, whether the application for that revocation was\nmade before, on or after commencement.\n(2)\nIf an application under section 42 of the Proceeds of Crime Act 2002 for\nthe revocation of a restraining order has been made but not determined\nas at commencement:\n\n(a) the applicant may vary the application to take account of\nparagraph 42(5)(b) of the Proceeds of Crime Act 2002 as in\nforce at commencement; and\n\n(b) if the application is varied under paragraph (a) of this\nsubitem—the applicant must give a copy of the application as\nvaried, and written notice of any additional grounds that he\nor she proposes to rely on in seeking that revocation, to the\nresponsible authority and the Official Trustee; and\n\n(c) the responsible authority may adduce additional material to\nthe court relating to those additional grounds.\n(3)\nIn this item:\ncommencement means the commencement of this item.\nComLaw Authoritative Act C2012C00115\n\nAmendments relating to controlled operations, assumed identities and witness identity\nprotection  Schedule 3\nMain amendments  Part 1\n\nCrimes Legislation Amendment (Serious and Organised Crime) Act 2010",
      "cml:asserts": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:crimes-legislation-amendment-serious-and-organised-crime-act-2010-sch-2-sec-107-norm"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:crimes-legislation-amendment-serious-and-organised-crime-act-2010-sch-2-sec-107-logic-descriptionlogic-1"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:crimes-legislation-amendment-serious-and-organised-crime-act-2010-sch-2-sec-107-logic-alleninterval-2"
        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "f273570a6e60cd08636c6dbff6088d03ef28fbf698520afc8e6c449a5def440d",
      "skos:note": "Application and transitional provisions for revocation of restraining orders"
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/crimes-legislation-amendment-serious-and-organised-crime-act-2010#sch-2-sec-107",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "107 Application and transitional",
      "values:kind": "section",
      "cof:pageNumber": 60,
      "values:originalText": "(1)\nThe amendment of section 42 of the Proceeds of Crime Act 2002 made\nby this Part applies in relation to the revocation of a restraining order on\nor after commencement, whether the application for that revocation was\nmade before, on or after commencement.\n(2)\nIf an application under section 42 of the Proceeds of Crime Act 2002 for\nthe revocation of a restraining order has been made but not determined\nas at commencement:\n\n(a) the applicant may vary the application to take account of\nparagraph 42(5)(b) of the Proceeds of Crime Act 2002 as in\nforce at commencement; and\n\n(b) if the application is varied under paragraph (a) of this\nsubitem—the applicant must give a copy of the application as\nvaried, and written notice of any additional grounds that he\nor she proposes to rely on in seeking that revocation, to the\nresponsible authority and the Official Trustee; and\n\n(c) the responsible authority may adduce additional material to\nthe court relating to those additional grounds.\n(3)\nIn this item:\ncommencement means the commencement of this item.\nComLaw Authoritative Act C2012C00115\n\nAmendments relating to controlled operations, assumed identities and witness identity\nprotection  Schedule 3\nMain amendments  Part 1\n\nCrimes Legislation Amendment (Serious and Organised Crime) Act 2010"
    },
