    {
      "@id": "concept:crimes-legislation-amendment-serious-and-organised-crime-act-2010-sch-3-sec-15g",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "15G Objects of Part",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/crimes-legislation-amendment-serious-and-organised-crime-act-2010#sch-3-sec-15g"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "crimes-legislation-amendment-serious-and-organised-crime-act-2010.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "crimes-legislation-amendment-serious-and-organised-crime-act-2010.pdf, p.62",
      "values:originalText": "The main objects of this Part are:\n\n(a) to provide for the authorisation, conduct and monitoring of\ncontrolled operations; and\n\n(b) to exempt from criminal liability, and to indemnify from civil\nliability:\n\n(i) law enforcement officers who, in the course of a\ncontrolled operation authorised under this Part, take an\nactive part in, or are otherwise involved in, the\ncommission of a Commonwealth offence or an offence\nagainst a law of a State or Territory or conduct that may\nresult in a civil liability; and\n\n(ii) certain other persons who, in accordance with the\ninstructions of a law enforcement officer and in the\ncourse of a controlled operation authorised under this\nPart, take an active part in, or are otherwise involved in,\nthe commission of a Commonwealth offence or an\noffence against a law of a State or Territory or conduct\nthat may result in a civil liability.",
      "skos:definition": "The main objects of this Part are:\n\n(a) to provide for the authorisation, conduct and monitoring of\ncontrolled operations; and\n\n(b) to exempt from criminal liability, and to indemnify from civil\nliability:\n\n(i) law enforcement officers who, in the course of a\ncontrolled operation authorised under this Part, take an\nactive part in, or are otherwise involved in, the\ncommission of a Commonwealth offence or an offence\nagainst a law of a State or Territory or conduct that may\nresult in a civil liability; and\n\n(ii) certain other persons who, in accordance with the\ninstructions of a law enforcement officer and in the\ncourse of a controlled operation authorised under this\nPart, take an active part in, or are otherwise involved in,\nthe commission of a Commonwealth offence or an\noffence against a law of a State or Territory or conduct\nthat may result in a civil liability.",
      "cml:asserts": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:crimes-legislation-amendment-serious-and-organised-crime-act-2010-sch-3-sec-15g-norm"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:crimes-legislation-amendment-serious-and-organised-crime-act-2010-sch-3-sec-15g-logic-deontic-1"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:crimes-legislation-amendment-serious-and-organised-crime-act-2010-sch-3-sec-15g-logic-deontic-2"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:crimes-legislation-amendment-serious-and-organised-crime-act-2010-sch-3-sec-15g-logic-deontic-3"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:crimes-legislation-amendment-serious-and-organised-crime-act-2010-sch-3-sec-15g-logic-deontic-4"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:crimes-legislation-amendment-serious-and-organised-crime-act-2010-sch-3-sec-15g-logic-deontic-5"
        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "77b795c769cab3309be0a4a01dfeeb1a4cef938128620ab6e75fa033ec74689e",
      "skos:note": "Exempts law enforcement officers and certain other persons from criminal liability and civil liability in the course of a controlled operation."
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/crimes-legislation-amendment-serious-and-organised-crime-act-2010#sch-3-sec-15g",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "15G Objects of Part",
      "values:kind": "section",
      "cof:pageNumber": 62,
      "values:originalText": "The main objects of this Part are:\n\n(a) to provide for the authorisation, conduct and monitoring of\ncontrolled operations; and\n\n(b) to exempt from criminal liability, and to indemnify from civil\nliability:\n\n(i) law enforcement officers who, in the course of a\ncontrolled operation authorised under this Part, take an\nactive part in, or are otherwise involved in, the\ncommission of a Commonwealth offence or an offence\nagainst a law of a State or Territory or conduct that may\nresult in a civil liability; and\n\n(ii) certain other persons who, in accordance with the\ninstructions of a law enforcement officer and in the\ncourse of a controlled operation authorised under this\nPart, take an active part in, or are otherwise involved in,\nthe commission of a Commonwealth offence or an\noffence against a law of a State or Territory or conduct\nthat may result in a civil liability."
    },
    {
      "@id": "concept:crimes-legislation-amendment-serious-and-organised-crime-act-2010-sch-3-sec-15g-norm",
      "@type": "values:Obligation",
      "cml:modality": {
        "@id": "cml:Deontic"
      },
      "values:partOf": {
        "@id": "concept:crimes-legislation-amendment-serious-and-organised-crime-act-2010-sch-3-sec-15g"
      },
      "values:deonticStatus": {
        "@id": "values:HeuristicDerived"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "values:borneBy": {
        "@id": "values:State"
      },
      "skos:scopeNote": "borne by: State"
    },
    {
      "@id": "concept:crimes-legislation-amendment-serious-and-organised-crime-act-2010-sch-3-sec-15g-logic-deontic-1",
      "@type": "cml:LogicApplication",
      "cml:modality": {
        "@id": "cml:Deontic"
      },
      "cml:operator": "Exemption",
      "cml:logicSummary": "Exempts individuals from liability",
      "cml:executionSurface": "modalities::logic::deontic",
      "cml:confidence": {
        "@value": 1.0,
        "@type": "xsd:decimal"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:premiseText": "Law enforcement officers and certain other persons are exempt from criminal liability and civil liability.",
      "cml:conclusionText": "No liability for the individual."
    },
    {
      "@id": "concept:crimes-legislation-amendment-serious-and-organised-crime-act-2010-sch-3-sec-15g-logic-deontic-2",
      "@type": "cml:LogicApplication",
      "cml:modality": {
        "@id": "cml:Deontic"
      },
      "cml:operator": "Permission",
      "cml:logicSummary": "Permits law enforcement officers and certain other persons to engage in activities without liability",
      "cml:executionSurface": "modalities::logic::deontic",
      "cml:confidence": {
        "@value": 1.0,
        "@type": "xsd:decimal"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:premiseText": "The exemption permits law enforcement officers who take an active part in a controlled operation to engage in the commission of a Commonwealth offence or an offence against a law of a State or Territory.",
      "cml:conclusionText": "Law enforcement officers are permitted to engage in the commission of a Commonwealth offence or an offence against a law of a State or Territory without liability."
    },
    {
      "@id": "concept:crimes-legislation-amendment-serious-and-organised-crime-act-2010-sch-3-sec-15g-logic-deontic-3",
      "@type": "cml:LogicApplication",
      "cml:modality": {
        "@id": "cml:Deontic"
      },
      "cml:operator": "Obligation",
      "cml:logicSummary": "Imposes an obligation on law enforcement officers and certain other persons to take part in controlled operations",
      "cml:executionSurface": "modalities::logic::deontic",
      "cml:confidence": {
        "@value": 1.0,
        "@type": "xsd:decimal"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:premiseText": "The exemption requires law enforcement officers who take an active part in a controlled operation to engage in the commission of a Commonwealth offence or an offence against a law of a State or Territory.",
      "cml:conclusionText": "Law enforcement officers have an obligation to take part in controlled operations."
    },
    {
      "@id": "concept:crimes-legislation-amendment-serious-and-organised-crime-act-2010-sch-3-sec-15g-logic-deontic-4",
      "@type": "cml:LogicApplication",
      "cml:modality": {
        "@id": "cml:Deontic"
      },
      "cml:operator": "Right",
      "cml:logicSummary": "Grants law enforcement officers and certain other persons the right to engage in activities without liability",
      "cml:executionSurface": "modalities::logic::deontic",
      "cml:confidence": {
        "@value": 1.0,
        "@type": "xsd:decimal"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:premiseText": "The exemption grants law enforcement officers who take an active part in a controlled operation the right to engage in the commission of a Commonwealth offence or an offence against a law of a State or Territory.",
      "cml:conclusionText": "Law enforcement officers have the right to engage in the commission of a Commonwealth offence or an offence against a law of a State or Territory without liability."
    },
    {
      "@id": "concept:crimes-legislation-amendment-serious-and-organised-crime-act-2010-sch-3-sec-15g-logic-deontic-5",
      "@type": "cml:LogicApplication",
      "cml:modality": {
        "@id": "cml:Deontic"
      },
      "cml:operator": "Undertaking",
      "cml:logicSummary": "Establishes the scope and conditions of exemption",
      "cml:executionSurface": "modalities::logic::deontic",
      "cml:confidence": {
        "@value": 1.0,
        "@type": "xsd:decimal"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:premiseText": "The exemption applies to law enforcement officers who take an active part in a controlled operation and certain other persons who follow instructions from a law enforcement officer.",
      "cml:conclusionText": "The exemption is established for law enforcement officers and certain other persons under specific conditions."
    },
    {
      "@id": "concept:crimes-legislation-amendment-serious-and-organised-crime-act-2010-sch-3-sec-15ga",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "15GA Relationship to other laws and matters",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/crimes-legislation-amendment-serious-and-organised-crime-act-2010#sch-3-sec-15ga"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "crimes-legislation-amendment-serious-and-organised-crime-act-2010.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "crimes-legislation-amendment-serious-and-organised-crime-act-2010.pdf, p.62",
      "values:originalText": "(1) Subject to subsection (2) and section 15HZ, this Part is not\nintended to limit a discretion that a court has:\n\n(a) to admit or exclude evidence in any proceedings; or\n\n(b) to stay criminal proceedings in the interests of justice.\n\n(2) In determining whether evidence should be admitted or excluded in\nany proceedings, the fact that the evidence was obtained as a result\nof a person engaging in criminal activity is to be disregarded if:\n\n(a) both:\nComLaw Authoritative Act C2012C00115\n\nAmendments relating to controlled operations, assumed identities and witness identity\nprotection  Schedule 3\nMain amendments  Part 1\n\nCrimes Legislation Amendment (Serious and Organised Crime) Act 2010\n\n(i) the person was a participant in a controlled operation\nauthorised under this Part acting in the course of the\ncontrolled operation; and\n\n(ii) the criminal activity was controlled conduct; or\n\n(b) both:\n\n(i) the person was a participant in an operation authorised\nunder a corresponding State controlled operations law\nacting in the course of that operation; and\n\n(ii) the criminal activity was conduct constituting an\noffence for which a person would, but for\nsection 15HH, be criminally responsible.",
      "skos:definition": "(1) Subject to subsection (2) and section 15HZ, this Part is not\nintended to limit a discretion that a court has:\n\n(a) to admit or exclude evidence in any proceedings; or\n\n(b) to stay criminal proceedings in the interests of justice.\n\n(2) In determining whether evidence should be admitted or excluded in\nany proceedings, the fact that the evidence was obtained as a result\nof a person engaging in criminal activity is to be disregarded if:\n\n(a) both:\nComLaw Authoritative Act C2012C00115\n\nAmendments relating to controlled operations, assumed identities and witness identity\nprotection  Schedule 3\nMain amendments  Part 1\n\nCrimes Legislation Amendment (Serious and Organised Crime) Act 2010\n\n(i) the person was a participant in a controlled operation\nauthorised under this Part acting in the course of the\ncontrolled operation; and\n\n(ii) the criminal activity was controlled conduct; or\n\n(b) both:\n\n(i) the person was a participant in an operation authorised\nunder a corresponding State controlled operations law\nacting in the course of that operation; and\n\n(ii) the criminal activity was conduct constituting an\noffence for which a person would, but for\nsection 15HH, be criminally responsible.",
      "cml:hasPart": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:crimes-legislation-amendment-serious-and-organised-crime-act-2010-sch-3-sec-15ga-ss-1"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:crimes-legislation-amendment-serious-and-organised-crime-act-2010-sch-3-sec-15ga-ss-2"
        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "8c672e7b5cd64435d535a7a3b44d8a05bd501a3aaf7181cd7d15d6c3990f2c5f"
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/crimes-legislation-amendment-serious-and-organised-crime-act-2010#sch-3-sec-15ga",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "15GA Relationship to other laws and matters",
      "values:kind": "section",
      "cof:pageNumber": 62,
      "values:originalText": "(1) Subject to subsection (2) and section 15HZ, this Part is not\nintended to limit a discretion that a court has:\n\n(a) to admit or exclude evidence in any proceedings; or\n\n(b) to stay criminal proceedings in the interests of justice.\n\n(2) In determining whether evidence should be admitted or excluded in\nany proceedings, the fact that the evidence was obtained as a result\nof a person engaging in criminal activity is to be disregarded if:\n\n(a) both:\nComLaw Authoritative Act C2012C00115\n\nAmendments relating to controlled operations, assumed identities and witness identity\nprotection  Schedule 3\nMain amendments  Part 1\n\nCrimes Legislation Amendment (Serious and Organised Crime) Act 2010\n\n(i) the person was a participant in a controlled operation\nauthorised under this Part acting in the course of the\ncontrolled operation; and\n\n(ii) the criminal activity was controlled conduct; or\n\n(b) both:\n\n(i) the person was a participant in an operation authorised\nunder a corresponding State controlled operations law\nacting in the course of that operation; and\n\n(ii) the criminal activity was conduct constituting an\noffence for which a person would, but for\nsection 15HH, be criminally responsible."
    },
