          "@id": "concept:crimes-legislation-amendment-serious-and-organised-crime-act-2010-sch-3-sec-15ga-ss-2-logic-deontic-1"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:crimes-legislation-amendment-serious-and-organised-crime-act-2010-sch-3-sec-15ga-ss-2-logic-alleninterval-2"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:crimes-legislation-amendment-serious-and-organised-crime-act-2010-sch-3-sec-15ga-ss-2-logic-deontic-3"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:crimes-legislation-amendment-serious-and-organised-crime-act-2010-sch-3-sec-15ga-ss-2-logic-deontic-4"
        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "1f1c2cb23224f1dc734c47db4d75e4e47495b9f8214e50f96da0d4361e4a2668",
      "skos:note": "Disregard evidence obtained from criminal activity under certain conditions."
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/crimes-legislation-amendment-serious-and-organised-crime-act-2010#sch-3-sec-15ga-ss-2",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "15GA(2) Relationship to other laws and matters",
      "values:kind": "subsection",
      "cof:pageNumber": 62,
      "values:originalText": "(2) In determining whether evidence should be admitted or excluded in\nany proceedings, the fact that the evidence was obtained as a result\nof a person engaging in criminal activity is to be disregarded if:\n\n(a) both:\nComLaw Authoritative Act C2012C00115\n\nAmendments relating to controlled operations, assumed identities and witness identity\nprotection  Schedule 3\nMain amendments  Part 1\n\nCrimes Legislation Amendment (Serious and Organised Crime) Act 2010\n\n(i) the person was a participant in a controlled operation\nauthorised under this Part acting in the course of the\ncontrolled operation; and\n\n(ii) the criminal activity was controlled conduct; or\n\n(b) both:\n\n(i) the person was a participant in an operation authorised\nunder a corresponding State controlled operations law\nacting in the course of that operation; and\n\n(ii) the criminal activity was conduct constituting an\noffence for which a person would, but for\nsection 15HH, be criminally responsible."
    },
