    {
      "@id": "concept:crimes-legislation-amendment-serious-and-organised-crime-act-2010-sch-3-sec-15gd",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "15GD Meaning of controlled operation and major controlled",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/crimes-legislation-amendment-serious-and-organised-crime-act-2010#sch-3-sec-15gd"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "crimes-legislation-amendment-serious-and-organised-crime-act-2010.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "crimes-legislation-amendment-serious-and-organised-crime-act-2010.pdf, p.66",
      "values:originalText": "operation\n\n(1) A controlled operation is an operation that:\nComLaw Authoritative Act C2012C00115\n\nAmendments relating to controlled operations, assumed identities and witness identity\nprotection  Schedule 3\nMain amendments  Part 1\n\nCrimes Legislation Amendment (Serious and Organised Crime) Act 2010\n\n(a) involves the participation of law enforcement officers; and\n\n(b) is carried out for the purpose of obtaining evidence that may\nlead to the prosecution of a person for a serious\nCommonwealth offence or a serious State offence that has a\nfederal aspect; and\n\n(c) may involve a law enforcement officer or other person in\nconduct that would, apart from section 15HA, constitute a\nCommonwealth offence or an offence against a law of a State\nor Territory.\nNote:\nSection 15GN specifies when a controlled operation begins and ends.\n\n(2) A major controlled operation is a controlled operation that is\nlikely to:\n\n(a) involve the infiltration of an organised criminal group by one\nor more undercover law enforcement officers for a period of\nmore than 7 days; or\n\n(b) continue for more than 3 months; or\n\n(c) be directed against suspected criminal activity that includes a\nthreat to human life.\nNote:\nSection 15GN specifies when a controlled operation begins and ends.",
      "skos:definition": "operation\n\n(1) A controlled operation is an operation that:\nComLaw Authoritative Act C2012C00115\n\nAmendments relating to controlled operations, assumed identities and witness identity\nprotection  Schedule 3\nMain amendments  Part 1\n\nCrimes Legislation Amendment (Serious and Organised Crime) Act 2010\n\n(a) involves the participation of law enforcement officers; and\n\n(b) is carried out for the purpose of obtaining evidence that may\nlead to the prosecution of a person for a serious\nCommonwealth offence or a serious State offence that has a\nfederal aspect; and\n\n(c) may involve a law enforcement officer or other person in\nconduct that would, apart from section 15HA, constitute a\nCommonwealth offence or an offence against a law of a State\nor Territory.\nNote:\nSection 15GN specifies when a controlled operation begins and ends.\n\n(2) A major controlled operation is a controlled operation that is\nlikely to:\n\n(a) involve the infiltration of an organised criminal group by one\nor more undercover law enforcement officers for a period of\nmore than 7 days; or\n\n(b) continue for more than 3 months; or\n\n(c) be directed against suspected criminal activity that includes a\nthreat to human life.\nNote:\nSection 15GN specifies when a controlled operation begins and ends.",
      "cml:hasPart": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:crimes-legislation-amendment-serious-and-organised-crime-act-2010-sch-3-sec-15gd-ss-1"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:crimes-legislation-amendment-serious-and-organised-crime-act-2010-sch-3-sec-15gd-ss-2"
        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "9bf5a24e4aa779981ac41f1a0f8713ec758e12df95fa51866869849c06e51175"
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/crimes-legislation-amendment-serious-and-organised-crime-act-2010#sch-3-sec-15gd",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "15GD Meaning of controlled operation and major controlled",
      "values:kind": "section",
      "cof:pageNumber": 66,
      "values:originalText": "operation\n\n(1) A controlled operation is an operation that:\nComLaw Authoritative Act C2012C00115\n\nAmendments relating to controlled operations, assumed identities and witness identity\nprotection  Schedule 3\nMain amendments  Part 1\n\nCrimes Legislation Amendment (Serious and Organised Crime) Act 2010\n\n(a) involves the participation of law enforcement officers; and\n\n(b) is carried out for the purpose of obtaining evidence that may\nlead to the prosecution of a person for a serious\nCommonwealth offence or a serious State offence that has a\nfederal aspect; and\n\n(c) may involve a law enforcement officer or other person in\nconduct that would, apart from section 15HA, constitute a\nCommonwealth offence or an offence against a law of a State\nor Territory.\nNote:\nSection 15GN specifies when a controlled operation begins and ends.\n\n(2) A major controlled operation is a controlled operation that is\nlikely to:\n\n(a) involve the infiltration of an organised criminal group by one\nor more undercover law enforcement officers for a period of\nmore than 7 days; or\n\n(b) continue for more than 3 months; or\n\n(c) be directed against suspected criminal activity that includes a\nthreat to human life.\nNote:\nSection 15GN specifies when a controlled operation begins and ends."
    },
