      "dc:source": "crimes-legislation-amendment-serious-and-organised-crime-act-2010.pdf, p.71",
      "values:originalText": "(3) Nothing in this Part prevents an application for an authority being\nmade in respect of a controlled operation that has been the subject\nof a previous application, but in that case the subsequent\napplication must be a formal application.\nNote:\nAn urgent authority can be varied, but not so as to extend its\nduration—see sections 15GO and 15GS.",
      "skos:definition": "(3) Nothing in this Part prevents an application for an authority being\nmade in respect of a controlled operation that has been the subject\nof a previous application, but in that case the subsequent\napplication must be a formal application.\nNote:\nAn urgent authority can be varied, but not so as to extend its\nduration—see sections 15GO and 15GS.",
      "values:partOf": {
