    {
      "@id": "concept:crimes-legislation-amendment-serious-and-organised-crime-act-2010-sch-3-sec-68",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "68 Crimes Legislation Amendment (Serious and Organised Crime) Act",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/crimes-legislation-amendment-serious-and-organised-crime-act-2010#sch-3-sec-68"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "crimes-legislation-amendment-serious-and-organised-crime-act-2010.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "crimes-legislation-amendment-serious-and-organised-crime-act-2010.pdf, p.72",
      "values:originalText": "(5) An authorising officer may require an applicant to provide such\nadditional information concerning the proposed controlled\noperation as is necessary for the proper consideration of the\napplication.\n\n(6) As soon as practicable after making an urgent application that was\nnot made in writing, the applicant must make a written record of\nthe application and give a copy of it to the authorising officer to\nwhom the application was made.",
      "skos:definition": "(5) An authorising officer may require an applicant to provide such\nadditional information concerning the proposed controlled\noperation as is necessary for the proper consideration of the\napplication.\n\n(6) As soon as practicable after making an urgent application that was\nnot made in writing, the applicant must make a written record of\nthe application and give a copy of it to the authorising officer to\nwhom the application was made.",
      "cml:hasPart": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:crimes-legislation-amendment-serious-and-organised-crime-act-2010-sch-3-sec-68-ss-5"
        },
        {
