      },
      "cml:premiseText": "An authority granted under this section is a type of artificial intelligence system.",
      "cml:conclusionText": "An authority granted under this section is not an artificial intelligence system."
    },
    {
      "@id": "concept:crimes-legislation-amendment-serious-and-organised-crime-act-2010-sch-3-sec-15gj",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "15GJ Manner of granting authority",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/crimes-legislation-amendment-serious-and-organised-crime-act-2010#sch-3-sec-15gj"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "crimes-legislation-amendment-serious-and-organised-crime-act-2010.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "crimes-legislation-amendment-serious-and-organised-crime-act-2010.pdf, p.73",
      "values:originalText": "(1) An authority to conduct a controlled operation may be granted:\n\n(a) in the case of a formal application (other than a formal\napplication referred to in subparagraph (b)(ii))—by means of\na written document, signed by the authorising officer (such\nan authority is a formal authority); or\n\n(b) in the case of:\n\n(i) an urgent application; or\n\n(ii) a formal application, if the authorising officer is\nsatisfied that the delay caused by granting a formal\nauthority may affect the success of the controlled\noperation;\n\norally in person, or by telephone or any other means of\ncommunication (such an authority is an urgent authority).\nComLaw Authoritative Act C2012C00115\n\nSchedule 3  Amendments relating to controlled operations, assumed identities and\nwitness identity protection",
      "skos:definition": "(1) An authority to conduct a controlled operation may be granted:\n\n(a) in the case of a formal application (other than a formal\napplication referred to in subparagraph (b)(ii))—by means of\na written document, signed by the authorising officer (such\nan authority is a formal authority); or\n\n(b) in the case of:\n\n(i) an urgent application; or\n\n(ii) a formal application, if the authorising officer is\nsatisfied that the delay caused by granting a formal\nauthority may affect the success of the controlled\noperation;\n\norally in person, or by telephone or any other means of\ncommunication (such an authority is an urgent authority).\nComLaw Authoritative Act C2012C00115\n\nSchedule 3  Amendments relating to controlled operations, assumed identities and\nwitness identity protection",
      "cml:asserts": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:crimes-legislation-amendment-serious-and-organised-crime-act-2010-sch-3-sec-15gj-norm"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:crimes-legislation-amendment-serious-and-organised-crime-act-2010-sch-3-sec-15gj-logic-deontic-1"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:crimes-legislation-amendment-serious-and-organised-crime-act-2010-sch-3-sec-15gj-logic-descriptionlogic-2"
        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "c5f3546eb1b48d4e94e7399b806c630bf8f081cfc39c05812b60ba79765536c7",
      "skos:note": "Authority to conduct a controlled operation may be granted by means of a written document or orally in person, telephone, or other communication."
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/crimes-legislation-amendment-serious-and-organised-crime-act-2010#sch-3-sec-15gj",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "15GJ Manner of granting authority",
      "values:kind": "section",
      "cof:pageNumber": 73,
      "values:originalText": "(1) An authority to conduct a controlled operation may be granted:\n\n(a) in the case of a formal application (other than a formal\napplication referred to in subparagraph (b)(ii))—by means of\na written document, signed by the authorising officer (such\nan authority is a formal authority); or\n\n(b) in the case of:\n\n(i) an urgent application; or\n\n(ii) a formal application, if the authorising officer is\nsatisfied that the delay caused by granting a formal\nauthority may affect the success of the controlled\noperation;\n\norally in person, or by telephone or any other means of\ncommunication (such an authority is an urgent authority).\nComLaw Authoritative Act C2012C00115\n\nSchedule 3  Amendments relating to controlled operations, assumed identities and\nwitness identity protection"
    },
