    {
      "@id": "concept:crimes-legislation-amendment-serious-and-organised-crime-act-2010-sch-3-sec-15go",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "15GO Variation of authority by appropriate authorising officer",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/crimes-legislation-amendment-serious-and-organised-crime-act-2010#sch-3-sec-15go"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "crimes-legislation-amendment-serious-and-organised-crime-act-2010.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "crimes-legislation-amendment-serious-and-organised-crime-act-2010.pdf, p.77",
      "values:originalText": "(1) An appropriate authorising officer may vary an authority:\n\n(a) at any time on the authorising officer’s own initiative; or\n\n(b) on application under subsection 15GP(1).\n\n(2) A variation may:\n\n(a) extend the period of effect of the authority (subject to\nsubsections (3) and (4)); or\n\n(b) authorise additional persons to engage in controlled conduct\nfor the purposes of the controlled operation and specify:\n\n(i) with respect to additional law enforcement\nparticipants—the nature of the controlled conduct that\nthose participants may engage in; and\n\n(ii) with respect to additional civilian participants—the\nparticular controlled conduct (if any) that each such\nparticipant may engage in; or\n\n(c) provide that specified persons are no longer authorised to\nengage in controlled conduct for the purposes of the\ncontrolled operation; or\n\n(d) authorise participants in the controlled operation to engage in\nadditional or alternative controlled conduct.\n\n(3) A variation cannot be made that has the effect of extending the\nperiod of effect of an urgent authority.\nComLaw Authoritative Act C2012C00115\n\nSchedule 3  Amendments relating to controlled operations, assumed identities and\nwitness identity protection",
      "skos:definition": "(1) An appropriate authorising officer may vary an authority:\n\n(a) at any time on the authorising officer’s own initiative; or\n\n(b) on application under subsection 15GP(1).\n\n(2) A variation may:\n\n(a) extend the period of effect of the authority (subject to\nsubsections (3) and (4)); or\n\n(b) authorise additional persons to engage in controlled conduct\nfor the purposes of the controlled operation and specify:\n\n(i) with respect to additional law enforcement\nparticipants—the nature of the controlled conduct that\nthose participants may engage in; and\n\n(ii) with respect to additional civilian participants—the\nparticular controlled conduct (if any) that each such\nparticipant may engage in; or\n\n(c) provide that specified persons are no longer authorised to\nengage in controlled conduct for the purposes of the\ncontrolled operation; or\n\n(d) authorise participants in the controlled operation to engage in\nadditional or alternative controlled conduct.\n\n(3) A variation cannot be made that has the effect of extending the\nperiod of effect of an urgent authority.\nComLaw Authoritative Act C2012C00115\n\nSchedule 3  Amendments relating to controlled operations, assumed identities and\nwitness identity protection",
      "cml:hasPart": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:crimes-legislation-amendment-serious-and-organised-crime-act-2010-sch-3-sec-15go-ss-1"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:crimes-legislation-amendment-serious-and-organised-crime-act-2010-sch-3-sec-15go-ss-2"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:crimes-legislation-amendment-serious-and-organised-crime-act-2010-sch-3-sec-15go-ss-3"
        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "363b6875d7f6a92d58faa95f0f7d792750eebc1ac73a4415aba791db4119a937"
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/crimes-legislation-amendment-serious-and-organised-crime-act-2010#sch-3-sec-15go",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "15GO Variation of authority by appropriate authorising officer",
      "values:kind": "section",
      "cof:pageNumber": 77,
      "values:originalText": "(1) An appropriate authorising officer may vary an authority:\n\n(a) at any time on the authorising officer’s own initiative; or\n\n(b) on application under subsection 15GP(1).\n\n(2) A variation may:\n\n(a) extend the period of effect of the authority (subject to\nsubsections (3) and (4)); or\n\n(b) authorise additional persons to engage in controlled conduct\nfor the purposes of the controlled operation and specify:\n\n(i) with respect to additional law enforcement\nparticipants—the nature of the controlled conduct that\nthose participants may engage in; and\n\n(ii) with respect to additional civilian participants—the\nparticular controlled conduct (if any) that each such\nparticipant may engage in; or\n\n(c) provide that specified persons are no longer authorised to\nengage in controlled conduct for the purposes of the\ncontrolled operation; or\n\n(d) authorise participants in the controlled operation to engage in\nadditional or alternative controlled conduct.\n\n(3) A variation cannot be made that has the effect of extending the\nperiod of effect of an urgent authority.\nComLaw Authoritative Act C2012C00115\n\nSchedule 3  Amendments relating to controlled operations, assumed identities and\nwitness identity protection"
    },
