    {
      "@id": "concept:crimes-legislation-amendment-serious-and-organised-crime-act-2010-sch-3-sec-15gp-ss-6",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "15GP(6) Application to appropriate authorising officer",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/crimes-legislation-amendment-serious-and-organised-crime-act-2010#sch-3-sec-15gp-ss-6"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "crimes-legislation-amendment-serious-and-organised-crime-act-2010.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "crimes-legislation-amendment-serious-and-organised-crime-act-2010.pdf, p.78",
      "values:originalText": "(6) If the variation would extend the period of effect of a formal\nauthority, the application (whether a formal variation application or\nan urgent variation application) must state the proposed period of\nthe extension, which must not exceed:\n\n(a) in the case of a formal variation application—the period that\nwould result in the period of effect of the authority exceeding\n3 months (including any previous extensions); and\n\n(b) in the case of an urgent variation application—the lesser of:\n\n(i) 7 days; and\n\n(ii) a period that would result in the period of effect of the\nauthority exceeding 3 months (including any previous\nextensions).",
      "skos:definition": "(6) If the variation would extend the period of effect of a formal\nauthority, the application (whether a formal variation application or\nan urgent variation application) must state the proposed period of\nthe extension, which must not exceed:\n\n(a) in the case of a formal variation application—the period that\nwould result in the period of effect of the authority exceeding\n3 months (including any previous extensions); and\n\n(b) in the case of an urgent variation application—the lesser of:\n\n(i) 7 days; and\n\n(ii) a period that would result in the period of effect of the\nauthority exceeding 3 months (including any previous\nextensions).",
      "values:partOf": {
        "@id": "concept:crimes-legislation-amendment-serious-and-organised-crime-act-2010-sch-3-sec-15gp"
      },
      "cml:asserts": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:crimes-legislation-amendment-serious-and-organised-crime-act-2010-sch-3-sec-15gp-ss-6-norm"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:crimes-legislation-amendment-serious-and-organised-crime-act-2010-sch-3-sec-15gp-ss-6-logic-deontic-1"
        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "c08a7a73272ab4a49a50fde42a2149238b76eb734a18039b71ef8fe19cfd1b5e",
      "skos:note": "Application must state proposed period of extension not exceeding 3 months.",
      "dc:description": "Proposed period of extension"
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/crimes-legislation-amendment-serious-and-organised-crime-act-2010#sch-3-sec-15gp-ss-6",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "15GP(6) Application to appropriate authorising officer",
      "values:kind": "subsection",
      "cof:pageNumber": 78,
      "values:originalText": "(6) If the variation would extend the period of effect of a formal\nauthority, the application (whether a formal variation application or\nan urgent variation application) must state the proposed period of\nthe extension, which must not exceed:\n\n(a) in the case of a formal variation application—the period that\nwould result in the period of effect of the authority exceeding\n3 months (including any previous extensions); and\n\n(b) in the case of an urgent variation application—the lesser of:\n\n(i) 7 days; and\n\n(ii) a period that would result in the period of effect of the\nauthority exceeding 3 months (including any previous\nextensions)."
    },
    {
