    {
      "@id": "concept:crimes-legislation-amendment-serious-and-organised-crime-act-2010-sch-3-sec-15gr",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "15GR Manner of varying authority",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/crimes-legislation-amendment-serious-and-organised-crime-act-2010#sch-3-sec-15gr"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "crimes-legislation-amendment-serious-and-organised-crime-act-2010.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "crimes-legislation-amendment-serious-and-organised-crime-act-2010.pdf, p.81",
      "values:originalText": "(1) An authority may be varied by an appropriate authorising officer\n(whether on application or on the authorising officer’s own\ninitiative) only:\n\n(a) in the case of a variation on the authorising officer’s own\ninitiative or on a formal variation application (other than a\nvariation referred to in subparagraph (b)(ii))—by means of a\nwritten document, signed by the authorising officer (such a\nvariation is a formal variation of authority); or\n\n(b) in the case of a variation on:\n\n(i) an urgent variation application; or\n\n(ii) the authorising officer’s own initiative or a formal\nvariation application, if the authorising officer is\nsatisfied that the delay caused by granting a formal\nvariation of authority may affect the success of the\ncontrolled operation;\n\norally in person, or by telephone or any other means of\ncommunication (such a variation is an urgent variation of\nauthority).\n\n(2) The authorising officer must, as soon as practicable, prepare and\ngive a written document that complies with section 15GS to the\napplicant or, if the variation was on the initiative of the authorising\nofficer, to the principal law enforcement officer for the controlled\noperation.",
      "skos:definition": "(1) An authority may be varied by an appropriate authorising officer\n(whether on application or on the authorising officer’s own\ninitiative) only:\n\n(a) in the case of a variation on the authorising officer’s own\ninitiative or on a formal variation application (other than a\nvariation referred to in subparagraph (b)(ii))—by means of a\nwritten document, signed by the authorising officer (such a\nvariation is a formal variation of authority); or\n\n(b) in the case of a variation on:\n\n(i) an urgent variation application; or\n\n(ii) the authorising officer’s own initiative or a formal\nvariation application, if the authorising officer is\nsatisfied that the delay caused by granting a formal\nvariation of authority may affect the success of the\ncontrolled operation;\n\norally in person, or by telephone or any other means of\ncommunication (such a variation is an urgent variation of\nauthority).\n\n(2) The authorising officer must, as soon as practicable, prepare and\ngive a written document that complies with section 15GS to the\napplicant or, if the variation was on the initiative of the authorising\nofficer, to the principal law enforcement officer for the controlled\noperation.",
      "cml:hasPart": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:crimes-legislation-amendment-serious-and-organised-crime-act-2010-sch-3-sec-15gr-ss-1"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:crimes-legislation-amendment-serious-and-organised-crime-act-2010-sch-3-sec-15gr-ss-2"
        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "28218ca3ece865792f8736bdeddc16594c4a22ed15900e212ac5eba2ae4d913a"
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/crimes-legislation-amendment-serious-and-organised-crime-act-2010#sch-3-sec-15gr",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "15GR Manner of varying authority",
      "values:kind": "section",
      "cof:pageNumber": 81,
      "values:originalText": "(1) An authority may be varied by an appropriate authorising officer\n(whether on application or on the authorising officer’s own\ninitiative) only:\n\n(a) in the case of a variation on the authorising officer’s own\ninitiative or on a formal variation application (other than a\nvariation referred to in subparagraph (b)(ii))—by means of a\nwritten document, signed by the authorising officer (such a\nvariation is a formal variation of authority); or\n\n(b) in the case of a variation on:\n\n(i) an urgent variation application; or\n\n(ii) the authorising officer’s own initiative or a formal\nvariation application, if the authorising officer is\nsatisfied that the delay caused by granting a formal\nvariation of authority may affect the success of the\ncontrolled operation;\n\norally in person, or by telephone or any other means of\ncommunication (such a variation is an urgent variation of\nauthority).\n\n(2) The authorising officer must, as soon as practicable, prepare and\ngive a written document that complies with section 15GS to the\napplicant or, if the variation was on the initiative of the authorising\nofficer, to the principal law enforcement officer for the controlled\noperation."
    },
