      },
      "dc:source": "crimes-legislation-amendment-serious-and-organised-crime-act-2010.pdf, p.81",
      "values:originalText": "(1) A variation of an authority by an appropriate authorising officer\n(whether formal or urgent) must:\n\n(a) identify the controlled operation to which the authority\nrelates; and\n\n(b) state the name and rank or position of the person varying the\nauthority; and\n\n(c) if the authority was varied on an application made under\nsection 15GP, state:\n\n(i) the name of the applicant; and\n\n(ii) whether the application was a formal variation\napplication or an urgent variation application; and\nComLaw Authoritative Act C2012C00115\n\nSchedule 3  Amendments relating to controlled operations, assumed identities and\nwitness identity protection",
      "skos:definition": "(1) A variation of an authority by an appropriate authorising officer\n(whether formal or urgent) must:\n\n(a) identify the controlled operation to which the authority\nrelates; and\n\n(b) state the name and rank or position of the person varying the\nauthority; and\n\n(c) if the authority was varied on an application made under\nsection 15GP, state:\n\n(i) the name of the applicant; and\n\n(ii) whether the application was a formal variation\napplication or an urgent variation application; and\nComLaw Authoritative Act C2012C00115\n\nSchedule 3  Amendments relating to controlled operations, assumed identities and\nwitness identity protection",
