    {
      "@id": "concept:crimes-legislation-amendment-serious-and-organised-crime-act-2010-sch-3-sec-78",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "78 Crimes Legislation Amendment (Serious and Organised Crime) Act",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/crimes-legislation-amendment-serious-and-organised-crime-act-2010#sch-3-sec-78"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "crimes-legislation-amendment-serious-and-organised-crime-act-2010.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "crimes-legislation-amendment-serious-and-organised-crime-act-2010.pdf, p.82",
      "values:originalText": "(d) state the date and time when the variation of authority is or\nwas granted; and\n\n(e) describe the variation having regard to the matters referred to\nin subsection 15GO(2); and\n\n(f) if the variation extends the period of effect of a formal\nauthority—state the period of the extension.\n\n(2) For the purposes of paragraph (1)(f), the period of the extension\nmust not exceed:\n\n(a) in the case of a formal variation of authority—the period that\nwould result in the period of effect of the authority exceeding\n3 months (including any previous extensions); and\n\n(b) in the case of an urgent variation of authority—the lesser of:\n\n(i) 7 days; and\n\n(ii) a period that would result in the period of effect of the\nauthority exceeding 3 months (including any previous\nextensions).\nSubdivision C—Variations of authorities by nominated\nTribunal member: extensions beyond 3 months",
      "skos:definition": "(d) state the date and time when the variation of authority is or\nwas granted; and\n\n(e) describe the variation having regard to the matters referred to\nin subsection 15GO(2); and\n\n(f) if the variation extends the period of effect of a formal\nauthority—state the period of the extension.\n\n(2) For the purposes of paragraph (1)(f), the period of the extension\nmust not exceed:\n\n(a) in the case of a formal variation of authority—the period that\nwould result in the period of effect of the authority exceeding\n3 months (including any previous extensions); and\n\n(b) in the case of an urgent variation of authority—the lesser of:\n\n(i) 7 days; and\n\n(ii) a period that would result in the period of effect of the\nauthority exceeding 3 months (including any previous\nextensions).\nSubdivision C—Variations of authorities by nominated\nTribunal member: extensions beyond 3 months",
      "cml:asserts": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:crimes-legislation-amendment-serious-and-organised-crime-act-2010-sch-3-sec-78-norm"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:crimes-legislation-amendment-serious-and-organised-crime-act-2010-sch-3-sec-78-logic-deontic-1"
        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "cf32ea3266f2235fef56d0c55bb2fd5464f1b040d98b590a393c3e8f0c881caf",
      "skos:note": "Provide details about a variation of authority, including date and time, description, and period of extension.",
      "dc:description": "true"
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/crimes-legislation-amendment-serious-and-organised-crime-act-2010#sch-3-sec-78",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
