      "cof:title": "15GT(4) Variation of formal authority to extend period of effect",
      "values:kind": "subsection",
      "cof:pageNumber": 82,
      "values:originalText": "(4) A nominated Tribunal member may only vary a formal authority\nduring the period of 2 weeks before the end of the period of effect\nof the authority.\nComLaw Authoritative Act C2012C00115\n\nAmendments relating to controlled operations, assumed identities and witness identity\nprotection  Schedule 3\nMain amendments  Part 1\n\nCrimes Legislation Amendment (Serious and Organised Crime) Act 2010"
    },
    {
      "@id": "concept:crimes-legislation-amendment-serious-and-organised-crime-act-2010-sch-3-sec-15gt-ss-4-norm",
      "@type": "values:Obligation",
      "cml:modality": {
        "@id": "cml:Deontic"
      },
      "values:partOf": {
        "@id": "concept:crimes-legislation-amendment-serious-and-organised-crime-act-2010-sch-3-sec-15gt-ss-4"
      },
      "values:deonticStatus": {
        "@id": "values:HeuristicDerived"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "values:borneBy": {
        "@id": "values:Agent"
      }
    },
    {
      "@id": "concept:crimes-legislation-amendment-serious-and-organised-crime-act-2010-sch-3-sec-15gt-ss-4-logic-deontic-1",
      "@type": "cml:LogicApplication",
      "cml:modality": {
