      "dc:source": "crimes-legislation-amendment-serious-and-organised-crime-act-2010.pdf, p.83",
      "values:originalText": "(5) An application for a variation (whether a formal variation\napplication or an urgent variation application) must state:\n\n(a) whether or not the controlled operation has been the subject\nof an earlier urgent variation application under this section\nand, if so:\nComLaw Authoritative Act C2012C00115\n\nSchedule 3  Amendments relating to controlled operations, assumed identities and\nwitness identity protection",
      "skos:definition": "(5) An application for a variation (whether a formal variation\napplication or an urgent variation application) must state:\n\n(a) whether or not the controlled operation has been the subject\nof an earlier urgent variation application under this section\nand, if so:\nComLaw Authoritative Act C2012C00115\n\nSchedule 3  Amendments relating to controlled operations, assumed identities and\nwitness identity protection",
