    {
      "@id": "concept:crimes-legislation-amendment-serious-and-organised-crime-act-2010-sch-3-sec-80",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "80 Crimes Legislation Amendment (Serious and Organised Crime) Act",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/crimes-legislation-amendment-serious-and-organised-crime-act-2010#sch-3-sec-80"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "crimes-legislation-amendment-serious-and-organised-crime-act-2010.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "crimes-legislation-amendment-serious-and-organised-crime-act-2010.pdf, p.84",
      "values:originalText": "(i) whether the urgent variation application was the last\napplication under this section for a variation; and\n\n(ii) whether or not the variation was granted; and\n\n(b) the proposed period of the extension, which must be such as\nto comply with subsection (2) and must not exceed:\n\n(i) in the case of a formal variation application—3 months;\nand\n\n(ii) in the case of an urgent variation application—7 days.\n\n(6) The nominated Tribunal member may require the applicant to\nprovide such information concerning the proposed variation as is\nnecessary for the nominated Tribunal member’s proper\nconsideration of the application.\n\n(7) As soon as practicable after making an urgent variation application\nthat was not made in writing, the applicant must make a written\nrecord of the application and give a copy of it to the nominated\nTribunal member to whom the application was made.",
      "skos:definition": "(i) whether the urgent variation application was the last\napplication under this section for a variation; and\n\n(ii) whether or not the variation was granted; and\n\n(b) the proposed period of the extension, which must be such as\nto comply with subsection (2) and must not exceed:\n\n(i) in the case of a formal variation application—3 months;\nand\n\n(ii) in the case of an urgent variation application—7 days.\n\n(6) The nominated Tribunal member may require the applicant to\nprovide such information concerning the proposed variation as is\nnecessary for the nominated Tribunal member’s proper\nconsideration of the application.\n\n(7) As soon as practicable after making an urgent variation application\nthat was not made in writing, the applicant must make a written\nrecord of the application and give a copy of it to the nominated\nTribunal member to whom the application was made.",
      "cml:hasPart": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:crimes-legislation-amendment-serious-and-organised-crime-act-2010-sch-3-sec-80-ss-6"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:crimes-legislation-amendment-serious-and-organised-crime-act-2010-sch-3-sec-80-ss-7"
        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "81c13dafcfe2ce4183d4632a40fb4f07cad1742bb669b0dba663e34de8733f0c"
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/crimes-legislation-amendment-serious-and-organised-crime-act-2010#sch-3-sec-80",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "80 Crimes Legislation Amendment (Serious and Organised Crime) Act",
      "values:kind": "section",
      "cof:pageNumber": 84,
      "values:originalText": "(i) whether the urgent variation application was the last\napplication under this section for a variation; and\n\n(ii) whether or not the variation was granted; and\n\n(b) the proposed period of the extension, which must be such as\nto comply with subsection (2) and must not exceed:\n\n(i) in the case of a formal variation application—3 months;\nand\n\n(ii) in the case of an urgent variation application—7 days.\n\n(6) The nominated Tribunal member may require the applicant to\nprovide such information concerning the proposed variation as is\nnecessary for the nominated Tribunal member’s proper\nconsideration of the application.\n\n(7) As soon as practicable after making an urgent variation application\nthat was not made in writing, the applicant must make a written\nrecord of the application and give a copy of it to the nominated\nTribunal member to whom the application was made."
    },
