    {
      "@id": "concept:crimes-legislation-amendment-serious-and-organised-crime-act-2010-sch-3-sec-15gy",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "15GY Cancellation of authorities",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/crimes-legislation-amendment-serious-and-organised-crime-act-2010#sch-3-sec-15gy"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "crimes-legislation-amendment-serious-and-organised-crime-act-2010.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "crimes-legislation-amendment-serious-and-organised-crime-act-2010.pdf, p.86",
      "values:originalText": "(1) An appropriate authorising officer may, by order in writing given\nto the principal law enforcement officer for a controlled operation,\nComLaw Authoritative Act C2012C00115\n\nAmendments relating to controlled operations, assumed identities and witness identity\nprotection  Schedule 3\nMain amendments  Part 1\n\nCrimes Legislation Amendment (Serious and Organised Crime) Act 2010\ncancel the authority to conduct the controlled operation at any time\nand for any reason.\n\n(2) Without limiting subsection (1), an appropriate authorising officer\nmay cancel an authority at any time at the request of the principal\nlaw enforcement officer for the controlled operation concerned.\n\n(3) Cancellation of an authority takes effect at the time the order is\nmade or at the later time specified in the order.",
      "skos:definition": "(1) An appropriate authorising officer may, by order in writing given\nto the principal law enforcement officer for a controlled operation,\nComLaw Authoritative Act C2012C00115\n\nAmendments relating to controlled operations, assumed identities and witness identity\nprotection  Schedule 3\nMain amendments  Part 1\n\nCrimes Legislation Amendment (Serious and Organised Crime) Act 2010\ncancel the authority to conduct the controlled operation at any time\nand for any reason.\n\n(2) Without limiting subsection (1), an appropriate authorising officer\nmay cancel an authority at any time at the request of the principal\nlaw enforcement officer for the controlled operation concerned.\n\n(3) Cancellation of an authority takes effect at the time the order is\nmade or at the later time specified in the order.",
      "cml:hasPart": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:crimes-legislation-amendment-serious-and-organised-crime-act-2010-sch-3-sec-15gy-ss-1"
        },
        {
