      "skos:definition": "(1) Subject to subsection (2), an authority:\n\n(a) authorises each law enforcement participant in the controlled\noperation to which the authority relates who is identified in\nthe authority to engage in the controlled conduct specified in\nthe authority in respect of that participant; and\n\n(b) authorises each civilian participant (if any) in the controlled\noperation to which the authority relates who is identified in\nthe authority to engage in the particular controlled conduct (if\nany) specified in the authority in respect of that participant.",
      "values:partOf": {
        "@id": "concept:crimes-legislation-amendment-serious-and-organised-crime-act-2010-sch-3-sec-15gz"
      },
      "cml:asserts": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:crimes-legislation-amendment-serious-and-organised-crime-act-2010-sch-3-sec-15gz-ss-1-norm"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:crimes-legislation-amendment-serious-and-organised-crime-act-2010-sch-3-sec-15gz-ss-1-logic-deontic-1"
        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "09f119074b9ea46da5d44ff3b3cc2188d72f9d26f17ec8a3a299484d92206812",
      "skos:note": "Authorises law enforcement participants to engage in controlled conduct."
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/crimes-legislation-amendment-serious-and-organised-crime-act-2010#sch-3-sec-15gz-ss-1",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "15GZ(1) Effect of authorities",
      "values:kind": "subsection",
      "cof:pageNumber": 87,
      "values:originalText": "(1) Subject to subsection (2), an authority:\n\n(a) authorises each law enforcement participant in the controlled\noperation to which the authority relates who is identified in\nthe authority to engage in the controlled conduct specified in\nthe authority in respect of that participant; and\n\n(b) authorises each civilian participant (if any) in the controlled\noperation to which the authority relates who is identified in\nthe authority to engage in the particular controlled conduct (if\nany) specified in the authority in respect of that participant."
    },
