      "cml:premiseText": "(e) if the participant is a civilian participant in the operation—he\nor she acts in accordance with the instructions of a law\nenforcement officer.",
      "cml:conclusionText": "The participant must act."
    },
    {
      "@id": "concept:crimes-legislation-amendment-serious-and-organised-crime-act-2010-sch-3-sec-15hb",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "15HB Indemnification of participants against civil liability",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/crimes-legislation-amendment-serious-and-organised-crime-act-2010#sch-3-sec-15hb"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "crimes-legislation-amendment-serious-and-organised-crime-act-2010.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "crimes-legislation-amendment-serious-and-organised-crime-act-2010.pdf, p.88",
      "values:originalText": "The Commonwealth must indemnify a participant in a controlled\noperation against any civil liability (including reasonable costs) the\nparticipant incurs because of conduct the participant engages in if:\nComLaw Authoritative Act C2012C00115\n\nAmendments relating to controlled operations, assumed identities and witness identity\nprotection  Schedule 3\nMain amendments  Part 1\n\nCrimes Legislation Amendment (Serious and Organised Crime) Act 2010\n\n(a) the participant engages in the conduct in the course of, and\nfor the purposes of, the controlled operation in accordance\nwith the authority to conduct the controlled operation; and\n\n(b) the participant is identified in the authority as a person\nauthorised to engage in controlled conduct for the purposes\nof the controlled operation; and\n\n(c) the conduct does not involve the participant intentionally\ninducing a person to commit a Commonwealth offence or an\noffence under a law of a State or Territory that the person\nwould not otherwise have intended to commit; and\n\n(d) the conduct does not involve the participant engaging in any\nconduct that is likely to:\n\n(i) cause the death of, or serious injury to, any person; or\n\n(ii) involve the commission of a sexual offence against any\nperson; and\n\n(e) if the participant is a civilian participant in the operation—he\nor she acts in accordance with the instructions of a law\nenforcement officer; and\n\n(f) the requirements (if any) specified in the regulations have\nbeen met.",
      "skos:definition": "The Commonwealth must indemnify a participant in a controlled\noperation against any civil liability (including reasonable costs) the\nparticipant incurs because of conduct the participant engages in if:\nComLaw Authoritative Act C2012C00115\n\nAmendments relating to controlled operations, assumed identities and witness identity\nprotection  Schedule 3\nMain amendments  Part 1\n\nCrimes Legislation Amendment (Serious and Organised Crime) Act 2010\n\n(a) the participant engages in the conduct in the course of, and\nfor the purposes of, the controlled operation in accordance\nwith the authority to conduct the controlled operation; and\n\n(b) the participant is identified in the authority as a person\nauthorised to engage in controlled conduct for the purposes\nof the controlled operation; and\n\n(c) the conduct does not involve the participant intentionally\ninducing a person to commit a Commonwealth offence or an\noffence under a law of a State or Territory that the person\nwould not otherwise have intended to commit; and\n\n(d) the conduct does not involve the participant engaging in any\nconduct that is likely to:\n\n(i) cause the death of, or serious injury to, any person; or\n\n(ii) involve the commission of a sexual offence against any\nperson; and\n\n(e) if the participant is a civilian participant in the operation—he\nor she acts in accordance with the instructions of a law\nenforcement officer; and\n\n(f) the requirements (if any) specified in the regulations have\nbeen met.",
      "cml:asserts": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:crimes-legislation-amendment-serious-and-organised-crime-act-2010-sch-3-sec-15hb-norm"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:crimes-legislation-amendment-serious-and-organised-crime-act-2010-sch-3-sec-15hb-logic-deontic-1"
        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "69c5b0d5adb96a3f4afa51078d9889a99e9c995eb160edfe63f4a1514c1eebe6",
      "skos:note": "The Commonwealth must indemnify a participant in a controlled operation against any civil liability."
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/crimes-legislation-amendment-serious-and-organised-crime-act-2010#sch-3-sec-15hb",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "15HB Indemnification of participants against civil liability",
      "values:kind": "section",
      "cof:pageNumber": 88,
      "values:originalText": "The Commonwealth must indemnify a participant in a controlled\noperation against any civil liability (including reasonable costs) the\nparticipant incurs because of conduct the participant engages in if:\nComLaw Authoritative Act C2012C00115\n\nAmendments relating to controlled operations, assumed identities and witness identity\nprotection  Schedule 3\nMain amendments  Part 1\n\nCrimes Legislation Amendment (Serious and Organised Crime) Act 2010\n\n(a) the participant engages in the conduct in the course of, and\nfor the purposes of, the controlled operation in accordance\nwith the authority to conduct the controlled operation; and\n\n(b) the participant is identified in the authority as a person\nauthorised to engage in controlled conduct for the purposes\nof the controlled operation; and\n\n(c) the conduct does not involve the participant intentionally\ninducing a person to commit a Commonwealth offence or an\noffence under a law of a State or Territory that the person\nwould not otherwise have intended to commit; and\n\n(d) the conduct does not involve the participant engaging in any\nconduct that is likely to:\n\n(i) cause the death of, or serious injury to, any person; or\n\n(ii) involve the commission of a sexual offence against any\nperson; and\n\n(e) if the participant is a civilian participant in the operation—he\nor she acts in accordance with the instructions of a law\nenforcement officer; and\n\n(f) the requirements (if any) specified in the regulations have\nbeen met."
    },
    {
      "@id": "concept:crimes-legislation-amendment-serious-and-organised-crime-act-2010-sch-3-sec-15hb-norm",
      "@type": "values:Obligation",
      "cml:modality": {
        "@id": "cml:Deontic"
      },
      "values:partOf": {
        "@id": "concept:crimes-legislation-amendment-serious-and-organised-crime-act-2010-sch-3-sec-15hb"
      },
      "values:deonticStatus": {
        "@id": "values:HeuristicDerived"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "values:borneBy": {
        "@id": "values:State"
      },
      "skos:scopeNote": "borne by: State"
    },
    {
      "@id": "concept:crimes-legislation-amendment-serious-and-organised-crime-act-2010-sch-3-sec-15hb-logic-deontic-1",
      "@type": "cml:LogicApplication",
      "cml:modality": {
        "@id": "cml:Deontic"
      },
      "cml:operator": "Obligation",
      "cml:logicSummary": "The Commonwealth has an obligation to indemnify a participant.",
      "cml:executionSurface": "modalities::logic::deontic",
      "cml:confidence": {
        "@value": 1.0,
        "@type": "xsd:decimal"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      }
    },
    {
      "@id": "concept:crimes-legislation-amendment-serious-and-organised-crime-act-2010-sch-3-sec-15hc",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "15HC Effect of sections 15HA and 15HB on other laws relating to",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/crimes-legislation-amendment-serious-and-organised-crime-act-2010#sch-3-sec-15hc"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "crimes-legislation-amendment-serious-and-organised-crime-act-2010.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "crimes-legislation-amendment-serious-and-organised-crime-act-2010.pdf, p.89",
      "values:originalText": "criminal investigation\n\nSections 15HA and 15HB do not apply to a person’s conduct that\nis, or could have been, authorised under Commonwealth law or a\nlaw of a State or Territory relating to the following:\n\n(a) arrest or detention of individuals;\n\n(b) searches of individuals;\n\n(c) entry onto, or searches or inspection of, premises;\n\n(d) searches, inspections or seizures of other property;\n\n(e) forensic procedure;\n\n(f) electronic surveillance devices or telecommunications\ninterception;\n\n(g) identification procedures;\n\n(h) the acquisition or use of assumed identities;\n\n(i) any other matter concerning powers of criminal investigation.\nComLaw Authoritative Act C2012C00115\n\nSchedule 3  Amendments relating to controlled operations, assumed identities and\nwitness identity protection",
      "skos:definition": "criminal investigation\n\nSections 15HA and 15HB do not apply to a person’s conduct that\nis, or could have been, authorised under Commonwealth law or a\nlaw of a State or Territory relating to the following:\n\n(a) arrest or detention of individuals;\n\n(b) searches of individuals;\n\n(c) entry onto, or searches or inspection of, premises;\n\n(d) searches, inspections or seizures of other property;\n\n(e) forensic procedure;\n\n(f) electronic surveillance devices or telecommunications\ninterception;\n\n(g) identification procedures;\n\n(h) the acquisition or use of assumed identities;\n\n(i) any other matter concerning powers of criminal investigation.\nComLaw Authoritative Act C2012C00115\n\nSchedule 3  Amendments relating to controlled operations, assumed identities and\nwitness identity protection",
      "cml:asserts": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:crimes-legislation-amendment-serious-and-organised-crime-act-2010-sch-3-sec-15hc-norm"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:crimes-legislation-amendment-serious-and-organised-crime-act-2010-sch-3-sec-15hc-logic-deontic-1"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:crimes-legislation-amendment-serious-and-organised-crime-act-2010-sch-3-sec-15hc-logic-alleninterval-2"
        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "f403ef636f3396b1349cae92c3fa78283a5a4d017682fd87aaa3d372137c7d83",
      "skos:note": "Exemptions from sections 15HA and 15HB"
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/crimes-legislation-amendment-serious-and-organised-crime-act-2010#sch-3-sec-15hc",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "15HC Effect of sections 15HA and 15HB on other laws relating to",
      "values:kind": "section",
      "cof:pageNumber": 89,
      "values:originalText": "criminal investigation\n\nSections 15HA and 15HB do not apply to a person’s conduct that\nis, or could have been, authorised under Commonwealth law or a\nlaw of a State or Territory relating to the following:\n\n(a) arrest or detention of individuals;\n\n(b) searches of individuals;\n\n(c) entry onto, or searches or inspection of, premises;\n\n(d) searches, inspections or seizures of other property;\n\n(e) forensic procedure;\n\n(f) electronic surveillance devices or telecommunications\ninterception;\n\n(g) identification procedures;\n\n(h) the acquisition or use of assumed identities;\n\n(i) any other matter concerning powers of criminal investigation.\nComLaw Authoritative Act C2012C00115\n\nSchedule 3  Amendments relating to controlled operations, assumed identities and\nwitness identity protection"
