    {
      "@id": "concept:crimes-legislation-amendment-serious-and-organised-crime-act-2010-sch-3-sec-15hd",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "15HD Effect of being unaware of variation or cancellation of",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/crimes-legislation-amendment-serious-and-organised-crime-act-2010#sch-3-sec-15hd"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "crimes-legislation-amendment-serious-and-organised-crime-act-2010.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "crimes-legislation-amendment-serious-and-organised-crime-act-2010.pdf, p.90",
      "values:originalText": "authority\n\n(1) If an authority to conduct a controlled operation is varied in a way\nthat limits its scope, this Part continues to apply to a participant in\nthe controlled operation as if the authority had not been varied in\nthat way, for so long as the participant:\n\n(a) is unaware of the variation; and\n\n(b) is not reckless about the existence of the variation.\n\n(2) If an authority to conduct a controlled operation is cancelled, this\nPart continues to apply to a person who was a participant in the\ncontrolled operation immediately before the cancellation as if the\nauthority had not been cancelled in that way, for so long as the\nperson:\n\n(a) is unaware of the cancellation; and\n\n(b) is not reckless about the existence of the cancellation.\n\n(3) For the purposes of this section, a person is reckless about the\nexistence of the variation or cancellation of an authority if:\n\n(a) the person is aware of a substantial risk that the variation or\ncancellation has happened; and\n\n(b) having regard to the circumstances known to the person, it is\nunjustifiable to take the risk that the authority has not been\nvaried or cancelled.",
      "skos:definition": "authority\n\n(1) If an authority to conduct a controlled operation is varied in a way\nthat limits its scope, this Part continues to apply to a participant in\nthe controlled operation as if the authority had not been varied in\nthat way, for so long as the participant:\n\n(a) is unaware of the variation; and\n\n(b) is not reckless about the existence of the variation.\n\n(2) If an authority to conduct a controlled operation is cancelled, this\nPart continues to apply to a person who was a participant in the\ncontrolled operation immediately before the cancellation as if the\nauthority had not been cancelled in that way, for so long as the\nperson:\n\n(a) is unaware of the cancellation; and\n\n(b) is not reckless about the existence of the cancellation.\n\n(3) For the purposes of this section, a person is reckless about the\nexistence of the variation or cancellation of an authority if:\n\n(a) the person is aware of a substantial risk that the variation or\ncancellation has happened; and\n\n(b) having regard to the circumstances known to the person, it is\nunjustifiable to take the risk that the authority has not been\nvaried or cancelled.",
      "cml:hasPart": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:crimes-legislation-amendment-serious-and-organised-crime-act-2010-sch-3-sec-15hd-ss-1"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:crimes-legislation-amendment-serious-and-organised-crime-act-2010-sch-3-sec-15hd-ss-2"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:crimes-legislation-amendment-serious-and-organised-crime-act-2010-sch-3-sec-15hd-ss-3"
        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "8f76fd501bb68ef71f4e276bc28f29bce1003b0c2c9d9478de81b5bfc0cde1e9"
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/crimes-legislation-amendment-serious-and-organised-crime-act-2010#sch-3-sec-15hd",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "15HD Effect of being unaware of variation or cancellation of",
      "values:kind": "section",
      "cof:pageNumber": 90,
      "values:originalText": "authority\n\n(1) If an authority to conduct a controlled operation is varied in a way\nthat limits its scope, this Part continues to apply to a participant in\nthe controlled operation as if the authority had not been varied in\nthat way, for so long as the participant:\n\n(a) is unaware of the variation; and\n\n(b) is not reckless about the existence of the variation.\n\n(2) If an authority to conduct a controlled operation is cancelled, this\nPart continues to apply to a person who was a participant in the\ncontrolled operation immediately before the cancellation as if the\nauthority had not been cancelled in that way, for so long as the\nperson:\n\n(a) is unaware of the cancellation; and\n\n(b) is not reckless about the existence of the cancellation.\n\n(3) For the purposes of this section, a person is reckless about the\nexistence of the variation or cancellation of an authority if:\n\n(a) the person is aware of a substantial risk that the variation or\ncancellation has happened; and\n\n(b) having regard to the circumstances known to the person, it is\nunjustifiable to take the risk that the authority has not been\nvaried or cancelled."
    },
