          "@id": "concept:crimes-legislation-amendment-serious-and-organised-crime-act-2010-sch-3-sec-15hd-ss-3-logic-deontic-1"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:crimes-legislation-amendment-serious-and-organised-crime-act-2010-sch-3-sec-15hd-ss-3-logic-epistemic-2"
        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "a16f3b6642329a11ba4c6ccd3d27fefa3e097c79200cc10ca299afbbef042616",
      "skos:note": "Be aware of substantial risk that authority has not been varied or cancelled."
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/crimes-legislation-amendment-serious-and-organised-crime-act-2010#sch-3-sec-15hd-ss-3",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "15HD(3) Effect of being unaware of variation or cancellation of",
      "values:kind": "subsection",
      "cof:pageNumber": 90,
      "values:originalText": "(3) For the purposes of this section, a person is reckless about the\nexistence of the variation or cancellation of an authority if:\n\n(a) the person is aware of a substantial risk that the variation or\ncancellation has happened; and\n\n(b) having regard to the circumstances known to the person, it is\nunjustifiable to take the risk that the authority has not been\nvaried or cancelled."
    },
