    },
    {
      "@id": "concept:crimes-legislation-amendment-serious-and-organised-crime-act-2010-sch-3-sec-15hh",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "15HH Protection from criminal responsibility for conduct under a",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/crimes-legislation-amendment-serious-and-organised-crime-act-2010#sch-3-sec-15hh"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "crimes-legislation-amendment-serious-and-organised-crime-act-2010.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "crimes-legislation-amendment-serious-and-organised-crime-act-2010.pdf, p.93",
      "values:originalText": "corresponding State controlled operations law\n\n(1) This section applies to a participant in an operation authorised\nunder a corresponding State controlled operations law if:\n\n(a) the participant engages in conduct in the course of, and for\nthe purposes of, the operation; and\n\n(b) engaging in that conduct is a Commonwealth offence.\n\n(2) Despite any other law of the Commonwealth, the participant is not\ncriminally responsible for the Commonwealth offence, if:\n\n(a) the conduct is authorised by, and is engaged in in accordance\nwith, the authority to conduct the controlled operation; and\n\n(b) the conduct does not involve the participant intentionally\ninducing a person to commit a Commonwealth offence or an\noffence against a law of a State or Territory that the person\nwould not otherwise have intended to commit; and\n\n(c) the conduct does not involve the participant engaging in any\nconduct that is likely to:\n\n(i) cause the death of, or serious injury to, any person; or\n\n(ii) involve the commission of a sexual offence against any\nperson; and\n\n(d) if the person is a civilian participant in the operation—he or\nshe acts in accordance with the instructions of a law\nenforcement officer.\n\n(3) Expressions used in this section have the same meanings as in the\ncorresponding State controlled operations law under which the\noperation was authorised.",
      "skos:definition": "corresponding State controlled operations law\n\n(1) This section applies to a participant in an operation authorised\nunder a corresponding State controlled operations law if:\n\n(a) the participant engages in conduct in the course of, and for\nthe purposes of, the operation; and\n\n(b) engaging in that conduct is a Commonwealth offence.\n\n(2) Despite any other law of the Commonwealth, the participant is not\ncriminally responsible for the Commonwealth offence, if:\n\n(a) the conduct is authorised by, and is engaged in in accordance\nwith, the authority to conduct the controlled operation; and\n\n(b) the conduct does not involve the participant intentionally\ninducing a person to commit a Commonwealth offence or an\noffence against a law of a State or Territory that the person\nwould not otherwise have intended to commit; and\n\n(c) the conduct does not involve the participant engaging in any\nconduct that is likely to:\n\n(i) cause the death of, or serious injury to, any person; or\n\n(ii) involve the commission of a sexual offence against any\nperson; and\n\n(d) if the person is a civilian participant in the operation—he or\nshe acts in accordance with the instructions of a law\nenforcement officer.\n\n(3) Expressions used in this section have the same meanings as in the\ncorresponding State controlled operations law under which the\noperation was authorised.",
      "cml:hasPart": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:crimes-legislation-amendment-serious-and-organised-crime-act-2010-sch-3-sec-15hh-ss-1"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:crimes-legislation-amendment-serious-and-organised-crime-act-2010-sch-3-sec-15hh-ss-2"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:crimes-legislation-amendment-serious-and-organised-crime-act-2010-sch-3-sec-15hh-ss-3"
        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "7463f4a19ba92dedcd97556c59524278b43a6f3faefccbbf1f42a1b66391a75c"
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/crimes-legislation-amendment-serious-and-organised-crime-act-2010#sch-3-sec-15hh",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "15HH Protection from criminal responsibility for conduct under a",
      "values:kind": "section",
      "cof:pageNumber": 93,
      "values:originalText": "corresponding State controlled operations law\n\n(1) This section applies to a participant in an operation authorised\nunder a corresponding State controlled operations law if:\n\n(a) the participant engages in conduct in the course of, and for\nthe purposes of, the operation; and\n\n(b) engaging in that conduct is a Commonwealth offence.\n\n(2) Despite any other law of the Commonwealth, the participant is not\ncriminally responsible for the Commonwealth offence, if:\n\n(a) the conduct is authorised by, and is engaged in in accordance\nwith, the authority to conduct the controlled operation; and\n\n(b) the conduct does not involve the participant intentionally\ninducing a person to commit a Commonwealth offence or an\noffence against a law of a State or Territory that the person\nwould not otherwise have intended to commit; and\n\n(c) the conduct does not involve the participant engaging in any\nconduct that is likely to:\n\n(i) cause the death of, or serious injury to, any person; or\n\n(ii) involve the commission of a sexual offence against any\nperson; and\n\n(d) if the person is a civilian participant in the operation—he or\nshe acts in accordance with the instructions of a law\nenforcement officer.\n\n(3) Expressions used in this section have the same meanings as in the\ncorresponding State controlled operations law under which the\noperation was authorised."
    },
