    {
      "@id": "concept:crimes-legislation-amendment-serious-and-organised-crime-act-2010-sch-3-sec-15hj",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "15HJ Protection from criminal responsibility for certain ancillary",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/crimes-legislation-amendment-serious-and-organised-crime-act-2010#sch-3-sec-15hj"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "crimes-legislation-amendment-serious-and-organised-crime-act-2010.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "crimes-legislation-amendment-serious-and-organised-crime-act-2010.pdf, p.94",
      "values:originalText": "conduct\n\n(1) This section applies if:\n\n(a) a person engages in conduct (the ancillary conduct) that\nrelates to conduct (the related conduct) that:\n\n(i) was engaged in by another person; and\n\n(ii) constitutes an offence for which a person would, but for\nsection 15HH, be criminally responsible; and\n\n(b) engaging in the ancillary conduct is an ancillary offence\n(within the meaning of the Criminal Code) in relation to the\noffence constituted by the related conduct.\n\n(2) Despite any law of the Commonwealth, the person who engaged in\nthe ancillary conduct is not criminally responsible for the ancillary\noffence if, at the time the person engaged in the ancillary conduct,\nhe or she believed the related conduct was being engaged in, or\nwould be engaged in, by a participant in an operation authorised\nunder a corresponding State controlled operations law.\n\n(3) Expressions used in this section have the same meanings as in the\ncorresponding State controlled operations law under which the\nperson believed the controlled conduct was being engaged in.",
      "skos:definition": "conduct\n\n(1) This section applies if:\n\n(a) a person engages in conduct (the ancillary conduct) that\nrelates to conduct (the related conduct) that:\n\n(i) was engaged in by another person; and\n\n(ii) constitutes an offence for which a person would, but for\nsection 15HH, be criminally responsible; and\n\n(b) engaging in the ancillary conduct is an ancillary offence\n(within the meaning of the Criminal Code) in relation to the\noffence constituted by the related conduct.\n\n(2) Despite any law of the Commonwealth, the person who engaged in\nthe ancillary conduct is not criminally responsible for the ancillary\noffence if, at the time the person engaged in the ancillary conduct,\nhe or she believed the related conduct was being engaged in, or\nwould be engaged in, by a participant in an operation authorised\nunder a corresponding State controlled operations law.\n\n(3) Expressions used in this section have the same meanings as in the\ncorresponding State controlled operations law under which the\nperson believed the controlled conduct was being engaged in.",
      "cml:hasPart": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:crimes-legislation-amendment-serious-and-organised-crime-act-2010-sch-3-sec-15hj-ss-1"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:crimes-legislation-amendment-serious-and-organised-crime-act-2010-sch-3-sec-15hj-ss-2"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:crimes-legislation-amendment-serious-and-organised-crime-act-2010-sch-3-sec-15hj-ss-3"
        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "85ca6d6d291c070dbcb28efa667bbed81c9c789b5bb515725a7bad753f6171ba"
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/crimes-legislation-amendment-serious-and-organised-crime-act-2010#sch-3-sec-15hj",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "15HJ Protection from criminal responsibility for certain ancillary",
      "values:kind": "section",
      "cof:pageNumber": 94,
      "values:originalText": "conduct\n\n(1) This section applies if:\n\n(a) a person engages in conduct (the ancillary conduct) that\nrelates to conduct (the related conduct) that:\n\n(i) was engaged in by another person; and\n\n(ii) constitutes an offence for which a person would, but for\nsection 15HH, be criminally responsible; and\n\n(b) engaging in the ancillary conduct is an ancillary offence\n(within the meaning of the Criminal Code) in relation to the\noffence constituted by the related conduct.\n\n(2) Despite any law of the Commonwealth, the person who engaged in\nthe ancillary conduct is not criminally responsible for the ancillary\noffence if, at the time the person engaged in the ancillary conduct,\nhe or she believed the related conduct was being engaged in, or\nwould be engaged in, by a participant in an operation authorised\nunder a corresponding State controlled operations law.\n\n(3) Expressions used in this section have the same meanings as in the\ncorresponding State controlled operations law under which the\nperson believed the controlled conduct was being engaged in."
    },
