    {
      "@id": "concept:crimes-legislation-amendment-serious-and-organised-crime-act-2010-sch-3-sec-15hl",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "15HL Unauthorised disclosure of information—endangering safety,",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/crimes-legislation-amendment-serious-and-organised-crime-act-2010#sch-3-sec-15hl"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "crimes-legislation-amendment-serious-and-organised-crime-act-2010.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "crimes-legislation-amendment-serious-and-organised-crime-act-2010.pdf, p.95",
      "values:originalText": "etc.\n\n(1) A person commits an offence if:\n\n(a) the person discloses information; and\n\n(b) the information relates to a controlled operation; and\n\n(c) either:\nComLaw Authoritative Act C2012C00115\n\nSchedule 3  Amendments relating to controlled operations, assumed identities and\nwitness identity protection",
      "skos:definition": "etc.\n\n(1) A person commits an offence if:\n\n(a) the person discloses information; and\n\n(b) the information relates to a controlled operation; and\n\n(c) either:\nComLaw Authoritative Act C2012C00115\n\nSchedule 3  Amendments relating to controlled operations, assumed identities and\nwitness identity protection",
      "cml:asserts": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:crimes-legislation-amendment-serious-and-organised-crime-act-2010-sch-3-sec-15hl-norm"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:crimes-legislation-amendment-serious-and-organised-crime-act-2010-sch-3-sec-15hl-logic-deontic-1"
        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "e7b8182f68122d95244ef4fbe95f004537f077466e130b1286e6f802641bee40",
      "skos:note": "Unauthorised disclosure of information—endangering safety"
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/crimes-legislation-amendment-serious-and-organised-crime-act-2010#sch-3-sec-15hl",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "15HL Unauthorised disclosure of information—endangering safety,",
      "values:kind": "section",
      "cof:pageNumber": 95,
      "values:originalText": "etc.\n\n(1) A person commits an offence if:\n\n(a) the person discloses information; and\n\n(b) the information relates to a controlled operation; and\n\n(c) either:\nComLaw Authoritative Act C2012C00115\n\nSchedule 3  Amendments relating to controlled operations, assumed identities and\nwitness identity protection"
    },
    {
      "@id": "concept:crimes-legislation-amendment-serious-and-organised-crime-act-2010-sch-3-sec-15hl-norm",
      "@type": "values:Prohibition",
      "cml:modality": {
        "@id": "cml:Deontic"
      },
      "values:partOf": {
        "@id": "concept:crimes-legislation-amendment-serious-and-organised-crime-act-2010-sch-3-sec-15hl"
      },
      "values:deonticStatus": {
        "@id": "values:HeuristicDerived"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "values:borneBy": {
        "@id": "values:State"
      },
      "skos:scopeNote": "borne by: State"
    },
    {
      "@id": "concept:crimes-legislation-amendment-serious-and-organised-crime-act-2010-sch-3-sec-15hl-logic-deontic-1",
      "@type": "cml:LogicApplication",
      "cml:modality": {
        "@id": "cml:Deontic"
      },
      "cml:operator": "Prohibit",
      "cml:logicSummary": "Prohibits disclosure of information endangering safety",
      "cml:executionSurface": "modalities::logic::deontic",
      "cml:confidence": {
        "@value": 1.0,
        "@type": "xsd:decimal"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:premiseText": "Disclosing information relating to a controlled operation",
      "cml:conclusionText": "Offence committed"
    },
    {
      "@id": "concept:crimes-legislation-amendment-serious-and-organised-crime-act-2010-sch-3-sec-92",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "92 Crimes Legislation Amendment (Serious and Organised Crime) Act",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/crimes-legislation-amendment-serious-and-organised-crime-act-2010#sch-3-sec-92"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "crimes-legislation-amendment-serious-and-organised-crime-act-2010.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "crimes-legislation-amendment-serious-and-organised-crime-act-2010.pdf, p.96",
      "values:originalText": "(i) the person intends to endanger the health or safety of\nany person or prejudice the effective conduct of a\ncontrolled operation; or\n\n(ii) the disclosure of the information will endanger the\nhealth or safety of any person or prejudice the effective\nconduct of a controlled operation.\nPenalty: Imprisonment for 10 years.\n\n(2) Subsection (1) does not apply if the disclosure was:\n\n(a) in connection with the administration or execution of this\nPart; or\n\n(b) for the purposes of any legal proceedings arising out of or\notherwise related to this Part or of any report of any such\nproceedings; or\n\n(c) for the purposes of obtaining legal advice in relation to the\ncontrolled operation; or\n\n(d) in accordance with any requirement imposed by law; or\n\n(e) in connection with the performance of functions or duties, or\nthe exercise of powers, of a law enforcement agency.\n\n(3) Subsection (1) does not apply if:\n\n(a) the person (the discloser) discloses the information to the\nOmbudsman or the Integrity Commissioner; and\n\n(b) the discloser informs the person to whom the disclosure is\nmade of the discloser’s identity before making the disclosure;\nand\n\n(c) the information concerns misconduct in relation to a\ncontrolled operation; and\n\n(d) the discloser considers that the information may assist a\nperson referred to in paragraph (a) to perform the person’s\nfunctions or duties; and\n\n(e) the discloser makes the disclosure in good faith.\nNote:\nA defendant bears an evidential burden in relation to the matters in\nsubsections (2) and (3)—see subsection 13.3(3) of the Criminal Code.\n\n(4) An offence against this section is an indictable offence.\nComLaw Authoritative Act C2012C00115\n\nAmendments relating to controlled operations, assumed identities and witness identity\nprotection  Schedule 3\nMain amendments  Part 1\n\nCrimes Legislation Amendment (Serious and Organised Crime) Act 2010",
      "skos:definition": "(i) the person intends to endanger the health or safety of\nany person or prejudice the effective conduct of a\ncontrolled operation; or\n\n(ii) the disclosure of the information will endanger the\nhealth or safety of any person or prejudice the effective\nconduct of a controlled operation.\nPenalty: Imprisonment for 10 years.\n\n(2) Subsection (1) does not apply if the disclosure was:\n\n(a) in connection with the administration or execution of this\nPart; or\n\n(b) for the purposes of any legal proceedings arising out of or\notherwise related to this Part or of any report of any such\nproceedings; or\n\n(c) for the purposes of obtaining legal advice in relation to the\ncontrolled operation; or\n\n(d) in accordance with any requirement imposed by law; or\n\n(e) in connection with the performance of functions or duties, or\nthe exercise of powers, of a law enforcement agency.\n\n(3) Subsection (1) does not apply if:\n\n(a) the person (the discloser) discloses the information to the\nOmbudsman or the Integrity Commissioner; and\n\n(b) the discloser informs the person to whom the disclosure is\nmade of the discloser’s identity before making the disclosure;\nand\n\n(c) the information concerns misconduct in relation to a\ncontrolled operation; and\n\n(d) the discloser considers that the information may assist a\nperson referred to in paragraph (a) to perform the person’s\nfunctions or duties; and\n\n(e) the discloser makes the disclosure in good faith.\nNote:\nA defendant bears an evidential burden in relation to the matters in\nsubsections (2) and (3)—see subsection 13.3(3) of the Criminal Code.\n\n(4) An offence against this section is an indictable offence.\nComLaw Authoritative Act C2012C00115\n\nAmendments relating to controlled operations, assumed identities and witness identity\nprotection  Schedule 3\nMain amendments  Part 1\n\nCrimes Legislation Amendment (Serious and Organised Crime) Act 2010",
      "cml:hasPart": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:crimes-legislation-amendment-serious-and-organised-crime-act-2010-sch-3-sec-92-ss-2"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:crimes-legislation-amendment-serious-and-organised-crime-act-2010-sch-3-sec-92-ss-3"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:crimes-legislation-amendment-serious-and-organised-crime-act-2010-sch-3-sec-92-ss-4"
        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "8d0b74dbc66ffc2a11fd0162cf7e64ffce1126834bedccef7e18743d91064ed7"
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/crimes-legislation-amendment-serious-and-organised-crime-act-2010#sch-3-sec-92",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "92 Crimes Legislation Amendment (Serious and Organised Crime) Act",
      "values:kind": "section",
      "cof:pageNumber": 96,
      "values:originalText": "(i) the person intends to endanger the health or safety of\nany person or prejudice the effective conduct of a\ncontrolled operation; or\n\n(ii) the disclosure of the information will endanger the\nhealth or safety of any person or prejudice the effective\nconduct of a controlled operation.\nPenalty: Imprisonment for 10 years.\n\n(2) Subsection (1) does not apply if the disclosure was:\n\n(a) in connection with the administration or execution of this\nPart; or\n\n(b) for the purposes of any legal proceedings arising out of or\notherwise related to this Part or of any report of any such\nproceedings; or\n\n(c) for the purposes of obtaining legal advice in relation to the\ncontrolled operation; or\n\n(d) in accordance with any requirement imposed by law; or\n\n(e) in connection with the performance of functions or duties, or\nthe exercise of powers, of a law enforcement agency.\n\n(3) Subsection (1) does not apply if:\n\n(a) the person (the discloser) discloses the information to the\nOmbudsman or the Integrity Commissioner; and\n\n(b) the discloser informs the person to whom the disclosure is\nmade of the discloser’s identity before making the disclosure;\nand\n\n(c) the information concerns misconduct in relation to a\ncontrolled operation; and\n\n(d) the discloser considers that the information may assist a\nperson referred to in paragraph (a) to perform the person’s\nfunctions or duties; and\n\n(e) the discloser makes the disclosure in good faith.\nNote:\nA defendant bears an evidential burden in relation to the matters in\nsubsections (2) and (3)—see subsection 13.3(3) of the Criminal Code.\n\n(4) An offence against this section is an indictable offence.\nComLaw Authoritative Act C2012C00115\n\nAmendments relating to controlled operations, assumed identities and witness identity\nprotection  Schedule 3\nMain amendments  Part 1\n\nCrimes Legislation Amendment (Serious and Organised Crime) Act 2010"
    },
