    {
      "@id": "concept:crimes-legislation-amendment-serious-and-organised-crime-act-2010-sch-3-sec-96",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "96 Crimes Legislation Amendment (Serious and Organised Crime) Act",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/crimes-legislation-amendment-serious-and-organised-crime-act-2010#sch-3-sec-96"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "crimes-legislation-amendment-serious-and-organised-crime-act-2010.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "crimes-legislation-amendment-serious-and-organised-crime-act-2010.pdf, p.100",
      "values:originalText": "(c) by an assumed name under which the person is operating; or\n\n(d) by a code name or code number;\nas long as the chief officer can match the assumed name, code\nname or code number to the person’s identity.\n\n(3) The Ombudsman may require the chief officer of an authorising\nagency to give additional information covering any controlled\noperation to which a report relates.\n\n(4) Nothing in paragraphs (2)(o) to (t) requires particulars of a\ncontrolled operation to be included in a report for a period of 6\nmonths if the operation had not been completed during that period,\nbut the particulars must instead be included in the report for the\nperiod of 6 months in which the operation is completed.\n\n(5) A copy of a report given to the Ombudsman under this section\nmust be given to the Minister at the same time as it is given to the\nOmbudsman.",
      "skos:definition": "(c) by an assumed name under which the person is operating; or\n\n(d) by a code name or code number;\nas long as the chief officer can match the assumed name, code\nname or code number to the person’s identity.\n\n(3) The Ombudsman may require the chief officer of an authorising\nagency to give additional information covering any controlled\noperation to which a report relates.\n\n(4) Nothing in paragraphs (2)(o) to (t) requires particulars of a\ncontrolled operation to be included in a report for a period of 6\nmonths if the operation had not been completed during that period,\nbut the particulars must instead be included in the report for the\nperiod of 6 months in which the operation is completed.\n\n(5) A copy of a report given to the Ombudsman under this section\nmust be given to the Minister at the same time as it is given to the\nOmbudsman.",
      "cml:hasPart": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:crimes-legislation-amendment-serious-and-organised-crime-act-2010-sch-3-sec-96-ss-3"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:crimes-legislation-amendment-serious-and-organised-crime-act-2010-sch-3-sec-96-ss-4"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:crimes-legislation-amendment-serious-and-organised-crime-act-2010-sch-3-sec-96-ss-5"
        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "349377dc3bfddb7638c4b71f62d594ef8eded89f5a7ba18f7d87360c19177c3e"
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/crimes-legislation-amendment-serious-and-organised-crime-act-2010#sch-3-sec-96",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "96 Crimes Legislation Amendment (Serious and Organised Crime) Act",
      "values:kind": "section",
      "cof:pageNumber": 100,
      "values:originalText": "(c) by an assumed name under which the person is operating; or\n\n(d) by a code name or code number;\nas long as the chief officer can match the assumed name, code\nname or code number to the person’s identity.\n\n(3) The Ombudsman may require the chief officer of an authorising\nagency to give additional information covering any controlled\noperation to which a report relates.\n\n(4) Nothing in paragraphs (2)(o) to (t) requires particulars of a\ncontrolled operation to be included in a report for a period of 6\nmonths if the operation had not been completed during that period,\nbut the particulars must instead be included in the report for the\nperiod of 6 months in which the operation is completed.\n\n(5) A copy of a report given to the Ombudsman under this section\nmust be given to the Minister at the same time as it is given to the\nOmbudsman."
    },
