      "dc:source": "crimes-legislation-amendment-serious-and-organised-crime-act-2010.pdf, p.101",
      "values:originalText": "(2) A report under this section must not include information which, if\nmade public, could reasonably be expected to:\n\n(a) endanger a person’s safety; or\n\n(b) prejudice an investigation or prosecution; or\nComLaw Authoritative Act C2012C00115\n\nSchedule 3  Amendments relating to controlled operations, assumed identities and\nwitness identity protection",
      "skos:definition": "(2) A report under this section must not include information which, if\nmade public, could reasonably be expected to:\n\n(a) endanger a person’s safety; or\n\n(b) prejudice an investigation or prosecution; or\nComLaw Authoritative Act C2012C00115\n\nSchedule 3  Amendments relating to controlled operations, assumed identities and\nwitness identity protection",
