      }
    },
    {
      "@id": "concept:crimes-legislation-amendment-serious-and-organised-crime-act-2010-sch-3-sec-15hq",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "15HQ General register",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/crimes-legislation-amendment-serious-and-organised-crime-act-2010#sch-3-sec-15hq"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "crimes-legislation-amendment-serious-and-organised-crime-act-2010.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "crimes-legislation-amendment-serious-and-organised-crime-act-2010.pdf, p.103",
      "values:originalText": "(1) The chief officer of each authorising agency must cause a general\nregister to be kept.\n\n(2) The general register is to specify:\n\n(a) for each application under this Part made to an authorising\nofficer of the agency (including an application for a variation\nof an authority):\n\n(i) the date of the application; and\n\n(ii) whether the application was formal or urgent; and\n\n(iii) whether the application was granted, refused or\nwithdrawn; and\n\n(iv) if the application was refused or withdrawn—the date\nand time of the refusal or withdrawal; and\n\n(b) for each authority under this Part granted by an authorising\nofficer of the agency:\n\n(i) the date and time the authority was granted; and\n\n(ii) whether the authority was formal or urgent; and\n\n(iii) the name and rank or position of the person who granted\nthe authority; and\n\n(iv) each serious Commonwealth offence or serious State\noffence that has a federal aspect in respect of which\ncontrolled conduct under the authority was to be\nengaged in; and\n\n(v) the period of effect of the authority; and\nComLaw Authoritative Act C2012C00115\n\nSchedule 3  Amendments relating to controlled operations, assumed identities and\nwitness identity protection",
      "skos:definition": "(1) The chief officer of each authorising agency must cause a general\nregister to be kept.\n\n(2) The general register is to specify:\n\n(a) for each application under this Part made to an authorising\nofficer of the agency (including an application for a variation\nof an authority):\n\n(i) the date of the application; and\n\n(ii) whether the application was formal or urgent; and\n\n(iii) whether the application was granted, refused or\nwithdrawn; and\n\n(iv) if the application was refused or withdrawn—the date\nand time of the refusal or withdrawal; and\n\n(b) for each authority under this Part granted by an authorising\nofficer of the agency:\n\n(i) the date and time the authority was granted; and\n\n(ii) whether the authority was formal or urgent; and\n\n(iii) the name and rank or position of the person who granted\nthe authority; and\n\n(iv) each serious Commonwealth offence or serious State\noffence that has a federal aspect in respect of which\ncontrolled conduct under the authority was to be\nengaged in; and\n\n(v) the period of effect of the authority; and\nComLaw Authoritative Act C2012C00115\n\nSchedule 3  Amendments relating to controlled operations, assumed identities and\nwitness identity protection",
      "cml:hasPart": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:crimes-legislation-amendment-serious-and-organised-crime-act-2010-sch-3-sec-15hq-ss-1"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:crimes-legislation-amendment-serious-and-organised-crime-act-2010-sch-3-sec-15hq-ss-2"
        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "429d3369c2a69bd9ae7a5042cafe22a069e39ff8f6fe1c1dbbcbe598e6b1ac2d"
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/crimes-legislation-amendment-serious-and-organised-crime-act-2010#sch-3-sec-15hq",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "15HQ General register",
      "values:kind": "section",
      "cof:pageNumber": 103,
      "values:originalText": "(1) The chief officer of each authorising agency must cause a general\nregister to be kept.\n\n(2) The general register is to specify:\n\n(a) for each application under this Part made to an authorising\nofficer of the agency (including an application for a variation\nof an authority):\n\n(i) the date of the application; and\n\n(ii) whether the application was formal or urgent; and\n\n(iii) whether the application was granted, refused or\nwithdrawn; and\n\n(iv) if the application was refused or withdrawn—the date\nand time of the refusal or withdrawal; and\n\n(b) for each authority under this Part granted by an authorising\nofficer of the agency:\n\n(i) the date and time the authority was granted; and\n\n(ii) whether the authority was formal or urgent; and\n\n(iii) the name and rank or position of the person who granted\nthe authority; and\n\n(iv) each serious Commonwealth offence or serious State\noffence that has a federal aspect in respect of which\ncontrolled conduct under the authority was to be\nengaged in; and\n\n(v) the period of effect of the authority; and\nComLaw Authoritative Act C2012C00115\n\nSchedule 3  Amendments relating to controlled operations, assumed identities and\nwitness identity protection"
    },
