      }
    },
    {
      "@id": "concept:crimes-legislation-amendment-serious-and-organised-crime-act-2010-sch-3-sec-100-ss-2c",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "100(2C) Crimes Legislation Amendment (Serious and Organised Crime) Act",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/crimes-legislation-amendment-serious-and-organised-crime-act-2010#sch-3-sec-100-ss-2c"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "crimes-legislation-amendment-serious-and-organised-crime-act-2010.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "crimes-legislation-amendment-serious-and-organised-crime-act-2010.pdf, p.104",
      "values:originalText": "(2C) If the chief officer of the authorising agency is of the view that\ndisclosing the identity of a person may:\n\n(a) endanger the safety of the person; or\n\n(b) prejudice an investigation or prosecution;\nthen the person is sufficiently identified for the purposes of\nparagraphs (2A)(b) and (2B)(b) if the person is identified:\n\n(c) by an assumed name under which the person is operating; or\n\n(d) by a code name or code number;\nas long as the chief officer can match the assumed name, code\nname or code number to the person’s identity.",
      "skos:definition": "(2C) If the chief officer of the authorising agency is of the view that\ndisclosing the identity of a person may:\n\n(a) endanger the safety of the person; or\n\n(b) prejudice an investigation or prosecution;\nthen the person is sufficiently identified for the purposes of\nparagraphs (2A)(b) and (2B)(b) if the person is identified:\n\n(c) by an assumed name under which the person is operating; or\n\n(d) by a code name or code number;\nas long as the chief officer can match the assumed name, code\nname or code number to the person’s identity.",
      "values:partOf": {
        "@id": "concept:crimes-legislation-amendment-serious-and-organised-crime-act-2010-sch-3-sec-100"
      },
      "cml:asserts": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:crimes-legislation-amendment-serious-and-organised-crime-act-2010-sch-3-sec-100-ss-2c-norm"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:crimes-legislation-amendment-serious-and-organised-crime-act-2010-sch-3-sec-100-ss-2c-logic-deontic-1"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:crimes-legislation-amendment-serious-and-organised-crime-act-2010-sch-3-sec-100-ss-2c-logic-alleninterval-2"
        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "3fa84461d41c1e1bc1b8fe7ef1e93323e1c1295a291d5bb9a603abcc073d428d",
      "skos:note": "Identifying a person by assumed name or code is permitted if it can be matched to the person's identity."
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/crimes-legislation-amendment-serious-and-organised-crime-act-2010#sch-3-sec-100-ss-2c",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "100(2C) Crimes Legislation Amendment (Serious and Organised Crime) Act",
      "values:kind": "subsection",
      "cof:pageNumber": 104,
      "values:originalText": "(2C) If the chief officer of the authorising agency is of the view that\ndisclosing the identity of a person may:\n\n(a) endanger the safety of the person; or\n\n(b) prejudice an investigation or prosecution;\nthen the person is sufficiently identified for the purposes of\nparagraphs (2A)(b) and (2B)(b) if the person is identified:\n\n(c) by an assumed name under which the person is operating; or\n\n(d) by a code name or code number;\nas long as the chief officer can match the assumed name, code\nname or code number to the person’s identity."
    },
