          "@id": "concept:crimes-legislation-amendment-serious-and-organised-crime-act-2010-sch-3-sec-15hs-ss-3-logic-deontic-2"
        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "9cff62b31373fc2bd37dacfae7f9f331d7e95b67bc273e0c4c74cdc30cdd9b4c",
      "skos:note": "Ombudsman may enter premises, access records, and require staff information."
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/crimes-legislation-amendment-serious-and-organised-crime-act-2010#sch-3-sec-15hs-ss-3",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "15HS(3) Inspection of records by the Ombudsman",
      "values:kind": "subsection",
      "cof:pageNumber": 106,
      "values:originalText": "(3) For the purpose of an inspection under this section, the\nOmbudsman:\n\n(a) may, after notifying the chief officer of the agency, enter at\nany reasonable time premises occupied by the agency; and\n\n(b) is entitled to have full and free access at all reasonable times\nto all records of the agency that are relevant to the inspection;\nand\n\n(c) may require a member of staff of the agency to give the\nOmbudsman any information that the Ombudsman considers\nnecessary, being information that is in the member’s\npossession, or to which the member has access, and that is\nrelevant to the inspection; and\n\n(d) may, despite any other law, make copies of, and take extracts\nfrom, records of the agency."
    },
