    {
      "@id": "concept:crimes-legislation-amendment-serious-and-organised-crime-act-2010-sch-3-sec-15hw",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "15HW Exchange of information between Ombudsman and State",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/crimes-legislation-amendment-serious-and-organised-crime-act-2010#sch-3-sec-15hw"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "crimes-legislation-amendment-serious-and-organised-crime-act-2010.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "crimes-legislation-amendment-serious-and-organised-crime-act-2010.pdf, p.109",
      "values:originalText": "inspecting authorities\n\n(1) In this section:\nState or Territory agency means a law enforcement agency of a\nState or Territory within the meaning of a corresponding State\ncontrolled operations law.\nState or Territory inspecting authority, in relation to a State or\nTerritory agency, means the authority that, under the law of the\nState or Territory concerned, has the function of making\ninspections of a similar kind to those provided for in section 15HS\nwhen the State or Territory agency is exercising powers under a\ncorresponding State controlled operations law.\n\n(2) The Ombudsman may give information that:\n\n(a) relates to a State or Territory agency; and\nComLaw Authoritative Act C2012C00115\n\nSchedule 3  Amendments relating to controlled operations, assumed identities and\nwitness identity protection",
      "skos:definition": "inspecting authorities\n\n(1) In this section:\nState or Territory agency means a law enforcement agency of a\nState or Territory within the meaning of a corresponding State\ncontrolled operations law.\nState or Territory inspecting authority, in relation to a State or\nTerritory agency, means the authority that, under the law of the\nState or Territory concerned, has the function of making\ninspections of a similar kind to those provided for in section 15HS\nwhen the State or Territory agency is exercising powers under a\ncorresponding State controlled operations law.\n\n(2) The Ombudsman may give information that:\n\n(a) relates to a State or Territory agency; and\nComLaw Authoritative Act C2012C00115\n\nSchedule 3  Amendments relating to controlled operations, assumed identities and\nwitness identity protection",
      "cml:hasPart": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:crimes-legislation-amendment-serious-and-organised-crime-act-2010-sch-3-sec-15hw-ss-1"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:crimes-legislation-amendment-serious-and-organised-crime-act-2010-sch-3-sec-15hw-ss-2"
        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "516548d0cfde581deae940307cc8454dbb916b4cc2940cc91b4c9f8de1a1586b"
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/crimes-legislation-amendment-serious-and-organised-crime-act-2010#sch-3-sec-15hw",
