    {
      "@id": "concept:crimes-legislation-amendment-serious-and-organised-crime-act-2010-sch-3-sec-106",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "106 Crimes Legislation Amendment (Serious and Organised Crime) Act",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/crimes-legislation-amendment-serious-and-organised-crime-act-2010#sch-3-sec-106"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "crimes-legislation-amendment-serious-and-organised-crime-act-2010.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "crimes-legislation-amendment-serious-and-organised-crime-act-2010.pdf, p.110",
      "values:originalText": "(b) was obtained by the Ombudsman under this Division;\nto the State or Territory inspecting authority in relation to the\nagency.\n\n(3) The Ombudsman may only give information to an authority under\nsubsection (2) if the Ombudsman is satisfied that the giving of the\ninformation is necessary to enable the authority to perform its\nfunctions in relation to the State or Territory agency.\n\n(4) The Ombudsman may receive from a State or Territory inspecting\nauthority information relevant to the performance of the\nOmbudsman’s functions under this Division.",
      "skos:definition": "(b) was obtained by the Ombudsman under this Division;\nto the State or Territory inspecting authority in relation to the\nagency.\n\n(3) The Ombudsman may only give information to an authority under\nsubsection (2) if the Ombudsman is satisfied that the giving of the\ninformation is necessary to enable the authority to perform its\nfunctions in relation to the State or Territory agency.\n\n(4) The Ombudsman may receive from a State or Territory inspecting\nauthority information relevant to the performance of the\nOmbudsman’s functions under this Division.",
      "cml:hasPart": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:crimes-legislation-amendment-serious-and-organised-crime-act-2010-sch-3-sec-106-ss-3"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:crimes-legislation-amendment-serious-and-organised-crime-act-2010-sch-3-sec-106-ss-4"
        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "4ef117611984d9d6a30d08afc9f14e1d6f9a13332c3d3fbb00b279e28ec17078"
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/crimes-legislation-amendment-serious-and-organised-crime-act-2010#sch-3-sec-106",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "106 Crimes Legislation Amendment (Serious and Organised Crime) Act",
      "values:kind": "section",
      "cof:pageNumber": 110,
      "values:originalText": "(b) was obtained by the Ombudsman under this Division;\nto the State or Territory inspecting authority in relation to the\nagency.\n\n(3) The Ombudsman may only give information to an authority under\nsubsection (2) if the Ombudsman is satisfied that the giving of the\ninformation is necessary to enable the authority to perform its\nfunctions in relation to the State or Territory agency.\n\n(4) The Ombudsman may receive from a State or Territory inspecting\nauthority information relevant to the performance of the\nOmbudsman’s functions under this Division."
    },
    {
      "@id": "concept:crimes-legislation-amendment-serious-and-organised-crime-act-2010-sch-3-sec-106-ss-3",
