      }
    },
    {
      "@id": "concept:crimes-legislation-amendment-serious-and-organised-crime-act-2010-sch-3-sec-15ka-ss-5",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "15KA(5) Application for authority to acquire or use assumed identity",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/crimes-legislation-amendment-serious-and-organised-crime-act-2010#sch-3-sec-15ka-ss-5"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "crimes-legislation-amendment-serious-and-organised-crime-act-2010.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "crimes-legislation-amendment-serious-and-organised-crime-act-2010.pdf, p.116",
      "values:originalText": "(5) An application:\n\n(a) must be in writing in the form approved by the chief officer;\nand\n\n(b) must contain:\n\n(i) the name of the applicant; and\n\n(ii) the name of the person to be authorised to acquire or use\nan assumed identity (if not the applicant); and\n\n(iii) if the person referred to in subparagraph (ii) is not an\nofficer of either an intelligence agency or a law\nenforcement agency or a foreign officer—the name and\nrank or position of the person proposed to be appointed\nas supervisor and an explanation of why it is necessary\nfor a person who is not an officer to acquire or use the\nassumed identity; and\n\n(iv) details of the proposed assumed identity; and\n\n(v) reasons for the need to acquire or use an assumed\nidentity; and\n\n(vi) if the assumed identity is necessary for a purpose\nmentioned in subparagraph 15KB(2)(a)(i) or (ii)—\ndetails of the investigation or intelligence-gathering\nexercise in which the assumed identity will be used (to\nthe extent known); and\n\n(vii) details of any issuing agencies and the types of evidence\nto be issued by them; and\n\n(viii) details of any application of a kind referred to in\nsection 15KG (making entries in register of births,\ndeaths or marriages) that is to be made under a\ncorresponding assumed identity law.\nComLaw Authoritative Act C2012C00115\n\nSchedule 3  Amendments relating to controlled operations, assumed identities and\nwitness identity protection",
      "skos:definition": "(5) An application:\n\n(a) must be in writing in the form approved by the chief officer;\nand\n\n(b) must contain:\n\n(i) the name of the applicant; and\n\n(ii) the name of the person to be authorised to acquire or use\nan assumed identity (if not the applicant); and\n\n(iii) if the person referred to in subparagraph (ii) is not an\nofficer of either an intelligence agency or a law\nenforcement agency or a foreign officer—the name and\nrank or position of the person proposed to be appointed\nas supervisor and an explanation of why it is necessary\nfor a person who is not an officer to acquire or use the\nassumed identity; and\n\n(iv) details of the proposed assumed identity; and\n\n(v) reasons for the need to acquire or use an assumed\nidentity; and\n\n(vi) if the assumed identity is necessary for a purpose\nmentioned in subparagraph 15KB(2)(a)(i) or (ii)—\ndetails of the investigation or intelligence-gathering\nexercise in which the assumed identity will be used (to\nthe extent known); and\n\n(vii) details of any issuing agencies and the types of evidence\nto be issued by them; and\n\n(viii) details of any application of a kind referred to in\nsection 15KG (making entries in register of births,\ndeaths or marriages) that is to be made under a\ncorresponding assumed identity law.\nComLaw Authoritative Act C2012C00115\n\nSchedule 3  Amendments relating to controlled operations, assumed identities and\nwitness identity protection",
      "values:partOf": {
        "@id": "concept:crimes-legislation-amendment-serious-and-organised-crime-act-2010-sch-3-sec-15ka"
      },
      "cml:asserts": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:crimes-legislation-amendment-serious-and-organised-crime-act-2010-sch-3-sec-15ka-ss-5-norm"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:crimes-legislation-amendment-serious-and-organised-crime-act-2010-sch-3-sec-15ka-ss-5-logic-deontic-1"
        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "8aec59c5bf25d6785d452f1be4cae2a7e663fc462f66d6a93de35f8815124329",
      "skos:note": "Application for authority to acquire or use assumed identity must be in writing and contain specific information.",
      "dc:description": "yes"
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/crimes-legislation-amendment-serious-and-organised-crime-act-2010#sch-3-sec-15ka-ss-5",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "15KA(5) Application for authority to acquire or use assumed identity",
      "values:kind": "subsection",
      "cof:pageNumber": 116,
      "values:originalText": "(5) An application:\n\n(a) must be in writing in the form approved by the chief officer;\nand\n\n(b) must contain:\n\n(i) the name of the applicant; and\n\n(ii) the name of the person to be authorised to acquire or use\nan assumed identity (if not the applicant); and\n\n(iii) if the person referred to in subparagraph (ii) is not an\nofficer of either an intelligence agency or a law\nenforcement agency or a foreign officer—the name and\nrank or position of the person proposed to be appointed\nas supervisor and an explanation of why it is necessary\nfor a person who is not an officer to acquire or use the\nassumed identity; and\n\n(iv) details of the proposed assumed identity; and\n\n(v) reasons for the need to acquire or use an assumed\nidentity; and\n\n(vi) if the assumed identity is necessary for a purpose\nmentioned in subparagraph 15KB(2)(a)(i) or (ii)—\ndetails of the investigation or intelligence-gathering\nexercise in which the assumed identity will be used (to\nthe extent known); and\n\n(vii) details of any issuing agencies and the types of evidence\nto be issued by them; and\n\n(viii) details of any application of a kind referred to in\nsection 15KG (making entries in register of births,\ndeaths or marriages) that is to be made under a\ncorresponding assumed identity law.\nComLaw Authoritative Act C2012C00115\n\nSchedule 3  Amendments relating to controlled operations, assumed identities and\nwitness identity protection"
    },
    {
