          "@id": "concept:crimes-legislation-amendment-serious-and-organised-crime-act-2010-sch-3-sec-15kb-ss-5-logic-deontic-1"
        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "6c185a7254cded9266920edfa8e22b3a451b7a6bcd1f2fe11d9374c230486ddc",
      "skos:note": "Authorise applications for assumed identities"
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/crimes-legislation-amendment-serious-and-organised-crime-act-2010#sch-3-sec-15kb-ss-5",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "15KB(5) Determination of applications",
      "values:kind": "subsection",
      "cof:pageNumber": 118,
      "values:originalText": "(5) An authority may also authorise any one or more of the following:\n\n(a) an application of a kind referred to in section 15KG for an\norder for an entry in a register of births, deaths or marriages\nunder a corresponding assumed identity law;\n\n(b) a request under section 15KI or 15KX;\n\n(c) the use of an assumed identity in a foreign country.\nComLaw Authoritative Act C2012C00115\n\nSchedule 3  Amendments relating to controlled operations, assumed identities and\nwitness identity protection"
    },
