    {
      "@id": "concept:crimes-legislation-amendment-serious-and-organised-crime-act-2010-sch-3-sec-116",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "116 Crimes Legislation Amendment (Serious and Organised Crime) Act",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/crimes-legislation-amendment-serious-and-organised-crime-act-2010#sch-3-sec-116"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "crimes-legislation-amendment-serious-and-organised-crime-act-2010.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "crimes-legislation-amendment-serious-and-organised-crime-act-2010.pdf, p.120",
      "values:originalText": "(6) However, the chief officer of the ACC, the chief officer of the\nAustralian Federal Police or the chief officer of an intelligence\nagency may only authorise the use of the assumed identity in a\nforeign country if he or she is satisfied that it is reasonably\nnecessary to do so.\nNote:\nThis subsection does not affect any obligation to obtain authority to\nuse the assumed identity in the foreign country.\n\n(7) A separate authority is required for each assumed identity.\nNote:\nThe chief officer may delegate functions under this section—see\nsection 15LH.\n\n(8) An authority is not a legislative instrument.",
      "skos:definition": "(6) However, the chief officer of the ACC, the chief officer of the\nAustralian Federal Police or the chief officer of an intelligence\nagency may only authorise the use of the assumed identity in a\nforeign country if he or she is satisfied that it is reasonably\nnecessary to do so.\nNote:\nThis subsection does not affect any obligation to obtain authority to\nuse the assumed identity in the foreign country.\n\n(7) A separate authority is required for each assumed identity.\nNote:\nThe chief officer may delegate functions under this section—see\nsection 15LH.\n\n(8) An authority is not a legislative instrument.",
      "cml:hasPart": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:crimes-legislation-amendment-serious-and-organised-crime-act-2010-sch-3-sec-116-ss-6"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:crimes-legislation-amendment-serious-and-organised-crime-act-2010-sch-3-sec-116-ss-7"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:crimes-legislation-amendment-serious-and-organised-crime-act-2010-sch-3-sec-116-ss-8"
        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "461e28a04d405137d671e9141f36c0f1d8a00e482b05911b0a3e7fab7f2a5e1e"
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/crimes-legislation-amendment-serious-and-organised-crime-act-2010#sch-3-sec-116",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "116 Crimes Legislation Amendment (Serious and Organised Crime) Act",
      "values:kind": "section",
      "cof:pageNumber": 120,
      "values:originalText": "(6) However, the chief officer of the ACC, the chief officer of the\nAustralian Federal Police or the chief officer of an intelligence\nagency may only authorise the use of the assumed identity in a\nforeign country if he or she is satisfied that it is reasonably\nnecessary to do so.\nNote:\nThis subsection does not affect any obligation to obtain authority to\nuse the assumed identity in the foreign country.\n\n(7) A separate authority is required for each assumed identity.\nNote:\nThe chief officer may delegate functions under this section—see\nsection 15LH.\n\n(8) An authority is not a legislative instrument."
    },
    {
