    {
      "@id": "concept:crimes-legislation-amendment-serious-and-organised-crime-act-2010-sch-3-sec-15kc",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "15KC Form of authority",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/crimes-legislation-amendment-serious-and-organised-crime-act-2010#sch-3-sec-15kc"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "crimes-legislation-amendment-serious-and-organised-crime-act-2010.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "crimes-legislation-amendment-serious-and-organised-crime-act-2010.pdf, p.120",
      "values:originalText": "(1) An authority must be:\n\n(a) in writing in the form approved by the chief officer; and\n\n(b) signed by the person granting it.\n\n(2) An authority must state the following:\n\n(a) the name of the person granting the authority;\n\n(b) the date of the authority;\n\n(c) details of the assumed identity authorised;\n\n(d) details of any evidence of the assumed identity that may be\nacquired under the authority;\n\n(e) the conditions (if any) to which the authority is subject;\n\n(f) why the authority is granted;\n\n(g) if the authority relates to an authorised intelligence officer, an\nauthorised law enforcement officer or a foreign officer—the\nname of the officer;\n\n(h) if the authority relates to an authorised civilian whose\nsupervisor is a law enforcement officer:\n\n(i) the name of the authorised civilian; and\n\n(ii) the name of his or her supervisor under the authority;\nand\n\n(iii) the period for which the authority will remain in force,\nbeing a period not exceeding 3 months;\n\n(i) if the authority relates to an authorised civilian whose\nsupervisor is an intelligence officer:\nComLaw Authoritative Act C2012C00115\n\nAmendments relating to controlled operations, assumed identities and witness identity\nprotection  Schedule 3\nMain amendments  Part 1\n\nCrimes Legislation Amendment (Serious and Organised Crime) Act 2010\n\n(i) the name of the authorised civilian; and\n\n(ii) the name of his or her supervisor under the authority.\n\n(3) The authority must also state the following:\n\n(a) each issuing agency to which a request may be made under\nsection 15KI or 15KX;\n\n(b) whether it authorises an application under a corresponding\nassumed identity law for an order for an entry in a register of\nbirths, deaths or marriages;\n\n(c) whether the assumed identity can be used in a foreign\ncountry and the reasons for the need for this use.\nNote:\nThe chief officer may delegate functions under this section—see\nsection 15LH.\n\n(4) To avoid doubt, subparagraph (2)(h)(iii) does not prevent the grant\nof one or more further authorities in relation to an authorised\ncivilian.",
      "skos:definition": "(1) An authority must be:\n\n(a) in writing in the form approved by the chief officer; and\n\n(b) signed by the person granting it.\n\n(2) An authority must state the following:\n\n(a) the name of the person granting the authority;\n\n(b) the date of the authority;\n\n(c) details of the assumed identity authorised;\n\n(d) details of any evidence of the assumed identity that may be\nacquired under the authority;\n\n(e) the conditions (if any) to which the authority is subject;\n\n(f) why the authority is granted;\n\n(g) if the authority relates to an authorised intelligence officer, an\nauthorised law enforcement officer or a foreign officer—the\nname of the officer;\n\n(h) if the authority relates to an authorised civilian whose\nsupervisor is a law enforcement officer:\n\n(i) the name of the authorised civilian; and\n\n(ii) the name of his or her supervisor under the authority;\nand\n\n(iii) the period for which the authority will remain in force,\nbeing a period not exceeding 3 months;\n\n(i) if the authority relates to an authorised civilian whose\nsupervisor is an intelligence officer:\nComLaw Authoritative Act C2012C00115\n\nAmendments relating to controlled operations, assumed identities and witness identity\nprotection  Schedule 3\nMain amendments  Part 1\n\nCrimes Legislation Amendment (Serious and Organised Crime) Act 2010\n\n(i) the name of the authorised civilian; and\n\n(ii) the name of his or her supervisor under the authority.\n\n(3) The authority must also state the following:\n\n(a) each issuing agency to which a request may be made under\nsection 15KI or 15KX;\n\n(b) whether it authorises an application under a corresponding\nassumed identity law for an order for an entry in a register of\nbirths, deaths or marriages;\n\n(c) whether the assumed identity can be used in a foreign\ncountry and the reasons for the need for this use.\nNote:\nThe chief officer may delegate functions under this section—see\nsection 15LH.\n\n(4) To avoid doubt, subparagraph (2)(h)(iii) does not prevent the grant\nof one or more further au",
      "cml:hasPart": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:crimes-legislation-amendment-serious-and-organised-crime-act-2010-sch-3-sec-15kc-ss-1"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:crimes-legislation-amendment-serious-and-organised-crime-act-2010-sch-3-sec-15kc-ss-2"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:crimes-legislation-amendment-serious-and-organised-crime-act-2010-sch-3-sec-15kc-ss-3"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:crimes-legislation-amendment-serious-and-organised-crime-act-2010-sch-3-sec-15kc-ss-4"
        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "672a512a3ea3f28469a66fa1f602e42ac5a9450d0a1a2d45ba3de5df90ad8dec"
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/crimes-legislation-amendment-serious-and-organised-crime-act-2010#sch-3-sec-15kc",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "15KC Form of authority",
      "values:kind": "section",
      "cof:pageNumber": 120,
      "values:originalText": "(1) An authority must be:\n\n(a) in writing in the form approved by the chief officer; and\n\n(b) signed by the person granting it.\n\n(2) An authority must state the following:\n\n(a) the name of the person granting the authority;\n\n(b) the date of the authority;\n\n(c) details of the assumed identity authorised;\n\n(d) details of any evidence of the assumed identity that may be\nacquired under the authority;\n\n(e) the conditions (if any) to which the authority is subject;\n\n(f) why the authority is granted;\n\n(g) if the authority relates to an authorised intelligence officer, an\nauthorised law enforcement officer or a foreign officer—the\nname of the officer;\n\n(h) if the authority relates to an authorised civilian whose\nsupervisor is a law enforcement officer:\n\n(i) the name of the authorised civilian; and\n\n(ii) the name of his or her supervisor under the authority;\nand\n\n(iii) the period for which the authority will remain in force,\nbeing a period not exceeding 3 months;\n\n(i) if the authority relates to an authorised civilian whose\nsupervisor is an intelligence officer:\nComLaw Authoritative Act C2012C00115\n\nAmendments relating to controlled operations, assumed identities and witness identity\nprotection  Schedule 3\nMain amendments  Part 1\n\nCrimes Legislation Amendment (Serious and Organised Crime) Act 2010\n\n(i) the name of the authorised civilian; and\n\n(ii) the name of his or her supervisor under the authority.\n\n(3) The authority must also state the following:\n\n(a) each issuing agency to which a request may be made under\nsection 15KI or 15KX;\n\n(b) whether it authorises an application under a corresponding\nassumed identity law for an order for an entry in a register of\nbirths, deaths or marriages;\n\n(c) whether the assumed identity can be used in a foreign\ncountry and the reasons for the need for this use.\nNote:\nThe chief officer may delegate functions under this section—see\nsection 15LH.\n\n(4) To avoid doubt, subparagraph (2)(h)(iii) does not prevent the grant\nof one or more further authorities in relation to an authorised\ncivilian."
    },
