    {
      "@id": "concept:crimes-legislation-amendment-serious-and-organised-crime-act-2010-sch-3-sec-15kc-ss-3",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "15KC(3) Form of authority",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/crimes-legislation-amendment-serious-and-organised-crime-act-2010#sch-3-sec-15kc-ss-3"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "crimes-legislation-amendment-serious-and-organised-crime-act-2010.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "crimes-legislation-amendment-serious-and-organised-crime-act-2010.pdf, p.120",
      "values:originalText": "(3) The authority must also state the following:\n\n(a) each issuing agency to which a request may be made under\nsection 15KI or 15KX;\n\n(b) whether it authorises an application under a corresponding\nassumed identity law for an order for an entry in a register of\nbirths, deaths or marriages;\n\n(c) whether the assumed identity can be used in a foreign\ncountry and the reasons for the need for this use.\nNote:\nThe chief officer may delegate functions under this section—see\nsection 15LH.",
      "skos:definition": "(3) The authority must also state the following:\n\n(a) each issuing agency to which a request may be made under\nsection 15KI or 15KX;\n\n(b) whether it authorises an application under a corresponding\nassumed identity law for an order for an entry in a register of\nbirths, deaths or marriages;\n\n(c) whether the assumed identity can be used in a foreign\ncountry and the reasons for the need for this use.\nNote:\nThe chief officer may delegate functions under this section—see\nsection 15LH.",
      "values:partOf": {
        "@id": "concept:crimes-legislation-amendment-serious-and-organised-crime-act-2010-sch-3-sec-15kc"
      },
      "cml:asserts": [
