    {
      "@id": "concept:crimes-legislation-amendment-serious-and-organised-crime-act-2010-sch-3-sec-15ke",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "15KE Variation or cancellation of authority",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/crimes-legislation-amendment-serious-and-organised-crime-act-2010#sch-3-sec-15ke"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "crimes-legislation-amendment-serious-and-organised-crime-act-2010.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "crimes-legislation-amendment-serious-and-organised-crime-act-2010.pdf, p.121",
      "values:originalText": "(1) The chief officer of an agency:\n\n(a) may, at any time, vary or cancel an authority that was granted\nby the chief officer of the agency; and\n\n(b) must cancel the authority if the chief officer is satisfied (on a\nreview under section 15KF or otherwise) that use of the\nassumed identity is no longer necessary.\nNote:\nSection 15KW modifies the effect of this provision if control of the\nauthority is transferred.\nComLaw Authoritative Act C2012C00115\n\nSchedule 3  Amendments relating to controlled operations, assumed identities and\nwitness identity protection",
      "skos:definition": "(1) The chief officer of an agency:\n\n(a) may, at any time, vary or cancel an authority that was granted\nby the chief officer of the agency; and\n\n(b) must cancel the authority if the chief officer is satisfied (on a\nreview under section 15KF or otherwise) that use of the\nassumed identity is no longer necessary.\nNote:\nSection 15KW modifies the effect of this provision if control of the\nauthority is transferred.\nComLaw Authoritative Act C2012C00115\n\nSchedule 3  Amendments relating to controlled operations, assumed identities and\nwitness identity protection",
      "cml:asserts": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:crimes-legislation-amendment-serious-and-organised-crime-act-2010-sch-3-sec-15ke-norm"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:crimes-legislation-amendment-serious-and-organised-crime-act-2010-sch-3-sec-15ke-logic-deontic-1"
        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "d81bfdd9c5e515f1c1dbaad782614781d9015cc041ecec02d143bd3443fcf6b1",
      "skos:note": "Chief officer may vary or cancel authority at any time."
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/crimes-legislation-amendment-serious-and-organised-crime-act-2010#sch-3-sec-15ke",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "15KE Variation or cancellation of authority",
      "values:kind": "section",
      "cof:pageNumber": 121,
      "values:originalText": "(1) The chief officer of an agency:\n\n(a) may, at any time, vary or cancel an authority that was granted\nby the chief officer of the agency; and\n\n(b) must cancel the authority if the chief officer is satisfied (on a\nreview under section 15KF or otherwise) that use of the\nassumed identity is no longer necessary.\nNote:\nSection 15KW modifies the effect of this provision if control of the\nauthority is transferred.\nComLaw Authoritative Act C2012C00115\n\nSchedule 3  Amendments relating to controlled operations, assumed identities and\nwitness identity protection"
    },
    {
      "@id": "concept:crimes-legislation-amendment-serious-and-organised-crime-act-2010-sch-3-sec-15ke-norm",
      "@type": "values:Obligation",
      "cml:modality": {
        "@id": "cml:Deontic"
      },
      "values:partOf": {
