      "dc:source": "crimes-legislation-amendment-serious-and-organised-crime-act-2010.pdf, p.122",
      "values:originalText": "(4) The variation or cancellation takes effect:\n\n(a) if the written notice is given to the authorised person and the\nauthorised person is not an authorised civilian—on the day\nthe written notice is given to the authorised person or, if a\nlater day is stated in the notice, on the later day; or\n\n(b) if the authorised person is an authorised civilian and the\nwritten notice is given to the authorised person’s\nsupervisor—on the day the written notice is given to the\nauthorised person’s supervisor or, if a later day is stated in\nthe notice, on the later day; or\n\n(c) in any other case—on the day stated in the notice.\nNote 1:\nThe chief officer may delegate functions under this section—see\nsection 15LH.\nNote 2:\nDespite the variation or cancellation of an authority, a person is, in\ncertain circumstances, protected from prosecution for offences even if\nthe person is unaware of the variation or cancellation—see\nsection 15KU.",
      "skos:definition": "(4) The variation or cancellation takes effect:\n\n(a) if the written notice is given to the authorised person and the\nauthorised person is not an authorised civilian—on the day\nthe written notice is given to the authorised person or, if a\nlater day is stated in the notice, on the later day; or\n\n(b) if the authorised person is an authorised civilian and the\nwritten notice is given to the authorised person’s\nsupervisor—on the day the written notice is given to the\nauthorised person’s supervisor or, if a later day is stated in\nthe notice, on the later day; or\n\n(c) in any other case—on the day stated in the notice.\nNote 1:\nThe chief officer may delegate functions under this section—see\nsection 15LH.\nNote 2:\nDespite the variation or cancellation of an authority, a person is, in\ncertain circumstances, protected from prosecution for offences even if\nthe person is unaware of the variation or cancellation—see\nsection 15KU.",
      "values:partOf": {
        "@id": "concept:crimes-legislation-amendment-serious-and-organised-crime-act-2010-sch-3-sec-118"
      },
      "cml:asserts": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:crimes-legislation-amendment-serious-and-organised-crime-act-2010-sch-3-sec-118-ss-4-norm"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:crimes-legislation-amendment-serious-and-organised-crime-act-2010-sch-3-sec-118-ss-4-logic-alleninterval-1"
        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "8538b0aa53842696f5c2ce26b0f028daa71ab54f9a5639236043922fe0a2a5d8",
      "skos:note": "Variation or cancellation of authority takes effect on specified day"
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/crimes-legislation-amendment-serious-and-organised-crime-act-2010#sch-3-sec-118-ss-4",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "118(4) Crimes Legislation Amendment (Serious and Organised Crime) Act",
      "values:kind": "subsection",
      "cof:pageNumber": 122,
      "values:originalText": "(4) The variation or cancellation takes effect:\n\n(a) if the written notice is given to the authorised person and the\nauthorised person is not an authorised civilian—on the day\nthe written notice is given to the authorised person or, if a\nlater day is stated in the notice, on the later day; or\n\n(b) if the authorised person is an authorised civilian and the\nwritten notice is given to the authorised person’s\nsupervisor—on the day the written notice is given to the\nauthorised person’s supervisor or, if a later day is stated in\nthe notice, on the later day; or\n\n(c) in any other case—on the day stated in the notice.\nNote 1:\nThe chief officer may delegate functions under this section—see\nsection 15LH.\nNote 2:\nDespite the variation or cancellation of an authority, a person is, in\ncertain circumstances, protected from prosecution for offences even if\nthe person is unaware of the variation or cancellation—see\nsection 15KU."
    },
