        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "52c6b936202c25738f4c9905901aa5ebe96fa6bfe582a2dabee14ad44d74ad21",
      "skos:note": "Chief officer must record opinion and reasons if use of assumed identity is necessary.",
      "dc:description": "Opinion and reasons"
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/crimes-legislation-amendment-serious-and-organised-crime-act-2010#sch-3-sec-15kf-ss-5",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "15KF(5) Yearly review of authority",
      "values:kind": "subsection",
      "cof:pageNumber": 122,
      "values:originalText": "(5) If the chief officer is satisfied on a review that use of the assumed\nidentity under the authority is still necessary, he or she must record\nhis or her opinion, and the reasons for it, in writing.\nNote:\nThe chief officer may delegate functions under this section—see\nsection 15LH."
    },
    {
