      "cml:premiseText": "(6) Failure to comply with the requirements of this section does not invalidate an authority or anything lawfully done under the authority.",
      "cml:conclusionText": "Compliance must be provided."
    },
    {
      "@id": "concept:crimes-legislation-amendment-serious-and-organised-crime-act-2010-sch-3-sec-15kg",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "15KG Making entries in register of births, deaths or marriages",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/crimes-legislation-amendment-serious-and-organised-crime-act-2010#sch-3-sec-15kg"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "crimes-legislation-amendment-serious-and-organised-crime-act-2010.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "crimes-legislation-amendment-serious-and-organised-crime-act-2010.pdf, p.123",
      "values:originalText": "The chief officer of:\n\n(a) a law enforcement agency; or\n\n(b) an intelligence agency;\nmay apply, under a corresponding assumed identity law, to the\nSupreme Court of a State or Territory of a participating jurisdiction\nfor an order that an entry be made in a register of births, deaths or\nmarriages under the relevant law of that jurisdiction in relation to\nthe acquisition of an assumed identity under an authority or\ncorresponding authority.",
      "skos:definition": "The chief officer of:\n\n(a) a law enforcement agency; or\n\n(b) an intelligence agency;\nmay apply, under a corresponding assumed identity law, to the\nSupreme Court of a State or Territory of a participating jurisdiction\nfor an order that an entry be made in a register of births, deaths or\nmarriages under the relevant law of that jurisdiction in relation to\nthe acquisition of an assumed identity under an authority or\ncorresponding authority.",
      "cml:asserts": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:crimes-legislation-amendment-serious-and-organised-crime-act-2010-sch-3-sec-15kg-norm"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:crimes-legislation-amendment-serious-and-organised-crime-act-2010-sch-3-sec-15kg-logic-deontic-1"
        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "068d56b5fd81e679f0cf4a44345d4f4c4c6fcb5668ea82ea6f3ad193542376ac",
      "skos:note": "Chief officer may apply for order to make entry in register of births, deaths or marriages."
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/crimes-legislation-amendment-serious-and-organised-crime-act-2010#sch-3-sec-15kg",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "15KG Making entries in register of births, deaths or marriages",
      "values:kind": "section",
      "cof:pageNumber": 123,
      "values:originalText": "The chief officer of:\n\n(a) a law enforcement agency; or\n\n(b) an intelligence agency;\nmay apply, under a corresponding assumed identity law, to the\nSupreme Court of a State or Territory of a participating jurisdiction\nfor an order that an entry be made in a register of births, deaths or\nmarriages under the relevant law of that jurisdiction in relation to\nthe acquisition of an assumed identity under an authority or\ncorresponding authority."
    },
    {
      "@id": "concept:crimes-legislation-amendment-serious-and-organised-crime-act-2010-sch-3-sec-15kg-norm",
      "@type": "values:Obligation",
      "cml:modality": {
        "@id": "cml:Deontic"
      },
      "values:partOf": {
        "@id": "concept:crimes-legislation-amendment-serious-and-organised-crime-act-2010-sch-3-sec-15kg"
      },
      "values:deonticStatus": {
        "@id": "values:HeuristicDerived"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "values:borneBy": {
        "@id": "values:State"
      },
      "skos:scopeNote": "borne by: State"
    },
    {
      "@id": "concept:crimes-legislation-amendment-serious-and-organised-crime-act-2010-sch-3-sec-15kg-logic-deontic-1",
      "@type": "cml:LogicApplication",
      "cml:modality": {
        "@id": "cml:Deontic"
      },
      "cml:operator": "may",
      "cml:logicSummary": "Expresses permission or obligation.",
      "cml:executionSurface": "modalities::logic::deontic",
      "cml:confidence": {
        "@value": 1.0,
        "@type": "xsd:decimal"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      }
    },
    {
      "@id": "concept:crimes-legislation-amendment-serious-and-organised-crime-act-2010-sch-3-sec-15kh",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "15KH Effect of authority ceasing to be in force on register of births,",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/crimes-legislation-amendment-serious-and-organised-crime-act-2010#sch-3-sec-15kh"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "crimes-legislation-amendment-serious-and-organised-crime-act-2010.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "crimes-legislation-amendment-serious-and-organised-crime-act-2010.pdf, p.123",
      "values:originalText": "deaths or marriages\n\n(1) This section applies if:\n\n(a) an authority for an assumed identity ceases to be in force;\nand\n\n(b) there is an entry in relation to that assumed identity in a\nregister of births, deaths or marriages because of an order\nunder a corresponding assumed identity law.\nComLaw Authoritative Act C2012C00115\n\nSchedule 3  Amendments relating to controlled operations, assumed identities and\nwitness identity protection",
      "skos:definition": "deaths or marriages\n\n(1) This section applies if:\n\n(a) an authority for an assumed identity ceases to be in force;\nand\n\n(b) there is an entry in relation to that assumed identity in a\nregister of births, deaths or marriages because of an order\nunder a corresponding assumed identity law.\nComLaw Authoritative Act C2012C00115\n\nSchedule 3  Amendments relating to controlled operations, assumed identities and\nwitness identity protection",
      "cml:asserts": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:crimes-legislation-amendment-serious-and-organised-crime-act-2010-sch-3-sec-15kh-norm"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:crimes-legislation-amendment-serious-and-organised-crime-act-2010-sch-3-sec-15kh-logic-deontic-1"
        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "0750564531bdefc1193be9d0f39bb21f0517a96a62af1da993d8f0464c8ea28d",
      "skos:note": "Register of births, deaths or marriages must be updated when an authority ceases to be in force."
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/crimes-legislation-amendment-serious-and-organised-crime-act-2010#sch-3-sec-15kh",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "15KH Effect of authority ceasing to be in force on register of births,",
      "values:kind": "section",
      "cof:pageNumber": 123,
      "values:originalText": "deaths or marriages\n\n(1) This section applies if:\n\n(a) an authority for an assumed identity ceases to be in force;\nand\n\n(b) there is an entry in relation to that assumed identity in a\nregister of births, deaths or marriages because of an order\nunder a corresponding assumed identity law.\nComLaw Authoritative Act C2012C00115\n\nSchedule 3  Amendments relating to controlled operations, assumed identities and\nwitness identity protection"
    },
    {
      "@id": "concept:crimes-legislation-amendment-serious-and-organised-crime-act-2010-sch-3-sec-15kh-norm",
      "@type": "values:Obligation",
