          "@id": "concept:crimes-legislation-amendment-serious-and-organised-crime-act-2010-sch-3-sec-15ki-ss-6-logic-descriptionlogic-2"
        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "a0f1e094b836f4ee42edc02300a0e0c0d95ca0a354da8b3ef83f8c0fbd066dd7",
      "skos:note": "Definition of evidence for assumed identity"
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/crimes-legislation-amendment-serious-and-organised-crime-act-2010#sch-3-sec-15ki-ss-6",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "15KI(6) Request for evidence of assumed identity",
      "values:kind": "subsection",
      "cof:pageNumber": 124,
      "values:originalText": "(6) In this section:\nevidence means evidence similar to that ordinarily produced or\ngiven by the issuing agency.\nNote:\nThe chief officer may delegate functions under this section—see\nsection 15LH.\nComLaw Authoritative Act C2012C00115\n\nAmendments relating to controlled operations, assumed identities and witness identity\nprotection  Schedule 3\nMain amendments  Part 1\n\nCrimes Legislation Amendment (Serious and Organised Crime) Act 2010"
