    {
      "@id": "concept:crimes-legislation-amendment-serious-and-organised-crime-act-2010-sch-3-sec-15kl",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "15KL Cancellation of evidence of assumed identity",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/crimes-legislation-amendment-serious-and-organised-crime-act-2010#sch-3-sec-15kl"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "crimes-legislation-amendment-serious-and-organised-crime-act-2010.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "crimes-legislation-amendment-serious-and-organised-crime-act-2010.pdf, p.125",
      "values:originalText": "(1) The chief officer of an issuing agency who produces evidence of\nan assumed identity under this Part must cancel the evidence if\ndirected in writing to do so by the chief officer who requested the\nevidence.\nNote 1:\nThe chief officer who requested the evidence may delegate functions\nunder this section—see section 15LH.\nNote 2:\nSection 15KW modifies the effect of this provision if control of the\nauthority is transferred.\n\n(2) In this section:\ncancel includes delete or alter an entry in a record of information.",
      "skos:definition": "(1) The chief officer of an issuing agency who produces evidence of\nan assumed identity under this Part must cancel the evidence if\ndirected in writing to do so by the chief officer who requested the\nevidence.\nNote 1:\nThe chief officer who requested the evidence may delegate functions\nunder this section—see section 15LH.\nNote 2:\nSection 15KW modifies the effect of this provision if control of the\nauthority is transferred.\n\n(2) In this section:\ncancel includes delete or alter an entry in a record of information.",
      "cml:hasPart": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:crimes-legislation-amendment-serious-and-organised-crime-act-2010-sch-3-sec-15kl-ss-1"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:crimes-legislation-amendment-serious-and-organised-crime-act-2010-sch-3-sec-15kl-ss-2"
        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "e5a1e6cd67078d340133b123ec653b892c892f47bb84c39789478250877198a5"
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/crimes-legislation-amendment-serious-and-organised-crime-act-2010#sch-3-sec-15kl",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "15KL Cancellation of evidence of assumed identity",
      "values:kind": "section",
      "cof:pageNumber": 125,
      "values:originalText": "(1) The chief officer of an issuing agency who produces evidence of\nan assumed identity under this Part must cancel the evidence if\ndirected in writing to do so by the chief officer who requested the\nevidence.\nNote 1:\nThe chief officer who requested the evidence may delegate functions\nunder this section—see section 15LH.\nNote 2:\nSection 15KW modifies the effect of this provision if control of the\nauthority is transferred.\n\n(2) In this section:\ncancel includes delete or alter an entry in a record of information."
    },
