    {
      "@id": "concept:crimes-legislation-amendment-serious-and-organised-crime-act-2010-sch-3-sec-15km",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "15KM Return of evidence of assumed identity",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/crimes-legislation-amendment-serious-and-organised-crime-act-2010#sch-3-sec-15km"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "crimes-legislation-amendment-serious-and-organised-crime-act-2010.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "crimes-legislation-amendment-serious-and-organised-crime-act-2010.pdf, p.125",
      "values:originalText": "(1) This section applies if an authority for a person to acquire or use an\nassumed identity ceases to be in force.\n\n(2) The chief officer of a law enforcement agency or the chief officer\nof an intelligence agency may, in writing, request the person to\nreturn to the chief officer any evidence of the assumed identity\nacquired under the authority.\n\n(3) A person commits an offence if:\n\n(a) a request has been made to the person under subsection (2);\nand\n\n(b) the person fails to comply with the request.\nPenalty: 10 penalty units.\nComLaw Authoritative Act C2012C00115\n\nSchedule 3  Amendments relating to controlled operations, assumed identities and\nwitness identity protection",
      "skos:definition": "(1) This section applies if an authority for a person to acquire or use an\nassumed identity ceases to be in force.\n\n(2) The chief officer of a law enforcement agency or the chief officer\nof an intelligence agency may, in writing, request the person to\nreturn to the chief officer any evidence of the assumed identity\nacquired under the authority.\n\n(3) A person commits an offence if:\n\n(a) a request has been made to the person under subsection (2);\nand\n\n(b) the person fails to comply with the request.\nPenalty: 10 penalty units.\nComLaw Authoritative Act C2012C00115\n\nSchedule 3  Amendments relating to controlled operations, assumed identities and\nwitness identity protection",
      "cml:hasPart": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:crimes-legislation-amendment-serious-and-organised-crime-act-2010-sch-3-sec-15km-ss-1"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:crimes-legislation-amendment-serious-and-organised-crime-act-2010-sch-3-sec-15km-ss-2"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:crimes-legislation-amendment-serious-and-organised-crime-act-2010-sch-3-sec-15km-ss-3"
        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "9b15bebac84996641f2e200b93fb34c82bfa4384b115d9bc5dc3ad9606b5df2e"
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/crimes-legislation-amendment-serious-and-organised-crime-act-2010#sch-3-sec-15km",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "15KM Return of evidence of assumed identity",
      "values:kind": "section",
      "cof:pageNumber": 125,
      "values:originalText": "(1) This section applies if an authority for a person to acquire or use an\nassumed identity ceases to be in force.\n\n(2) The chief officer of a law enforcement agency or the chief officer\nof an intelligence agency may, in writing, request the person to\nreturn to the chief officer any evidence of the assumed identity\nacquired under the authority.\n\n(3) A person commits an offence if:\n\n(a) a request has been made to the person under subsection (2);\nand\n\n(b) the person fails to comply with the request.\nPenalty: 10 penalty units.\nComLaw Authoritative Act C2012C00115\n\nSchedule 3  Amendments relating to controlled operations, assumed identities and\nwitness identity protection"
    },
