    {
      "@id": "concept:crimes-legislation-amendment-serious-and-organised-crime-act-2010-sch-3-sec-15ks",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "15KS Indemnity for authorised persons",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/crimes-legislation-amendment-serious-and-organised-crime-act-2010#sch-3-sec-15ks"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "crimes-legislation-amendment-serious-and-organised-crime-act-2010.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "crimes-legislation-amendment-serious-and-organised-crime-act-2010.pdf, p.127",
      "values:originalText": "(1) This section applies if the chief officer of either a law enforcement\nagency or an intelligence agency grants an authority.\n\n(2) The Commonwealth must indemnify the authorised person under\nthe authority for any liability incurred by the person (including\nreasonable costs) because of something done by the person if:\nComLaw Authoritative Act C2012C00115\n\nSchedule 3  Amendments relating to controlled operations, assumed identities and\nwitness identity protection",
      "skos:definition": "(1) This section applies if the chief officer of either a law enforcement\nagency or an intelligence agency grants an authority.\n\n(2) The Commonwealth must indemnify the authorised person under\nthe authority for any liability incurred by the person (including\nreasonable costs) because of something done by the person if:\nComLaw Authoritative Act C2012C00115\n\nSchedule 3  Amendments relating to controlled operations, assumed identities and\nwitness identity protection",
