    {
      "@id": "concept:crimes-legislation-amendment-serious-and-organised-crime-act-2010-sch-3-sec-15kv-ss-3",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "15KV(3) Transfer of control of authorities",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/crimes-legislation-amendment-serious-and-organised-crime-act-2010#sch-3-sec-15kv-ss-3"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "crimes-legislation-amendment-serious-and-organised-crime-act-2010.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "crimes-legislation-amendment-serious-and-organised-crime-act-2010.pdf, p.129",
      "values:originalText": "(3) The chief officer of the originating agency must give the chief\nofficer of the receiving agency a written document setting out:\n\n(a) whether the authority has been reviewed under section 15KF,\nand if so, when a review was last conducted; and\n\n(b) whether control of the authority has previously been\ntransferred under this section, and if so:\nComLaw Authoritative Act C2012C00115\n\nSchedule 3  Amendments relating to controlled operations, assumed identities and\nwitness identity protection",
      "skos:definition": "(3) The chief officer of the originating agency must give the chief\nofficer of the receiving agency a written document setting out:\n\n(a) whether the authority has been reviewed under section 15KF,\nand if so, when a review was last conducted; and\n\n(b) whether control of the authority has previously been\ntransferred under this section, and if so:\nComLaw Authoritative Act C2012C00115\n\nSchedule 3  Amendments relating to controlled operations, assumed identities and\nwitness identity protection",
      "values:partOf": {
        "@id": "concept:crimes-legislation-amendment-serious-and-organised-crime-act-2010-sch-3-sec-15kv"
      },
      "cml:asserts": [
