      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:premiseText": "(b) whether control of the authority has previously been transferred under this section, and if so:"
    },
    {
      "@id": "concept:crimes-legislation-amendment-serious-and-organised-crime-act-2010-sch-3-sec-15kv-ss-3-logic-deontic-3",
      "@type": "cml:LogicApplication",
      "cml:modality": {
        "@id": "cml:Deontic"
      },
      "cml:operator": "MUST",
      "cml:logicSummary": "Must provide written document to chief officer of receiving agency",
      "cml:executionSurface": "modalities::logic::deontic",
      "cml:confidence": {
        "@value": 1.0,
        "@type": "xsd:decimal"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:premiseText": "(3) The chief officer of the originating agency must give the chief officer of the receiving agency a written document setting out:"
    },
    {
      "@id": "concept:crimes-legislation-amendment-serious-and-organised-crime-act-2010-sch-3-sec-126",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "126 Crimes Legislation Amendment (Serious and Organised Crime) Act",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/crimes-legislation-amendment-serious-and-organised-crime-act-2010#sch-3-sec-126"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "crimes-legislation-amendment-serious-and-organised-crime-act-2010.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "crimes-legislation-amendment-serious-and-organised-crime-act-2010.pdf, p.130",
      "values:originalText": "(i) the date of each such transfer; and\n\n(ii) the name of the originating agency and receiving agency\nin relation to each such transfer.\n\n(4) Control of the authority is transferred at the time when the chief\nofficer of the receiving agency signs and dates a copy of the\nauthority.\n\n(5) Despite subsection (4), if the authority relates to an authorised\ncivilian, control of the authority is not transferred until the chief\nofficer of the receiving agency appoints an officer of that agency to\nbe the authorised civilian’s supervisor.\n\n(6) The chief officer of the receiving agency must vary the authority in\naccordance with section 15KE to state the name of the supervisor\nappointed under subsection (5).\n\n(7) Control of an authority must not be transferred under this section\nif:\n\n(a) the person who is to acquire or use the assumed identity, or\nwho has acquired or used the assumed identity, is a foreign\nofficer authorised to acquire or use the assumed identity by\nthe chief officer of a law enforcement agency; or\n\n(b) the assumed identity is to be, is being or has been used in a\nforeign country and the authority was granted by the chief\nofficer of a law enforcement agency.",
      "skos:definition": "(i) the date of each such transfer; and\n\n(ii) the name of the originating agency and receiving agency\nin relation to each such transfer.\n\n(4) Control of the authority is transferred at the time when the chief\nofficer of the receiving agency signs and dates a copy of the\nauthority.\n\n(5) Despite subsection (4), if the authority relates to an authorised\ncivilian, control of the authority is not transferred until the chief\nofficer of the receiving agency appoints an officer of that agency to\nbe the authorised civilian’s supervisor.\n\n(6) The chief officer of the receiving agency must vary the authority in\naccordance with section 15KE to state the name of the supervisor\nappointed under subsection (5).\n\n(7) Control of an authority must not be transferred under this section\nif:\n\n(a) the person who is to acquire or use the assumed identity, or\nwho has acquired or used the assumed identity, is a foreign\nofficer authorised to acquire or use the assumed identity by\nthe chief officer of a law enforcement agency; or\n\n(b) the assumed identity is to be, is being or has been used in a\nforeign country and the authority was granted by the chief\nofficer of a law enforcement agency.",
      "cml:hasPart": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:crimes-legislation-amendment-serious-and-organised-crime-act-2010-sch-3-sec-126-ss-4"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:crimes-legislation-amendment-serious-and-organised-crime-act-2010-sch-3-sec-126-ss-5"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:crimes-legislation-amendment-serious-and-organised-crime-act-2010-sch-3-sec-126-ss-6"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:crimes-legislation-amendment-serious-and-organised-crime-act-2010-sch-3-sec-126-ss-7"
        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "3f915fc3c8542bd553cefd9381447c9dae41ce952172a2f5ddb93fea48a4554a"
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/crimes-legislation-amendment-serious-and-organised-crime-act-2010#sch-3-sec-126",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "126 Crimes Legislation Amendment (Serious and Organised Crime) Act",
      "values:kind": "section",
      "cof:pageNumber": 130,
      "values:originalText": "(i) the date of each such transfer; and\n\n(ii) the name of the originating agency and receiving agency\nin relation to each such transfer.\n\n(4) Control of the authority is transferred at the time when the chief\nofficer of the receiving agency signs and dates a copy of the\nauthority.\n\n(5) Despite subsection (4), if the authority relates to an authorised\ncivilian, control of the authority is not transferred until the chief\nofficer of the receiving agency appoints an officer of that agency to\nbe the authorised civilian’s supervisor.\n\n(6) The chief officer of the receiving agency must vary the authority in\naccordance with section 15KE to state the name of the supervisor\nappointed under subsection (5).\n\n(7) Control of an authority must not be transferred under this section\nif:\n\n(a) the person who is to acquire or use the assumed identity, or\nwho has acquired or used the assumed identity, is a foreign\nofficer authorised to acquire or use the assumed identity by\nthe chief officer of a law enforcement agency; or\n\n(b) the assumed identity is to be, is being or has been used in a\nforeign country and the authority was granted by the chief\nofficer of a law enforcement agency."
    },
