    {
      "@id": "concept:crimes-legislation-amendment-serious-and-organised-crime-act-2010-sch-3-sec-15kw",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "15KW Consequences of transfer of control of authorities",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/crimes-legislation-amendment-serious-and-organised-crime-act-2010#sch-3-sec-15kw"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "crimes-legislation-amendment-serious-and-organised-crime-act-2010.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "crimes-legislation-amendment-serious-and-organised-crime-act-2010.pdf, p.130",
      "values:originalText": "(1) This section sets out the consequences of the transfer of control of\nan authority under section 15KV.\n\n(2) The authority continues to be in force after the transfer.\n\n(3) The following provisions have effect, after the transfer, as if the\nchief officer of the receiving agency had granted the authority\ninstead of the chief officer of the originating agency:\n\n(a) section 15KE (which deals with variation and cancellation of\nauthorities);\n\n(b) section 15KF (which deals with review of authorities);\n\n(c) sections 15KI and 15KX (which deal with requests for\nevidence of assumed identities).\nComLaw Authoritative Act C2012C00115\n\nAmendments relating to controlled operations, assumed identities and witness identity\nprotection  Schedule 3\nMain amendments  Part 1\n\nCrimes Legislation Amendment (Serious and Organised Crime) Act 2010\n\n(4) To avoid doubt, the obligation under section 15KF, as that section\nhas effect because of subsection (3), for the chief officer of the\nreceiving agency to review the authority, only arises:\n\n(a) in the case of an authority transferred under subsection\n15KV(1):\n\n(i) 3 years after the last review of the authority by the chief\nofficer of an intelligence agency; or\n\n(ii) if no such review has been undertaken—3 years after\nthe authority was granted; and\n\n(b) in the case of an authority transferred under subsection\n15KV(2):\n\n(i) 12 months after the last review of the authority by the\nchief officer of a law enforcement agency; or\n\n(ii) if no such review has been undertaken—12 months after\nthe authority was granted.\n\n(5) Section 15KL (which deals with cancellation of evidence of\nassumed identity) has effect as if the chief officer of the receiving\nagency had made the request under section 15KI.",
      "skos:definition": "(1) This section sets out the consequences of the transfer of control of\nan authority under section 15KV.\n\n(2) The authority continues to be in force after the transfer.\n\n(3) The following provisions have effect, after the transfer, as if the\nchief officer of the receiving agency had granted the authority\ninstead of the chief officer of the originating agency:\n\n(a) section 15KE (which deals with variation and cancellation of\nauthorities);\n\n(b) section 15KF (which deals with review of authorities);\n\n(c) sections 15KI and 15KX (which deal with requests for\nevidence of assumed identities).\nComLaw Authoritative Act C2012C00115\n\nAmendments relating to controlled operations, assumed identities and witness identity\nprotection  Schedule 3\nMain amendments  Part 1\n\nCrimes Legislation Amendment (Serious and Organised Crime) Act 2010\n\n(4) To avoid doubt, the obligation under section 15KF, as that section\nhas effect because of subsection (3), for the chief officer of the\nreceiving agency to review the authority, only arises:\n\n(a) in the case of an authority transferred under subsection\n15KV(1):\n\n(i) 3 years after the last review of the authority by the chief\nofficer of an intelligence agency; or\n\n(ii) if no such review has been undertaken—3 years after\nthe authority was granted; and\n\n(b) in the case of an authority transferred under subsection\n15KV(2):\n\n(i) 12 months after the last review of the authority by the\nchief officer of a law enforcement agency; or\n\n(ii) if no such review has been undertaken—12 months after\nthe authority was granted.\n\n(5) Section 15KL (which deals with cancellation of evidence of\nassumed identity) has effect as if the chief officer of the receiving\nagency had made the request under section 15KI.",
      "cml:hasPart": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:crimes-legislation-amendment-serious-and-organised-crime-act-2010-sch-3-sec-15kw-ss-1"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:crimes-legislation-amendment-serious-and-organised-crime-act-2010-sch-3-sec-15kw-ss-2"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:crimes-legislation-amendment-serious-and-organised-crime-act-2010-sch-3-sec-15kw-ss-3"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:crimes-legislation-amendment-serious-and-organised-crime-act-2010-sch-3-sec-15kw-ss-4"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:crimes-legislation-amendment-serious-and-organised-crime-act-2010-sch-3-sec-15kw-ss-5"
        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "1d8663590b7ba7a7d918861d1573111abcdde228106dc7e6651903a1399c75d7"
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/crimes-legislation-amendment-serious-and-organised-crime-act-2010#sch-3-sec-15kw",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "15KW Consequences of transfer of control of authorities",
      "values:kind": "section",
      "cof:pageNumber": 130,
      "values:originalText": "(1) This section sets out the consequences of the transfer of control of\nan authority under section 15KV.\n\n(2) The authority continues to be in force after the transfer.\n\n(3) The following provisions have effect, after the transfer, as if the\nchief officer of the receiving agency had granted the authority\ninstead of the chief officer of the originating agency:\n\n(a) section 15KE (which deals with variation and cancellation of\nauthorities);\n\n(b) section 15KF (which deals with review of authorities);\n\n(c) sections 15KI and 15KX (which deal with requests for\nevidence of assumed identities).\nComLaw Authoritative Act C2012C00115\n\nAmendments relating to controlled operations, assumed identities and witness identity\nprotection  Schedule 3\nMain amendments  Part 1\n\nCrimes Legislation Amendment (Serious and Organised Crime) Act 2010\n\n(4) To avoid doubt, the obligation under section 15KF, as that section\nhas effect because of subsection (3), for the chief officer of the\nreceiving agency to review the authority, only arises:\n\n(a) in the case of an authority transferred under subsection\n15KV(1):\n\n(i) 3 years after the last review of the authority by the chief\nofficer of an intelligence agency; or\n\n(ii) if no such review has been undertaken—3 years after\nthe authority was granted; and\n\n(b) in the case of an authority transferred under subsection\n15KV(2):\n\n(i) 12 months after the last review of the authority by the\nchief officer of a law enforcement agency; or\n\n(ii) if no such review has been undertaken—12 months after\nthe authority was granted.\n\n(5) Section 15KL (which deals with cancellation of evidence of\nassumed identity) has effect as if the chief officer of the receiving\nagency had made the request under section 15KI."
    },
