    {
      "@id": "concept:crimes-legislation-amendment-serious-and-organised-crime-act-2010-sch-3-sec-15la",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "15LA Application of this Part to authorities under corresponding",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/crimes-legislation-amendment-serious-and-organised-crime-act-2010#sch-3-sec-15la"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "crimes-legislation-amendment-serious-and-organised-crime-act-2010.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "crimes-legislation-amendment-serious-and-organised-crime-act-2010.pdf, p.133",
      "values:originalText": "laws\n\n(1) The following provisions apply to anything done in relation to a\ncorresponding authority as if it were an authority granted under\nsection 15KB:\n\n(a) section 15KP (assumed identity may be acquired and used);\n\n(b) section 15KT (particular qualifications);\n\n(c) section 15KU (effect of being unaware of variation or\ncancellation of authority);\n\n(d) section 15LB (misuse of assumed identity);\n\n(e) section 15LC (disclosing information about assumed\nidentity).\n\n(2) Sections 15KN, 15KQ and 15KR apply to anything done in\nrelation to a corresponding authority as if:\n\n(a) the corresponding authority were an authority granted under\nsection 15KB; and\nComLaw Authoritative Act C2012C00115\n\nSchedule 3  Amendments relating to controlled operations, assumed identities and\nwitness identity protection",
      "skos:definition": "laws\n\n(1) The following provisions apply to anything done in relation to a\ncorresponding authority as if it were an authority granted under\nsection 15KB:\n\n(a) section 15KP (assumed identity may be acquired and used);\n\n(b) section 15KT (particular qualifications);\n\n(c) section 15KU (effect of being unaware of variation or\ncancellation of authority);\n\n(d) section 15LB (misuse of assumed identity);\n\n(e) section 15LC (disclosing information about assumed\nidentity).\n\n(2) Sections 15KN, 15KQ and 15KR apply to anything done in\nrelation to a corresponding authority as if:\n\n(a) the corresponding authority were an authority granted under\nsection 15KB; and\nComLaw Authoritative Act C2012C00115\n\nSchedule 3  Amendments relating to controlled operations, assumed identities and\nwitness identity protection",
      "cml:hasPart": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:crimes-legislation-amendment-serious-and-organised-crime-act-2010-sch-3-sec-15la-ss-1"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:crimes-legislation-amendment-serious-and-organised-crime-act-2010-sch-3-sec-15la-ss-2"
        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "8954b4ce200e1b10594592fbed1a8ba405c3e70d3a3ae2909815f7b5cdaf992c"
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/crimes-legislation-amendment-serious-and-organised-crime-act-2010#sch-3-sec-15la",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "15LA Application of this Part to authorities under corresponding",
      "values:kind": "section",
      "cof:pageNumber": 133,
      "values:originalText": "laws\n\n(1) The following provisions apply to anything done in relation to a\ncorresponding authority as if it were an authority granted under\nsection 15KB:\n\n(a) section 15KP (assumed identity may be acquired and used);\n\n(b) section 15KT (particular qualifications);\n\n(c) section 15KU (effect of being unaware of variation or\ncancellation of authority);\n\n(d) section 15LB (misuse of assumed identity);\n\n(e) section 15LC (disclosing information about assumed\nidentity).\n\n(2) Sections 15KN, 15KQ and 15KR apply to anything done in\nrelation to a corresponding authority as if:\n\n(a) the corresponding authority were an authority granted under\nsection 15KB; and\nComLaw Authoritative Act C2012C00115\n\nSchedule 3  Amendments relating to controlled operations, assumed identities and\nwitness identity protection"
    },
