    {
      "@id": "concept:crimes-legislation-amendment-serious-and-organised-crime-act-2010-sch-3-sec-15lb",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "15LB Misuse of assumed identity",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/crimes-legislation-amendment-serious-and-organised-crime-act-2010#sch-3-sec-15lb"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "crimes-legislation-amendment-serious-and-organised-crime-act-2010.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "crimes-legislation-amendment-serious-and-organised-crime-act-2010.pdf, p.134",
      "values:originalText": "(1) A person commits an offence if:\n\n(a) the person is an authorised person (other than an authorised\ncivilian); and\n\n(b) the person acquires evidence of, or uses, an assumed identity;\nand\n\n(c) the acquisition or use is not both:\n\n(i) in accordance with an authority; and\n\n(ii) in the course of duty; and\n\n(d) the person is reckless as to the circumstance mentioned in\nparagraph (c).\nPenalty: Imprisonment for 2 years.\n\n(2) An authorised civilian commits an offence if:\n\n(a) the authorised civilian acquires evidence of, or uses, an\nassumed identity; and\n\n(b) the acquisition or use is not in accordance with both:\n\n(i) an authority; and\n\n(ii) the directions of the authorised civilian’s supervisor\nunder the authority; and\n\n(c) the authorised civilian is reckless as to the circumstance\nmentioned in paragraph (b).\nPenalty: Imprisonment for 2 years.",
      "skos:definition": "(1) A person commits an offence if:\n\n(a) the person is an authorised person (other than an authorised\ncivilian); and\n\n(b) the person acquires evidence of, or uses, an assumed identity;\nand\n\n(c) the acquisition or use is not both:\n\n(i) in accordance with an authority; and\n\n(ii) in the course of duty; and\n\n(d) the person is reckless as to the circumstance mentioned in\nparagraph (c).\nPenalty: Imprisonment for 2 years.\n\n(2) An authorised civilian commits an offence if:\n\n(a) the authorised civilian acquires evidence of, or uses, an\nassumed identity; and\n\n(b) the acquisition or use is not in accordance with both:\n\n(i) an authority; and\n\n(ii) the directions of the authorised civilian’s supervisor\nunder the authority; and\n\n(c) the authorised civilian is reckless as to the circumstance\nmentioned in paragraph (b).\nPenalty: Imprisonment for 2 years.",
      "cml:hasPart": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:crimes-legislation-amendment-serious-and-organised-crime-act-2010-sch-3-sec-15lb-ss-1"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:crimes-legislation-amendment-serious-and-organised-crime-act-2010-sch-3-sec-15lb-ss-2"
        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "478c0697facc9ac5fb8c8eecbe6b3267453a2da07ae62aca43ab6027550e3ba7"
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/crimes-legislation-amendment-serious-and-organised-crime-act-2010#sch-3-sec-15lb",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "15LB Misuse of assumed identity",
      "values:kind": "section",
      "cof:pageNumber": 134,
      "values:originalText": "(1) A person commits an offence if:\n\n(a) the person is an authorised person (other than an authorised\ncivilian); and\n\n(b) the person acquires evidence of, or uses, an assumed identity;\nand\n\n(c) the acquisition or use is not both:\n\n(i) in accordance with an authority; and\n\n(ii) in the course of duty; and\n\n(d) the person is reckless as to the circumstance mentioned in\nparagraph (c).\nPenalty: Imprisonment for 2 years.\n\n(2) An authorised civilian commits an offence if:\n\n(a) the authorised civilian acquires evidence of, or uses, an\nassumed identity; and\n\n(b) the acquisition or use is not in accordance with both:\n\n(i) an authority; and\n\n(ii) the directions of the authorised civilian’s supervisor\nunder the authority; and\n\n(c) the authorised civilian is reckless as to the circumstance\nmentioned in paragraph (b).\nPenalty: Imprisonment for 2 years."
    },
