      },
      "cml:operator": "Overlaps",
      "cml:logicSummary": "Defines the temporal interval during which the obligation applies.",
      "cml:executionSurface": "modalities::interval_reasoning",
      "cml:confidence": {
        "@value": 1.0,
        "@type": "xsd:decimal"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:premiseText": "(2) An authorised civilian commits an offence...",
      "cml:conclusionText": "The obligation applies to all times after the commencement of this section."
    },
    {
      "@id": "concept:crimes-legislation-amendment-serious-and-organised-crime-act-2010-sch-3-sec-15lb-ss-2-logic-deontic-4",
      "@type": "cml:LogicApplication",
      "cml:modality": {
        "@id": "cml:Deontic"
      },
      "cml:operator": "Permission",
      "cml:logicSummary": "Permits authorised civilians to acquire or use assumed identities in accordance with authority and supervisor directions.",
      "cml:executionSurface": "modalities::logic::deontic",
      "cml:confidence": {
        "@value": 1.0,
        "@type": "xsd:decimal"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:premiseText": "(2) An authorised civilian commits an offence...",
      "cml:conclusionText": "Authorised civilians are permitted to acquire or use assumed identities in accordance with authority and supervisor directions."
    },
    {
      "@id": "concept:crimes-legislation-amendment-serious-and-organised-crime-act-2010-sch-3-sec-15lb-ss-2-logic-deontic-5",
      "@type": "cml:LogicApplication",
      "cml:modality": {
        "@id": "cml:Deontic"
      },
      "cml:operator": "Right",
      "cml:logicSummary": "Grants a right to authorised civilians to acquire or use assumed identities in accordance with authority and supervisor directions.",
      "cml:executionSurface": "modalities::logic::deontic",
      "cml:confidence": {
        "@value": 1.0,
        "@type": "xsd:decimal"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:premiseText": "(2) An authorised civilian commits an offence...",
      "cml:conclusionText": "Authorised civilians have a right to acquire or use assumed identities in accordance with authority and supervisor directions."
    },
    {
      "@id": "concept:crimes-legislation-amendment-serious-and-organised-crime-act-2010-sch-3-sec-15lc",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "15LC Disclosing information about assumed identity",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/crimes-legislation-amendment-serious-and-organised-crime-act-2010#sch-3-sec-15lc"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "crimes-legislation-amendment-serious-and-organised-crime-act-2010.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "crimes-legislation-amendment-serious-and-organised-crime-act-2010.pdf, p.134",
      "values:originalText": "(1) A person commits an offence if:\n\n(a) the person engages in conduct; and\n\n(b) the conduct causes the disclosure of information; and\nComLaw Authoritative Act C2012C00115\n\nAmendments relating to controlled operations, assumed identities and witness identity\nprotection  Schedule 3\nMain amendments  Part 1\n\nCrimes Legislation Amendment (Serious and Organised Crime) Act 2010\n\n(c) the information reveals, or is likely to reveal, that another\nperson has acquired, will acquire, is using or has used an\nassumed identity.\nPenalty: Imprisonment for 2 years.\n\n(2) A person commits an offence if:\n\n(a) the person engages in conduct; and\n\n(b) the conduct causes the disclosure of information; and\n\n(c) the information reveals, or is likely to reveal, that another\nperson has acquired, will acquire, is using or has used an\nassumed identity; and\n\n(d) the person is reckless as to whether his or her conduct will\nendanger the health or safety of any person.\nPenalty: Imprisonment for 10 years.\n\n(3) A person commits an offence if:\n\n(a) the person engages in conduct; and\n\n(b) the conduct causes the disclosure of information; and\n\n(c) the information reveals, or is likely to reveal, that another\nperson has acquired, will acquire, is using or has used an\nassumed identity; and\n\n(d) the person is reckless as to whether his or her conduct will\nprejudice the effective conduct of an investigation or\nintelligence-gathering in relation to criminal activity.\nPenalty: Imprisonment for 10 years.\n\n(4) A person does not commit an offence under subsection (1), (2) or\n(3) if the person causes the disclosure of information mentioned in\nparagraph (1)(c), (2)(c) or (3)(c) (as the case may be) and the\ndisclosure is:\n\n(a) in connection with the administration or execution of this\nPart or a corresponding assumed identity law; or\n\n(b) for the purposes of any legal proceeding arising out of or\notherwise related to this Part or a corresponding assumed\nidentity law or of any report of any such proceedings; or\n\n(c) made by the Commonwealth Director of Public Prosecutions\nfor the purposes of a legal proceeding; or\nComLaw Authoritative Act C2012C00115\n\nSchedule 3  Amendments relating to controlled operations, assumed identities and\nwitness identity protection",
      "skos:definition": "(1) A person commits an offence if:\n\n(a) the person engages in conduct; and\n\n(b) the conduct causes the disclosure of information; and\nComLaw Authoritative Act C2012C00115\n\nAmendments relating to controlled operations, assumed identities and witness identity\nprotection  Schedule 3\nMain amendments  Part 1\n\nCrimes Legislation Amendment (Serious and Organised Crime) Act 2010\n\n(c) the information reveals, or is likely to reveal, that another\nperson has acquired, will acquire, is using or has used an\nassumed identity.\nPenalty: Imprisonment for 2 years.\n\n(2) A person commits an offence if:\n\n(a) the person engages in conduct; and\n\n(b) the conduct causes the disclosure of information; and\n\n(c) the information reveals, or is likely to reveal, that another\nperson has acquired, will acquire, is using or has used an\nassumed identity; and\n\n(d) the person is reckless as to whether his or her conduct will\nendanger the health or safety of any person.\nPenalty: Imprisonment for 10 years.\n\n(3) A person commits an offence if:\n\n(a) the person engages in conduct; and\n\n(b) the conduct causes the disclosure of information; and\n\n(c) the information reveals, or is likely to reveal, that another\nperson has acquired, will acquire, is using or has used an\nassumed identity; and\n\n(d) the person is reckless as to whether his or her conduct will\nprejudice the effective conduct of an investigation or\nintelligence-gathering in relation to criminal activity.\nPenalty: Imprisonment for 10 years.\n\n(4) A person does not commit an offence under subsection (1), (2) or\n(3) if the person causes the disclosure of information mentioned in\nparagraph (1)(c), (2)(c) or (3)(c) (as the case may be) and the\ndisclosure is:\n\n(a) in connection with the administration or execution of this\nPart or a corresponding assumed identity law; or\n\n(b) for the purposes of any legal proceeding arising out of or\notherwise related to this Part or a corresponding assumed\nidentity law or of any report of any such proceedings; or\n\n(c) ma",
      "cml:hasPart": [
