    {
      "@id": "concept:crimes-legislation-amendment-serious-and-organised-crime-act-2010-sch-3-sec-15le",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "15LE Reports about authorities for assumed identities etc.—",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/crimes-legislation-amendment-serious-and-organised-crime-act-2010#sch-3-sec-15le"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "crimes-legislation-amendment-serious-and-organised-crime-act-2010.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "crimes-legislation-amendment-serious-and-organised-crime-act-2010.pdf, p.137",
      "values:originalText": "intelligence agencies\n\nAs soon as practicable after the end of each financial year, the\nchief officer of an intelligence agency must submit a report to the\nInspector-General of Intelligence and Security (the\nInspector-General) that includes the following information for the\nyear:\n\n(a) the number of authorities granted during the year;\n\n(b) a general description of the activities undertaken by\nauthorised civilians and authorised intelligence officers when\nusing assumed identities under this Part during the year;\n\n(c) the number of applications for authorities that were refused\nduring the year;\n\n(d) the number of authorities of which control was transferred by\nthe chief officer under section 15KV during the year;\n\n(e) the number of authorities of which control was transferred to\nthe chief officer under section 15KV during the year;\n\n(f) a statement whether or not any fraud or other unlawful\nactivity was identified by an audit under section 15LG during\nthe year;\n\n(g) any other information relating to authorities and assumed\nidentities and the administration of this Part that the\nInspector-General considers appropriate.\nComLaw Authoritative Act C2012C00115\n\nSchedule 3  Amendments relating to controlled operations, assumed identities and\nwitness identity protection",
      "skos:definition": "intelligence agencies\n\nAs soon as practicable after the end of each financial year, the\nchief officer of an intelligence agency must submit a report to the\nInspector-General of Intelligence and Security (the\nInspector-General) that includes the following information for the\nyear:\n\n(a) the number of authorities granted during the year;\n\n(b) a general description of the activities undertaken by\nauthorised civilians and authorised intelligence officers when\nusing assumed identities under this Part during the year;\n\n(c) the number of applications for authorities that were refused\nduring the year;\n\n(d) the number of authorities of which control was transferred by\nthe chief officer under section 15KV during the year;\n\n(e) the number of authorities of which control was transferred to\nthe chief officer under section 15KV during the year;\n\n(f) a statement whether or not any fraud or other unlawful\nactivity was identified by an audit under section 15LG during\nthe year;\n\n(g) any other information relating to authorities and assumed\nidentities and the administration of this Part that the\nInspector-General considers appropriate.\nComLaw Authoritative Act C2012C00115\n\nSchedule 3  Amendments relating to controlled operations, assumed identities and\nwitness identity protection",
      "cml:asserts": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:crimes-legislation-amendment-serious-and-organised-crime-act-2010-sch-3-sec-15le-norm"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:crimes-legislation-amendment-serious-and-organised-crime-act-2010-sch-3-sec-15le-logic-deontic-1"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:crimes-legislation-amendment-serious-and-organised-crime-act-2010-sch-3-sec-15le-logic-descriptionlogic-2"
        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "b4ccab7d34d97f725e75552636be04c808fe8ff4ccc000eec3f0ba2c8bab9729",
      "skos:note": "Chief officer of an intelligence agency must submit a report to the Inspector-General.",
      "dc:description": "Yes"
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/crimes-legislation-amendment-serious-and-organised-crime-act-2010#sch-3-sec-15le",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "15LE Reports about authorities for assumed identities etc.—",
      "values:kind": "section",
      "cof:pageNumber": 137,
      "values:originalText": "intelligence agencies\n\nAs soon as practicable after the end of each financial year, the\nchief officer of an intelligence agency must submit a report to the\nInspector-General of Intelligence and Security (the\nInspector-General) that includes the following information for the\nyear:\n\n(a) the number of authorities granted during the year;\n\n(b) a general description of the activities undertaken by\nauthorised civilians and authorised intelligence officers when\nusing assumed identities under this Part during the year;\n\n(c) the number of applications for authorities that were refused\nduring the year;\n\n(d) the number of authorities of which control was transferred by\nthe chief officer under section 15KV during the year;\n\n(e) the number of authorities of which control was transferred to\nthe chief officer under section 15KV during the year;\n\n(f) a statement whether or not any fraud or other unlawful\nactivity was identified by an audit under section 15LG during\nthe year;\n\n(g) any other information relating to authorities and assumed\nidentities and the administration of this Part that the\nInspector-General considers appropriate.\nComLaw Authoritative Act C2012C00115\n\nSchedule 3  Amendments relating to controlled operations, assumed identities and\nwitness identity protection"
    },
