    {
      "@id": "concept:crimes-legislation-amendment-serious-and-organised-crime-act-2010-sch-3-sec-15lg",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "15LG Audit of records",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/crimes-legislation-amendment-serious-and-organised-crime-act-2010#sch-3-sec-15lg"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "crimes-legislation-amendment-serious-and-organised-crime-act-2010.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "crimes-legislation-amendment-serious-and-organised-crime-act-2010.pdf, p.139",
      "values:originalText": "(1) The chief officer of either a law enforcement agency or an\nintelligence agency must cause the records kept under\nsection 15LF for each authority in respect of the agency to be\naudited:\n\n(a) at least once every 6 months while the authority is in force;\nand\n\n(b) at least once in the 6 months after the cancellation or expiry\nof the authority.\n\n(2) The audit is to be conducted by a person appointed by the chief\nofficer.\n\n(3) The person appointed to conduct the audit:\n\n(a) may, but need not be, an officer of the agency; and\n\n(b) must not be a person:\n\n(i) who granted, varied or cancelled any of the authorities\nto which the records under section 15LF relate; or\n\n(ii) to whom control of any of the authorities to which the\nrecords under section 15LF relate was transferred; or\n\n(iii) who is or was an authorised person under any of the\nauthorities to which those records relate.\n\n(4) The results of an audit must be reported to the chief officer.",
      "skos:definition": "(1) The chief officer of either a law enforcement agency or an\nintelligence agency must cause the records kept under\nsection 15LF for each authority in respect of the agency to be\naudited:\n\n(a) at least once every 6 months while the authority is in force;\nand\n\n(b) at least once in the 6 months after the cancellation or expiry\nof the authority.\n\n(2) The audit is to be conducted by a person appointed by the chief\nofficer.\n\n(3) The person appointed to conduct the audit:\n\n(a) may, but need not be, an officer of the agency; and\n\n(b) must not be a person:\n\n(i) who granted, varied or cancelled any of the authorities\nto which the records under section 15LF relate; or\n\n(ii) to whom control of any of the authorities to which the\nrecords under section 15LF relate was transferred; or\n\n(iii) who is or was an authorised person under any of the\nauthorities to which those records relate.\n\n(4) The results of an audit must be reported to the chief officer.",
      "cml:hasPart": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:crimes-legislation-amendment-serious-and-organised-crime-act-2010-sch-3-sec-15lg-ss-1"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:crimes-legislation-amendment-serious-and-organised-crime-act-2010-sch-3-sec-15lg-ss-2"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:crimes-legislation-amendment-serious-and-organised-crime-act-2010-sch-3-sec-15lg-ss-3"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:crimes-legislation-amendment-serious-and-organised-crime-act-2010-sch-3-sec-15lg-ss-4"
        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "8bb259aa39c0cf2ba4a0d640d86be85018f6279e24901bc2c5f0b2a3c779bc29"
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/crimes-legislation-amendment-serious-and-organised-crime-act-2010#sch-3-sec-15lg",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "15LG Audit of records",
      "values:kind": "section",
      "cof:pageNumber": 139,
      "values:originalText": "(1) The chief officer of either a law enforcement agency or an\nintelligence agency must cause the records kept under\nsection 15LF for each authority in respect of the agency to be\naudited:\n\n(a) at least once every 6 months while the authority is in force;\nand\n\n(b) at least once in the 6 months after the cancellation or expiry\nof the authority.\n\n(2) The audit is to be conducted by a person appointed by the chief\nofficer.\n\n(3) The person appointed to conduct the audit:\n\n(a) may, but need not be, an officer of the agency; and\n\n(b) must not be a person:\n\n(i) who granted, varied or cancelled any of the authorities\nto which the records under section 15LF relate; or\n\n(ii) to whom control of any of the authorities to which the\nrecords under section 15LF relate was transferred; or\n\n(iii) who is or was an authorised person under any of the\nauthorities to which those records relate.\n\n(4) The results of an audit must be reported to the chief officer."
    },
