    {
      "@id": "concept:crimes-legislation-amendment-serious-and-organised-crime-act-2010-sch-3-sec-15lh",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "15LH Delegation of chief officer’s functions",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/crimes-legislation-amendment-serious-and-organised-crime-act-2010#sch-3-sec-15lh"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "crimes-legislation-amendment-serious-and-organised-crime-act-2010.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "crimes-legislation-amendment-serious-and-organised-crime-act-2010.pdf, p.139",
      "values:originalText": "(1) Except as provided by this section (and despite any other Act or\nlaw to the contrary) the functions of a chief officer under this Part\nmay not be delegated to any other person.\n\n(2) A chief officer may delegate to a senior officer of the law\nenforcement agency or the intelligence agency (as the case may be)\nany of the chief officer’s functions under this Part relating to the\ngranting, variation, cancellation and transfer of control of\nauthorities (including, but not limited to conducting reviews under\nsection 15KF, making applications under section 15KG, giving\ndirections under section 15KL and making requests under\nsection 15KI or 15KX).\nComLaw Authoritative Act C2012C00115\n\nSchedule 3  Amendments relating to controlled operations, assumed identities and\nwitness identity protection",
      "skos:definition": "(1) Except as provided by this section (and despite any other Act or\nlaw to the contrary) the functions of a chief officer under this Part\nmay not be delegated to any other person.\n\n(2) A chief officer may delegate to a senior officer of the law\nenforcement agency or the intelligence agency (as the case may be)\nany of the chief officer’s functions under this Part relating to the\ngranting, variation, cancellation and transfer of control of\nauthorities (including, but not limited to conducting reviews under\nsection 15KF, making applications under section 15KG, giving\ndirections under section 15KL and making requests under\nsection 15KI or 15KX).\nComLaw Authoritative Act C2012C00115\n\nSchedule 3  Amendments relating to controlled operations, assumed identities and\nwitness identity protection",
      "cml:hasPart": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:crimes-legislation-amendment-serious-and-organised-crime-act-2010-sch-3-sec-15lh-ss-1"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:crimes-legislation-amendment-serious-and-organised-crime-act-2010-sch-3-sec-15lh-ss-2"
        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "e5d044699819cf529b19208041a3cb7e99f18a6828a2e400919daaa7f463c241"
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/crimes-legislation-amendment-serious-and-organised-crime-act-2010#sch-3-sec-15lh",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "15LH Delegation of chief officer’s functions",
      "values:kind": "section",
      "cof:pageNumber": 139,
      "values:originalText": "(1) Except as provided by this section (and despite any other Act or\nlaw to the contrary) the functions of a chief officer under this Part\nmay not be delegated to any other person.\n\n(2) A chief officer may delegate to a senior officer of the law\nenforcement agency or the intelligence agency (as the case may be)\nany of the chief officer’s functions under this Part relating to the\ngranting, variation, cancellation and transfer of control of\nauthorities (including, but not limited to conducting reviews under\nsection 15KF, making applications under section 15KG, giving\ndirections under section 15KL and making requests under\nsection 15KI or 15KX).\nComLaw Authoritative Act C2012C00115\n\nSchedule 3  Amendments relating to controlled operations, assumed identities and\nwitness identity protection"
    },
