    {
      "@id": "concept:crimes-legislation-amendment-serious-and-organised-crime-act-2010-sch-3-sec-15me",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "15ME Witness identity protection certificate",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/crimes-legislation-amendment-serious-and-organised-crime-act-2010#sch-3-sec-15me"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "crimes-legislation-amendment-serious-and-organised-crime-act-2010.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "crimes-legislation-amendment-serious-and-organised-crime-act-2010.pdf, p.145",
      "values:originalText": "(1) The chief officer of a law enforcement agency may give a witness\nidentity protection certificate for an operative in relation to a\nproceeding if:\n\n(a) the operative is, or may be required, to give evidence in the\nproceeding; and\nComLaw Authoritative Act C2012C00115\n\nSchedule 3  Amendments relating to controlled operations, assumed identities and\nwitness identity protection",
      "skos:definition": "(1) The chief officer of a law enforcement agency may give a witness\nidentity protection certificate for an operative in relation to a\nproceeding if:\n\n(a) the operative is, or may be required, to give evidence in the\nproceeding; and\nComLaw Authoritative Act C2012C00115\n\nSchedule 3  Amendments relating to controlled operations, assumed identities and\nwitness identity protection",
      "cml:asserts": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:crimes-legislation-amendment-serious-and-organised-crime-act-2010-sch-3-sec-15me-norm"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:crimes-legislation-amendment-serious-and-organised-crime-act-2010-sch-3-sec-15me-logic-deontic-1"
        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "c6b9583a860cd628032ae126f7533cc9213328aa04991b5a45cac5d939811582",
      "skos:note": "Chief officer may give witness identity protection certificate."
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/crimes-legislation-amendment-serious-and-organised-crime-act-2010#sch-3-sec-15me",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "15ME Witness identity protection certificate",
      "values:kind": "section",
      "cof:pageNumber": 145,
      "values:originalText": "(1) The chief officer of a law enforcement agency may give a witness\nidentity protection certificate for an operative in relation to a\nproceeding if:\n\n(a) the operative is, or may be required, to give evidence in the\nproceeding; and\nComLaw Authoritative Act C2012C00115\n\nSchedule 3  Amendments relating to controlled operations, assumed identities and\nwitness identity protection"
    },
    {
      "@id": "concept:crimes-legislation-amendment-serious-and-organised-crime-act-2010-sch-3-sec-15me-norm",
      "@type": "values:Obligation",
      "cml:modality": {
        "@id": "cml:Deontic"
      },
      "values:partOf": {
        "@id": "concept:crimes-legislation-amendment-serious-and-organised-crime-act-2010-sch-3-sec-15me"
      },
      "values:deonticStatus": {
        "@id": "values:HeuristicDerived"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "values:borneBy": {
        "@id": "values:State"
      },
      "skos:scopeNote": "borne by: State"
    },
    {
      "@id": "concept:crimes-legislation-amendment-serious-and-organised-crime-act-2010-sch-3-sec-15me-logic-deontic-1",
      "@type": "cml:LogicApplication",
      "cml:modality": {
        "@id": "cml:Deontic"
      },
      "cml:operator": "may",
      "cml:logicSummary": "Granting of obligation",
      "cml:executionSurface": "modalities::logic::deontic",
      "cml:confidence": {
        "@value": 1.0,
        "@type": "xsd:decimal"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      }
    },
    {
      "@id": "concept:crimes-legislation-amendment-serious-and-organised-crime-act-2010-sch-3-sec-142",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "142 Crimes Legislation Amendment (Serious and Organised Crime) Act",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/crimes-legislation-amendment-serious-and-organised-crime-act-2010#sch-3-sec-142"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "crimes-legislation-amendment-serious-and-organised-crime-act-2010.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "crimes-legislation-amendment-serious-and-organised-crime-act-2010.pdf, p.146",
      "values:originalText": "(b) the chief officer is satisfied on reasonable grounds that the\ndisclosure in the proceeding of the operative’s identity or\nwhere the operative lives is likely to:\n\n(i) endanger the safety of the operative or another person;\nor\n\n(ii) prejudice any current or future investigation; or\n\n(iii) prejudice any current or future activity relating to\nsecurity.\n\n(2) The chief officer must make all reasonable enquiries to enable the\nchief officer to ascertain the information required to be included in\nthe certificate by section 15MG.\n\n(3) The chief officer cannot give a certificate for an operative until the\nchief officer has obtained a statutory declaration from the operative\nunder section 15MF.\nNote:\nThe chief officer may delegate functions under this section—see\nsection 15MX.\n\n(4) A decision to give a witness identity protection certificate:\n\n(a) is final; and\n\n(b) cannot be appealed against, reviewed, called into question,\nquashed or invalidated in any court.\n\n(5) Subsection (4) does not prevent a decision to give a witness\nidentity protection certificate being called into question in the\ncourse of any proceedings of a disciplinary nature against the\nperson who made the decision.\n\n(6) A witness identity protection certificate purporting to be issued\nunder subsection (1):\n\n(a) must be taken to be such a certificate and to have been\nproperly issued; and\n\n(b) is prima facie evidence of the matters in the certificate.\n\n(7) A witness identity protection certificate is not a legislative\ninstrument.\nComLaw Authoritative Act C2012C00115\n\nAmendments relating to controlled operations, assumed identities and witness identity\nprotection  Schedule 3\nMain amendments  Part 1\n\nCrimes Legislation Amendment (Serious and Organised Crime) Act 2010",
      "skos:definition": "(b) the chief officer is satisfied on reasonable grounds that the\ndisclosure in the proceeding of the operative’s identity or\nwhere the operative lives is likely to:\n\n(i) endanger the safety of the operative or another person;\nor\n\n(ii) prejudice any current or future investigation; or\n\n(iii) prejudice any current or future activity relating to\nsecurity.\n\n(2) The chief officer must make all reasonable enquiries to enable the\nchief officer to ascertain the information required to be included in\nthe certificate by section 15MG.\n\n(3) The chief officer cannot give a certificate for an operative until the\nchief officer has obtained a statutory declaration from the operative\nunder section 15MF.\nNote:\nThe chief officer may delegate functions under this section—see\nsection 15MX.\n\n(4) A decision to give a witness identity protection certificate:\n\n(a) is final; and\n\n(b) cannot be appealed against, reviewed, called into question,\nquashed or invalidated in any court.\n\n(5) Subsection (4) does not prevent a decision to give a witness\nidentity protection certificate being called into question in the\ncourse of any proceedings of a disciplinary nature against the\nperson who made the decision.\n\n(6) A witness identity protection certificate purporting to be issued\nunder subsection (1):\n\n(a) must be taken to be such a certificate and to have been\nproperly issued; and\n\n(b) is prima facie evidence of the matters in the certificate.\n\n(7) A witness identity protection certificate is not a legislative\ninstrument.\nComLaw Authoritative Act C2012C00115\n\nAmendments relating to controlled operations, assumed identities and witness identity\nprotection  Schedule 3\nMain amendments  Part 1\n\nCrimes Legislation Amendment (Serious and Organised Crime) Act 2010",
      "cml:hasPart": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:crimes-legislation-amendment-serious-and-organised-crime-act-2010-sch-3-sec-142-ss-2"
        },
