    },
    {
      "@id": "concept:crimes-legislation-amendment-serious-and-organised-crime-act-2010-sch-3-sec-15mf",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "15MF Statutory declaration by operative",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/crimes-legislation-amendment-serious-and-organised-crime-act-2010#sch-3-sec-15mf"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "crimes-legislation-amendment-serious-and-organised-crime-act-2010.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "crimes-legislation-amendment-serious-and-organised-crime-act-2010.pdf, p.147",
      "values:originalText": "(1) Before a witness identity protection certificate is given for an\noperative, the operative must make a statutory declaration of the\nfollowing matters:\n\n(a) whether the operative has been convicted or found guilty of\nan offence and, if so, particulars of each offence;\n\n(b) whether any charges against the operative for an offence are\npending or outstanding and, if so, particulars of each charge;\n\n(c) if the operative is or was a law enforcement officer:\n\n(i) whether the operative has been found guilty of\nprofessional misconduct and, if so, particulars of each\nfinding; and\n\n(ii) whether, to the operative’s knowledge, any allegations\nof professional misconduct against him or her are\noutstanding and, if so, particulars of each allegation;\n\n(d) whether, to the operative’s knowledge, a court has made any\nadverse comment about the operative’s credibility and, if so,\nparticulars of the comment;\n\n(e) whether the operative has made a false representation when\nthe truth was required and, if so, particulars of the\nrepresentation;\n\n(f) if there is anything else known to the operative that may be\nrelevant to the operative’s credibility—particulars of the\nthing.\n\n(2) Subject to subsection (3), a person cannot be compelled to disclose\nor produce a statutory declaration made under this section in any\nproceeding.\n\n(3) Subsection (2) does not apply to:\n\n(a) proceedings for perjury or otherwise in respect of the falsity\nof the statutory declaration; or\n\n(b) proceedings of a disciplinary nature against a law\nenforcement officer; or\n\n(c) investigations or inquiries by a person or body in any\njurisdiction having jurisdiction to investigate or inquire into\nthe conduct of a law enforcement officer.\nComLaw Authoritative Act C2012C00115\n\nSchedule 3  Amendments relating to controlled operations, assumed identities and\nwitness identity protection",
      "skos:definition": "(1) Before a witness identity protection certificate is given for an\noperative, the operative must make a statutory declaration of the\nfollowing matters:\n\n(a) whether the operative has been convicted or found guilty of\nan offence and, if so, particulars of each offence;\n\n(b) whether any charges against the operative for an offence are\npending or outstanding and, if so, particulars of each charge;\n\n(c) if the operative is or was a law enforcement officer:\n\n(i) whether the operative has been found guilty of\nprofessional misconduct and, if so, particulars of each\nfinding; and\n\n(ii) whether, to the operative’s knowledge, any allegations\nof professional misconduct against him or her are\noutstanding and, if so, particulars of each allegation;\n\n(d) whether, to the operative’s knowledge, a court has made any\nadverse comment about the operative’s credibility and, if so,\nparticulars of the comment;\n\n(e) whether the operative has made a false representation when\nthe truth was required and, if so, particulars of the\nrepresentation;\n\n(f) if there is anything else known to the operative that may be\nrelevant to the operative’s credibility—particulars of the\nthing.\n\n(2) Subject to subsection (3), a person cannot be compelled to disclose\nor produce a statutory declaration made under this section in any\nproceeding.\n\n(3) Subsection (2) does not apply to:\n\n(a) proceedings for perjury or otherwise in respect of the falsity\nof the statutory declaration; or\n\n(b) proceedings of a disciplinary nature against a law\nenforcement officer; or\n\n(c) investigations or inquiries by a person or body in any\njurisdiction having jurisdiction to investigate or inquire into\nthe conduct of a law enforcement officer.\nComLaw Authoritative Act C2012C00115\n\nSchedule 3  Amendments relating to controlled operations, assumed identities and\nwitness identity protection",
      "cml:hasPart": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:crimes-legislation-amendment-serious-and-organised-crime-act-2010-sch-3-sec-15mf-ss-1"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:crimes-legislation-amendment-serious-and-organised-crime-act-2010-sch-3-sec-15mf-ss-2"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:crimes-legislation-amendment-serious-and-organised-crime-act-2010-sch-3-sec-15mf-ss-3"
        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "b52e024dfa5ccbcdfd03c9e2551db093244a40a5af767b3ac864357f1ede161d"
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/crimes-legislation-amendment-serious-and-organised-crime-act-2010#sch-3-sec-15mf",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "15MF Statutory declaration by operative",
      "values:kind": "section",
      "cof:pageNumber": 147,
      "values:originalText": "(1) Before a witness identity protection certificate is given for an\noperative, the operative must make a statutory declaration of the\nfollowing matters:\n\n(a) whether the operative has been convicted or found guilty of\nan offence and, if so, particulars of each offence;\n\n(b) whether any charges against the operative for an offence are\npending or outstanding and, if so, particulars of each charge;\n\n(c) if the operative is or was a law enforcement officer:\n\n(i) whether the operative has been found guilty of\nprofessional misconduct and, if so, particulars of each\nfinding; and\n\n(ii) whether, to the operative’s knowledge, any allegations\nof professional misconduct against him or her are\noutstanding and, if so, particulars of each allegation;\n\n(d) whether, to the operative’s knowledge, a court has made any\nadverse comment about the operative’s credibility and, if so,\nparticulars of the comment;\n\n(e) whether the operative has made a false representation when\nthe truth was required and, if so, particulars of the\nrepresentation;\n\n(f) if there is anything else known to the operative that may be\nrelevant to the operative’s credibility—particulars of the\nthing.\n\n(2) Subject to subsection (3), a person cannot be compelled to disclose\nor produce a statutory declaration made under this section in any\nproceeding.\n\n(3) Subsection (2) does not apply to:\n\n(a) proceedings for perjury or otherwise in respect of the falsity\nof the statutory declaration; or\n\n(b) proceedings of a disciplinary nature against a law\nenforcement officer; or\n\n(c) investigations or inquiries by a person or body in any\njurisdiction having jurisdiction to investigate or inquire into\nthe conduct of a law enforcement officer.\nComLaw Authoritative Act C2012C00115\n\nSchedule 3  Amendments relating to controlled operations, assumed identities and\nwitness identity protection"
    },
