      "skos:note": "Court may make order to protect witness identity"
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/crimes-legislation-amendment-serious-and-organised-crime-act-2010#sch-3-sec-146-ss-1",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "146(1) Crimes Legislation Amendment (Serious and Organised Crime) Act",
      "values:kind": "subsection",
      "cof:pageNumber": 150,
      "values:originalText": "(1) The court in which a witness identity protection certificate is filed\nmay make any order it considers necessary or desirable to protect\nthe identity of the operative for whom the certificate is given or to\nprevent the disclosure of where the operative lives."
    },
