    {
      "@id": "concept:crimes-legislation-amendment-serious-and-organised-crime-act-2010-sch-3-sec-148-ss-5",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "148(5) Crimes Legislation Amendment (Serious and Organised Crime) Act",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/crimes-legislation-amendment-serious-and-organised-crime-act-2010#sch-3-sec-148-ss-5"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "crimes-legislation-amendment-serious-and-organised-crime-act-2010.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "crimes-legislation-amendment-serious-and-organised-crime-act-2010.pdf, p.152",
      "values:originalText": "(5) However, the court must not give leave or make an order unless it\nis satisfied about each of the following:\n\n(a) there is evidence that, if accepted, would substantially call\ninto question the operative’s credibility;\n\n(b) it would be impractical to test properly the credibility of the\noperative without allowing the risk of disclosure of, or\ndisclosing, the operative’s identity or where the operative\nlives;\n\n(c) it is in the interests of justice for the operative’s credibility to\nbe able to be tested.",
      "skos:definition": "(5) However, the court must not give leave or make an order unless it\nis satisfied about each of the following:\n\n(a) there is evidence that, if accepted, would substantially call\ninto question the operative’s credibility;\n\n(b) it would be impractical to test properly the credibility of the\noperative without allowing the risk of disclosure of, or\ndisclosing, the operative’s identity or where the operative\nlives;\n\n(c) it is in the interests of justice for the operative’s credibility to\nbe able to be tested.",
      "values:partOf": {
        "@id": "concept:crimes-legislation-amendment-serious-and-organised-crime-act-2010-sch-3-sec-148"
      },
      "cml:asserts": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:crimes-legislation-amendment-serious-and-organised-crime-act-2010-sch-3-sec-148-ss-5-norm"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:crimes-legislation-amendment-serious-and-organised-crime-act-2010-sch-3-sec-148-ss-5-logic-deontic-1"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:crimes-legislation-amendment-serious-and-organised-crime-act-2010-sch-3-sec-148-ss-5-logic-epistemic-2"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:crimes-legislation-amendment-serious-and-organised-crime-act-2010-sch-3-sec-148-ss-5-logic-ltl-3"
        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "2e97e7ce4afc8d66d5443cb4f538efd092735d6172d5da0e47485cce5dd86374",
      "skos:note": "Court must be satisfied about evidence before giving leave or making an order regarding operative's credibility."
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/crimes-legislation-amendment-serious-and-organised-crime-act-2010#sch-3-sec-148-ss-5",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "148(5) Crimes Legislation Amendment (Serious and Organised Crime) Act",
      "values:kind": "subsection",
      "cof:pageNumber": 152,
      "values:originalText": "(5) However, the court must not give leave or make an order unless it\nis satisfied about each of the following:\n\n(a) there is evidence that, if accepted, would substantially call\ninto question the operative’s credibility;\n\n(b) it would be impractical to test properly the credibility of the\noperative without allowing the risk of disclosure of, or\ndisclosing, the operative’s identity or where the operative\nlives;\n\n(c) it is in the interests of justice for the operative’s credibility to\nbe able to be tested."
    },
