          "@id": "concept:crimes-legislation-amendment-serious-and-organised-crime-act-2010-sch-3-sec-148-ss-7-logic-deontic-1"
        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "eea9bb8fd2cb14ecefb7c88a4175c704878c13b717479971e7c646c13f8a9395",
      "skos:note": "Court must be closed during proceedings."
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/crimes-legislation-amendment-serious-and-organised-crime-act-2010#sch-3-sec-148-ss-7",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "148(7) Crimes Legislation Amendment (Serious and Organised Crime) Act",
      "values:kind": "subsection",
      "cof:pageNumber": 152,
      "values:originalText": "(7) Unless the court considers that the interests of justice require\notherwise, the court must be closed when:\n\n(a) the application is made; and\n\n(b) if leave is given or an order is made—the question is asked\n(and answered), the evidence is given, the information is\nprovided or the statement is made."
    },
