        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:crimes-legislation-amendment-serious-and-organised-crime-act-2010-sch-3-sec-148-ss-8-logic-deontic-1"
        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "f422276aa9b3cb5c5ca6eb6a87e9ddc4aa8cda71157cf12289d86a21c4778e67",
      "skos:note": "Court must suppress publication of certain information."
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/crimes-legislation-amendment-serious-and-organised-crime-act-2010#sch-3-sec-148-ss-8",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "148(8) Crimes Legislation Amendment (Serious and Organised Crime) Act",
      "values:kind": "subsection",
      "cof:pageNumber": 152,
      "values:originalText": "(8) The court must make an order suppressing the publication of\nanything said when:\n\n(a) the application is made; and\n\n(b) if leave is given or an order is made—the question is asked\n(and answered), the evidence is given, the information is\nprovided or the statement is made.\nComLaw Authoritative Act C2012C00115\n\nAmendments relating to controlled operations, assumed identities and witness identity\nprotection  Schedule 3\nMain amendments  Part 1\n\nCrimes Legislation Amendment (Serious and Organised Crime) Act 2010"
    },
