    {
      "@id": "concept:crimes-legislation-amendment-serious-and-organised-crime-act-2010-sch-3-sec-15mo",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "15MO Directions to jury",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/crimes-legislation-amendment-serious-and-organised-crime-act-2010#sch-3-sec-15mo"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "crimes-legislation-amendment-serious-and-organised-crime-act-2010.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "crimes-legislation-amendment-serious-and-organised-crime-act-2010.pdf, p.154",
      "values:originalText": "(1) This section applies if:\n\n(a) a witness identity protection certificate for an operative in\nrelation to a proceeding is filed in a court; and\n\n(b) there is a jury in the proceeding; and\n\n(c) the operative gives evidence.\n\n(2) The court must (unless it considers it inappropriate) direct the jury\nnot to give the operative’s evidence any more or less weight, or\ndraw any adverse inferences against the defendant or another party\nto the proceeding, because:\n\n(a) there is a witness identity protection certificate for the\noperative; or\n\n(b) the court has made an order under section 15MK or\nsubsection 15MM(8), (9) or (10).",
      "skos:definition": "(1) This section applies if:\n\n(a) a witness identity protection certificate for an operative in\nrelation to a proceeding is filed in a court; and\n\n(b) there is a jury in the proceeding; and\n\n(c) the operative gives evidence.\n\n(2) The court must (unless it considers it inappropriate) direct the jury\nnot to give the operative’s evidence any more or less weight, or\ndraw any adverse inferences against the defendant or another party\nto the proceeding, because:\n\n(a) there is a witness identity protection certificate for the\noperative; or\n\n(b) the court has made an order under section 15MK or\nsubsection 15MM(8), (9) or (10).",
      "cml:hasPart": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:crimes-legislation-amendment-serious-and-organised-crime-act-2010-sch-3-sec-15mo-ss-1"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:crimes-legislation-amendment-serious-and-organised-crime-act-2010-sch-3-sec-15mo-ss-2"
        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "9ad434b61712d375dac968bf7b1418efad32b2d484c8ab872356981e190eb8a4"
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/crimes-legislation-amendment-serious-and-organised-crime-act-2010#sch-3-sec-15mo",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "15MO Directions to jury",
      "values:kind": "section",
      "cof:pageNumber": 154,
      "values:originalText": "(1) This section applies if:\n\n(a) a witness identity protection certificate for an operative in\nrelation to a proceeding is filed in a court; and\n\n(b) there is a jury in the proceeding; and\n\n(c) the operative gives evidence.\n\n(2) The court must (unless it considers it inappropriate) direct the jury\nnot to give the operative’s evidence any more or less weight, or\ndraw any adverse inferences against the defendant or another party\nto the proceeding, because:\n\n(a) there is a witness identity protection certificate for the\noperative; or\n\n(b) the court has made an order under section 15MK or\nsubsection 15MM(8), (9) or (10)."
    },
