    {
      "@id": "concept:crimes-legislation-amendment-serious-and-organised-crime-act-2010-sch-3-sec-15mp-ss-4",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "15MP(4) Appeals and adjournments",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/crimes-legislation-amendment-serious-and-organised-crime-act-2010#sch-3-sec-15mp-ss-4"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "crimes-legislation-amendment-serious-and-organised-crime-act-2010.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "crimes-legislation-amendment-serious-and-organised-crime-act-2010.pdf, p.154",
      "values:originalText": "(4) If a party to the proceedings appeals against the decision to give or\nrefuse leave, or to make or refuse to make the order, the appeal\ncourt may allow the operative to whom the certificate relates, or\nthe chief officer who gave the certificate, to join the appeal as a\nrespondent, if the appeal court is satisfied that the operative or\nchief officer has a sufficient interest in the decision.",
      "skos:definition": "(4) If a party to the proceedings appeals against the decision to give or\nrefuse leave, or to make or refuse to make the order, the appeal\ncourt may allow the operative to whom the certificate relates, or\nthe chief officer who gave the certificate, to join the appeal as a\nrespondent, if the appeal court is satisfied that the operative or\nchief officer has a sufficient interest in the decision.",
      "values:partOf": {
        "@id": "concept:crimes-legislation-amendment-serious-and-organised-crime-act-2010-sch-3-sec-15mp"
      },
      "cml:asserts": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:crimes-legislation-amendment-serious-and-organised-crime-act-2010-sch-3-sec-15mp-ss-4-norm"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:crimes-legislation-amendment-serious-and-organised-crime-act-2010-sch-3-sec-15mp-ss-4-logic-deontic-1"
        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "84b1ff852595cf4c637ee7b2ac4c1b95c1b70f5d837a69993b08cffc16aec9fe",
      "skos:note": "Allow operative or chief officer to join appeal if they have a sufficient interest in the decision."
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/crimes-legislation-amendment-serious-and-organised-crime-act-2010#sch-3-sec-15mp-ss-4",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "15MP(4) Appeals and adjournments",
      "values:kind": "subsection",
      "cof:pageNumber": 154,
      "values:originalText": "(4) If a party to the proceedings appeals against the decision to give or\nrefuse leave, or to make or refuse to make the order, the appeal\ncourt may allow the operative to whom the certificate relates, or\nthe chief officer who gave the certificate, to join the appeal as a\nrespondent, if the appeal court is satisfied that the operative or\nchief officer has a sufficient interest in the decision."
    },
