    {
      "@id": "concept:crimes-legislation-amendment-serious-and-organised-crime-act-2010-sch-3-sec-15mq",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "15MQ Witness identity protection certificate—cancellation",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/crimes-legislation-amendment-serious-and-organised-crime-act-2010#sch-3-sec-15mq"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "crimes-legislation-amendment-serious-and-organised-crime-act-2010.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "crimes-legislation-amendment-serious-and-organised-crime-act-2010.pdf, p.155",
      "values:originalText": "(1) This section applies if the chief officer of a law enforcement\nagency gives a witness identity protection certificate for an\noperative in relation to a proceeding.\n\n(2) The chief officer must cancel the witness identity protection\ncertificate if the chief officer considers that it is no longer\nnecessary or appropriate to prevent the disclosure of the\noperative’s identity or where the operative lives.\n\n(3) If the chief officer cancels the certificate after it has been filed in a\ncourt, the chief officer must immediately give notice to the court\nand each party to the proceeding, in writing, that the certificate has\nbeen cancelled.\nNote:\nThe chief officer may delegate functions under this section—see\nsection 15MX.\nComLaw Authoritative Act C2012C00115\n\nSchedule 3  Amendments relating to controlled operations, assumed identities and\nwitness identity protection",
      "skos:definition": "(1) This section applies if the chief officer of a law enforcement\nagency gives a witness identity protection certificate for an\noperative in relation to a proceeding.\n\n(2) The chief officer must cancel the witness identity protection\ncertificate if the chief officer considers that it is no longer\nnecessary or appropriate to prevent the disclosure of the\noperative’s identity or where the operative lives.\n\n(3) If the chief officer cancels the certificate after it has been filed in a\ncourt, the chief officer must immediately give notice to the court\nand each party to the proceeding, in writing, that the certificate has\nbeen cancelled.\nNote:\nThe chief officer may delegate functions under this section—see\nsection 15MX.\nComLaw Authoritative Act C2012C00115\n\nSchedule 3  Amendments relating to controlled operations, assumed identities and\nwitness identity protection",
      "cml:hasPart": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:crimes-legislation-amendment-serious-and-organised-crime-act-2010-sch-3-sec-15mq-ss-1"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:crimes-legislation-amendment-serious-and-organised-crime-act-2010-sch-3-sec-15mq-ss-2"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:crimes-legislation-amendment-serious-and-organised-crime-act-2010-sch-3-sec-15mq-ss-3"
        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "cda88dc65c400e109236efbd12f38986d50dd0177a85165506ab747017ceb745"
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/crimes-legislation-amendment-serious-and-organised-crime-act-2010#sch-3-sec-15mq",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "15MQ Witness identity protection certificate—cancellation",
      "values:kind": "section",
      "cof:pageNumber": 155,
      "values:originalText": "(1) This section applies if the chief officer of a law enforcement\nagency gives a witness identity protection certificate for an\noperative in relation to a proceeding.\n\n(2) The chief officer must cancel the witness identity protection\ncertificate if the chief officer considers that it is no longer\nnecessary or appropriate to prevent the disclosure of the\noperative’s identity or where the operative lives.\n\n(3) If the chief officer cancels the certificate after it has been filed in a\ncourt, the chief officer must immediately give notice to the court\nand each party to the proceeding, in writing, that the certificate has\nbeen cancelled.\nNote:\nThe chief officer may delegate functions under this section—see\nsection 15MX.\nComLaw Authoritative Act C2012C00115\n\nSchedule 3  Amendments relating to controlled operations, assumed identities and\nwitness identity protection"
    },
