    {
      "@id": "concept:crimes-legislation-amendment-serious-and-organised-crime-act-2010-sch-3-sec-15mq-ss-3",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "15MQ(3) Witness identity protection certificate—cancellation",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/crimes-legislation-amendment-serious-and-organised-crime-act-2010#sch-3-sec-15mq-ss-3"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "crimes-legislation-amendment-serious-and-organised-crime-act-2010.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "crimes-legislation-amendment-serious-and-organised-crime-act-2010.pdf, p.155",
      "values:originalText": "(3) If the chief officer cancels the certificate after it has been filed in a\ncourt, the chief officer must immediately give notice to the court\nand each party to the proceeding, in writing, that the certificate has\nbeen cancelled.\nNote:\nThe chief officer may delegate functions under this section—see\nsection 15MX.\nComLaw Authoritative Act C2012C00115\n\nSchedule 3  Amendments relating to controlled operations, assumed identities and\nwitness identity protection",
      "skos:definition": "(3) If the chief officer cancels the certificate after it has been filed in a\ncourt, the chief officer must immediately give notice to the court\nand each party to the proceeding, in writing, that the certificate has\nbeen cancelled.\nNote:\nThe chief officer may delegate functions under this section—see\nsection 15MX.\nComLaw Authoritative Act C2012C00115\n\nSchedule 3  Amendments relating to controlled operations, assumed identities and\nwitness identity protection",
      "values:partOf": {
        "@id": "concept:crimes-legislation-amendment-serious-and-organised-crime-act-2010-sch-3-sec-15mq"
      },
      "cml:asserts": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:crimes-legislation-amendment-serious-and-organised-crime-act-2010-sch-3-sec-15mq-ss-3-norm"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:crimes-legislation-amendment-serious-and-organised-crime-act-2010-sch-3-sec-15mq-ss-3-logic-deontic-1"
        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "410c7a3cca0e78dfc425cfa9a1c64cbc04d0436793098cde30aedfb59786683d",
      "skos:note": "Chief officer must give notice to court and parties if certificate is cancelled.",
      "dc:description": "Notice in writing"
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/crimes-legislation-amendment-serious-and-organised-crime-act-2010#sch-3-sec-15mq-ss-3",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "15MQ(3) Witness identity protection certificate—cancellation",
      "values:kind": "subsection",
      "cof:pageNumber": 155,
      "values:originalText": "(3) If the chief officer cancels the certificate after it has been filed in a\ncourt, the chief officer must immediately give notice to the court\nand each party to the proceeding, in writing, that the certificate has\nbeen cancelled.\nNote:\nThe chief officer may delegate functions under this section—see\nsection 15MX.\nComLaw Authoritative Act C2012C00115\n\nSchedule 3  Amendments relating to controlled operations, assumed identities and\nwitness identity protection"
    },
