    {
      "@id": "concept:crimes-legislation-amendment-serious-and-organised-crime-act-2010-sch-3-sec-15mr",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "15MR Permission to give information disclosing operative’s identity",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/crimes-legislation-amendment-serious-and-organised-crime-act-2010#sch-3-sec-15mr"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "crimes-legislation-amendment-serious-and-organised-crime-act-2010.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "crimes-legislation-amendment-serious-and-organised-crime-act-2010.pdf, p.156",
      "values:originalText": "etc.\n\n(1) This section applies if the chief officer of a law enforcement\nagency gives a witness identity protection certificate for an\noperative in relation to a proceeding.\n\n(2) The chief officer may, in writing, permit a person to give\ninformation (otherwise than in the proceeding) that discloses, or\nmay lead to the disclosure of, the operative’s identity or where the\noperative lives if the chief officer considers it necessary or\nappropriate for the information to be given.\n\n(3) The permission:\n\n(a) must name the person who may give the information; and\n\n(b) must name the person to whom the information may be\ngiven; and\n\n(c) must state the information that may be given; and\n\n(d) may state how the information may be given.\nNote:\nThe chief officer may delegate functions under this section—see\nsection 15MX.",
      "skos:definition": "etc.\n\n(1) This section applies if the chief officer of a law enforcement\nagency gives a witness identity protection certificate for an\noperative in relation to a proceeding.\n\n(2) The chief officer may, in writing, permit a person to give\ninformation (otherwise than in the proceeding) that discloses, or\nmay lead to the disclosure of, the operative’s identity or where the\noperative lives if the chief officer considers it necessary or\nappropriate for the information to be given.\n\n(3) The permission:\n\n(a) must name the person who may give the information; and\n\n(b) must name the person to whom the information may be\ngiven; and\n\n(c) must state the information that may be given; and\n\n(d) may state how the information may be given.\nNote:\nThe chief officer may delegate functions under this section—see\nsection 15MX.",
      "cml:hasPart": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:crimes-legislation-amendment-serious-and-organised-crime-act-2010-sch-3-sec-15mr-ss-1"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:crimes-legislation-amendment-serious-and-organised-crime-act-2010-sch-3-sec-15mr-ss-2"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:crimes-legislation-amendment-serious-and-organised-crime-act-2010-sch-3-sec-15mr-ss-3"
        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "41b387a9617d9ffde9dc713bb94531bfc48d834db2fdc78d61c2040332d7bd35"
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/crimes-legislation-amendment-serious-and-organised-crime-act-2010#sch-3-sec-15mr",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "15MR Permission to give information disclosing operative’s identity",
      "values:kind": "section",
      "cof:pageNumber": 156,
      "values:originalText": "etc.\n\n(1) This section applies if the chief officer of a law enforcement\nagency gives a witness identity protection certificate for an\noperative in relation to a proceeding.\n\n(2) The chief officer may, in writing, permit a person to give\ninformation (otherwise than in the proceeding) that discloses, or\nmay lead to the disclosure of, the operative’s identity or where the\noperative lives if the chief officer considers it necessary or\nappropriate for the information to be given.\n\n(3) The permission:\n\n(a) must name the person who may give the information; and\n\n(b) must name the person to whom the information may be\ngiven; and\n\n(c) must state the information that may be given; and\n\n(d) may state how the information may be given.\nNote:\nThe chief officer may delegate functions under this section—see\nsection 15MX."
    },
