          "@id": "concept:crimes-legislation-amendment-serious-and-organised-crime-act-2010-sch-3-sec-15mr-ss-2-norm"
        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "ee3187068f741dca28ebb14eb3c8a5ee04c7191d2c4ce29a529e37ba52174fea",
      "skos:note": "Chief officer may permit person to give information disclosing operative's identity."
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/crimes-legislation-amendment-serious-and-organised-crime-act-2010#sch-3-sec-15mr-ss-2",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "15MR(2) Permission to give information disclosing operative’s identity",
      "values:kind": "subsection",
      "cof:pageNumber": 156,
      "values:originalText": "(2) The chief officer may, in writing, permit a person to give\ninformation (otherwise than in the proceeding) that discloses, or\nmay lead to the disclosure of, the operative’s identity or where the\noperative lives if the chief officer considers it necessary or\nappropriate for the information to be given."
    },
