    {
      "@id": "concept:crimes-legislation-amendment-serious-and-organised-crime-act-2010-sch-3-sec-15ms",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "15MS Disclosure offences",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/crimes-legislation-amendment-serious-and-organised-crime-act-2010#sch-3-sec-15ms"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "crimes-legislation-amendment-serious-and-organised-crime-act-2010.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "crimes-legislation-amendment-serious-and-organised-crime-act-2010.pdf, p.156",
      "values:originalText": "(1) A person commits an offence if:\n\n(a) a witness identity protection certificate for an operative in\nrelation to a proceeding has been given; and\n\n(b) the certificate has not been cancelled under section 15MQ;\nand\n\n(c) the person engages in conduct; and\n\n(d) the conduct results in the disclosure of the operative’s\nidentity or where the operative lives; and\n\n(e) none of the following applies:\n\n(i) the conduct is required by section 15ML;\n\n(ii) the conduct is authorised by leave or by an order under\nsection 15MM;\n\n(iii) the conduct is permitted under section 15MR.\nPenalty: Imprisonment for 2 years.\n\n(2) A person commits an offence if:\nComLaw Authoritative Act C2012C00115\n\nAmendments relating to controlled operations, assumed identities and witness identity\nprotection  Schedule 3\nMain amendments  Part 1\n\nCrimes Legislation Amendment (Serious and Organised Crime) Act 2010\n\n(a) a witness identity protection certificate for an operative in\nrelation to a proceeding has been given; and\n\n(b) the certificate has not been cancelled under section 15MQ;\nand\n\n(c) the person engages in conduct; and\n\n(d) the conduct results in the disclosure of the operative’s\nidentity or where the operative lives; and\n\n(e) none of the following applies:\n\n(i) the conduct is required by section 15ML;\n\n(ii) the conduct is authorised by leave or by an order under\nsection 15MM;\n\n(iii) the conduct is permitted under section 15MR; and\n\n(f) the person is reckless as to whether his or her conduct will\nendanger the health or safety of another person.\nPenalty: Imprisonment for 10 years.\n\n(3) A person commits an offence if:\n\n(a) a witness identity protection certificate for an operative in\nrelation to a proceeding has been given; and\n\n(b) the certificate has not been cancelled under section 15MQ;\nand\n\n(c) the person engages in conduct; and\n\n(d) the conduct results in the disclosure of the operative’s\nidentity or where the operative lives; and\n\n(e) none of the following applies:\n\n(i) the conduct is required by section 15ML;\n\n(ii) the conduct is authorised by leave or by an order under\nsection 15MM;\n\n(iii) the conduct is permitted under section 15MR; and\n\n(f) the person is reckless as to whether his or her conduct will:\n\n(i) prejudice any current or future investigation; or\n\n(ii) prejudice any current or future activity relating to\nsecurity.\nPenalty: Imprisonment for 10 years.\nComLaw Authoritative Act C2012C00115\n\nSchedule 3  Amendments relating to controlled operations, assumed identities and\nwitness identity protection",
      "skos:definition": "(1) A person commits an offence if:\n\n(a) a witness identity protection certificate for an operative in\nrelation to a proceeding has been given; and\n\n(b) the certificate has not been cancelled under section 15MQ;\nand\n\n(c) the person engages in conduct; and\n\n(d) the conduct results in the disclosure of the operative’s\nidentity or where the operative lives; and\n\n(e) none of the following applies:\n\n(i) the conduct is required by section 15ML;\n\n(ii) the conduct is authorised by leave or by an order under\nsection 15MM;\n\n(iii) the conduct is permitted under section 15MR.\nPenalty: Imprisonment for 2 years.\n\n(2) A person commits an offence if:\nComLaw Authoritative Act C2012C00115\n\nAmendments relating to controlled operations, assumed identities and witness identity\nprotection  Schedule 3\nMain amendments  Part 1\n\nCrimes Legislation Amendment (Serious and Organised Crime) Act 2010\n\n(a) a witness identity protection certificate for an operative in\nrelation to a proceeding has been given; and\n\n(b) the certificate has not been cancelled under section 15MQ;\nand\n\n(c) the person engages in conduct; and\n\n(d) the conduct results in the disclosure of the operative’s\nidentity or where the operative lives; and\n\n(e) none of the following applies:\n\n(i) the conduct is required by section 15ML;\n\n(ii) the conduct is authorised by leave or by an order under\nsection 15MM;\n\n(iii) the conduct is permitted under section 15MR; and\n\n(f) the person is reckless as to whether his or her conduct will\nendanger the health or safety of another person.\nPenalty: Imprisonment for 10 years.\n\n(3) A person commits an offence if:\n\n(a) a witness identity protection certificate for an operative in\nrelation to a proceeding has been given; and\n\n(b) the certificate has not been cancelled under section 15MQ;\nand\n\n(c) the person engages in conduct; and\n\n(d) the conduct results in the disclosure of the operative’s\nidentity or where the operative lives; and\n\n(e) none of the following applies:\n\n(i) the conduct is required ",
      "cml:hasPart": [
