    {
      "@id": "concept:crimes-legislation-amendment-serious-and-organised-crime-act-2010-sch-3-sec-15mt",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "15MT Evidentiary certificates",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/crimes-legislation-amendment-serious-and-organised-crime-act-2010#sch-3-sec-15mt"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "crimes-legislation-amendment-serious-and-organised-crime-act-2010.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "crimes-legislation-amendment-serious-and-organised-crime-act-2010.pdf, p.158",
      "values:originalText": "(1) A chief officer of a law enforcement agency may sign a certificate\nstating any of the following:\n\n(a) that, for the purposes of paragraph 15MS(1)(b), (2)(b) or\n(3)(b), a witness identity protection certificate for an\noperative in relation to a proceeding has not been cancelled\nunder section 15MQ;\n\n(b) whether, for the purposes of subparagraph 15MS(1)(e)(i),\n(2)(e)(i) or (3)(e)(i), the conduct that is the subject of the\noffence was required by section 15ML;\n\n(c) whether, for the purposes of subparagraph 15MS(1)(e)(ii),\n(2)(e)(ii) or (3)(e)(ii), the conduct that is the subject of the\noffence was authorised by leave or by an order under\nsection 15MM;\n\n(d) whether, for the purposes of subparagraph 15MS(1)(e)(iii),\n(2)(e)(iii) or (3)(e)(iii), the conduct that is the subject of the\noffence was permitted under section 15MR.\n\n(2) In any proceedings, a certificate given under this section is prima\nfacie evidence of the matters certified in it.",
      "skos:definition": "(1) A chief officer of a law enforcement agency may sign a certificate\nstating any of the following:\n\n(a) that, for the purposes of paragraph 15MS(1)(b), (2)(b) or\n(3)(b), a witness identity protection certificate for an\noperative in relation to a proceeding has not been cancelled\nunder section 15MQ;\n\n(b) whether, for the purposes of subparagraph 15MS(1)(e)(i),\n(2)(e)(i) or (3)(e)(i), the conduct that is the subject of the\noffence was required by section 15ML;\n\n(c) whether, for the purposes of subparagraph 15MS(1)(e)(ii),\n(2)(e)(ii) or (3)(e)(ii), the conduct that is the subject of the\noffence was authorised by leave or by an order under\nsection 15MM;\n\n(d) whether, for the purposes of subparagraph 15MS(1)(e)(iii),\n(2)(e)(iii) or (3)(e)(iii), the conduct that is the subject of the\noffence was permitted under section 15MR.\n\n(2) In any proceedings, a certificate given under this section is prima\nfacie evidence of the matters certified in it.",
      "cml:hasPart": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:crimes-legislation-amendment-serious-and-organised-crime-act-2010-sch-3-sec-15mt-ss-1"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:crimes-legislation-amendment-serious-and-organised-crime-act-2010-sch-3-sec-15mt-ss-2"
        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "00f6a7e9d7349778f7d995d3278d88ee13969a32d7ae6ce118643c86563daf38"
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/crimes-legislation-amendment-serious-and-organised-crime-act-2010#sch-3-sec-15mt",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "15MT Evidentiary certificates",
      "values:kind": "section",
      "cof:pageNumber": 158,
      "values:originalText": "(1) A chief officer of a law enforcement agency may sign a certificate\nstating any of the following:\n\n(a) that, for the purposes of paragraph 15MS(1)(b), (2)(b) or\n(3)(b), a witness identity protection certificate for an\noperative in relation to a proceeding has not been cancelled\nunder section 15MQ;\n\n(b) whether, for the purposes of subparagraph 15MS(1)(e)(i),\n(2)(e)(i) or (3)(e)(i), the conduct that is the subject of the\noffence was required by section 15ML;\n\n(c) whether, for the purposes of subparagraph 15MS(1)(e)(ii),\n(2)(e)(ii) or (3)(e)(ii), the conduct that is the subject of the\noffence was authorised by leave or by an order under\nsection 15MM;\n\n(d) whether, for the purposes of subparagraph 15MS(1)(e)(iii),\n(2)(e)(iii) or (3)(e)(iii), the conduct that is the subject of the\noffence was permitted under section 15MR.\n\n(2) In any proceedings, a certificate given under this section is prima\nfacie evidence of the matters certified in it."
    },
