    {
      "@id": "concept:crimes-legislation-amendment-serious-and-organised-crime-act-2010-sch-3-sec-12",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "12 Protection from criminal responsibility for conduct",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/crimes-legislation-amendment-serious-and-organised-crime-act-2010#sch-3-sec-12"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "crimes-legislation-amendment-serious-and-organised-crime-act-2010.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "crimes-legislation-amendment-serious-and-organised-crime-act-2010.pdf, p.163",
      "values:originalText": "engaged in before, on or after commencement under a\npre-commencement State authorisation\n(1)\nThis item applies to a participant in an operation authorised under a\nState controlled operations law if:\n\n(a) the operation was authorised before commencement; and\n\n(b) the participant engaged in conduct, whether before, on or\nafter commencement, in the course of, and for the purposes\nof, the operation; and\n\n(c) engaging in that conduct was a Commonwealth offence.\n(2)\nDespite any other law of the Commonwealth, the participant is not\ncriminally responsible for the Commonwealth offence, if:\n\n(a) the conduct was authorised by, and was engaged in in\naccordance with, the authority to conduct the controlled\noperation; and\n\n(b) the conduct did not involve the participant intentionally\ninducing a person to commit a Commonwealth offence or an\noffence against a law of a State or Territory that the person\nwould not otherwise have intended to commit; and\n\n(c) the conduct did not involve the participant engaging in any\nconduct that was likely to:\n\n(i) cause the death of, or serious injury to, any person; or\n\n(ii) involve the commission of a sexual offence against any\nperson; and\n\n(d) if the person is a civilian participant in the operation—he or\nshe acts in accordance with the instructions of a law\nenforcement officer.\n(3)\nExpressions used in this item have the same meanings as in the State\ncontrolled operations law under which the operation was authorised.",
      "skos:definition": "engaged in before, on or after commencement under a\npre-commencement State authorisation\n(1)\nThis item applies to a participant in an operation authorised under a\nState controlled operations law if:\n\n(a) the operation was authorised before commencement; and\n\n(b) the participant engaged in conduct, whether before, on or\nafter commencement, in the course of, and for the purposes\nof, the operation; and\n\n(c) engaging in that conduct was a Commonwealth offence.\n(2)\nDespite any other law of the Commonwealth, the participant is not\ncriminally responsible for the Commonwealth offence, if:\n\n(a) the conduct was authorised by, and was engaged in in\naccordance with, the authority to conduct the controlled\noperation; and\n\n(b) the conduct did not involve the participant intentionally\ninducing a person to commit a Commonwealth offence or an\noffence against a law of a State or Territory that the person\nwould not otherwise have intended to commit; and\n\n(c) the conduct did not involve the participant engaging in any\nconduct that was likely to:\n\n(i) cause the death of, or serious injury to, any person; or\n\n(ii) involve the commission of a sexual offence against any\nperson; and\n\n(d) if the person is a civilian participant in the operation—he or\nshe acts in accordance with the instructions of a law\nenforcement officer.\n(3)\nExpressions used in this item have the same meanings as in the State\ncontrolled operations law under which the operation was authorised.",
      "cml:asserts": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:crimes-legislation-amendment-serious-and-organised-crime-act-2010-sch-3-sec-12-norm"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:crimes-legislation-amendment-serious-and-organised-crime-act-2010-sch-3-sec-12-logic-deontic-1"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:crimes-legislation-amendment-serious-and-organised-crime-act-2010-sch-3-sec-12-logic-alleninterval-2"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:crimes-legislation-amendment-serious-and-organised-crime-act-2010-sch-3-sec-12-logic-ltl-3"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:crimes-legislation-amendment-serious-and-organised-crime-act-2010-sch-3-sec-12-logic-deontic-4"
        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "310a93124eb3d6f860b246db278744a9c390b2febb26b8678762861c76d31398",
      "skos:note": "Participant not criminally responsible for Commonwealth offence if conduct was authorized and met certain conditions."
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/crimes-legislation-amendment-serious-and-organised-crime-act-2010#sch-3-sec-12",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "12 Protection from criminal responsibility for conduct",
      "values:kind": "section",
      "cof:pageNumber": 163,
      "values:originalText": "engaged in before, on or after commencement under a\npre-commencement State authorisation\n(1)\nThis item applies to a participant in an operation authorised under a\nState controlled operations law if:\n\n(a) the operation was authorised before commencement; and\n\n(b) the participant engaged in conduct, whether before, on or\nafter commencement, in the course of, and for the purposes\nof, the operation; and\n\n(c) engaging in that conduct was a Commonwealth offence.\n(2)\nDespite any other law of the Commonwealth, the participant is not\ncriminally responsible for the Commonwealth offence, if:\n\n(a) the conduct was authorised by, and was engaged in in\naccordance with, the authority to conduct the controlled\noperation; and\n\n(b) the conduct did not involve the participant intentionally\ninducing a person to commit a Commonwealth offence or an\noffence against a law of a State or Territory that the person\nwould not otherwise have intended to commit; and\n\n(c) the conduct did not involve the participant engaging in any\nconduct that was likely to:\n\n(i) cause the death of, or serious injury to, any person; or\n\n(ii) involve the commission of a sexual offence against any\nperson; and\n\n(d) if the person is a civilian participant in the operation—he or\nshe acts in accordance with the instructions of a law\nenforcement officer.\n(3)\nExpressions used in this item have the same meanings as in the State\ncontrolled operations law under which the operation was authorised."
    },
    {
      "@id": "concept:crimes-legislation-amendment-serious-and-organised-crime-act-2010-sch-3-sec-12-norm",
