        "@type": "xsd:decimal"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:premiseText": "(f) electronic surveillance devices or telecommunications interception;",
      "cml:conclusionText": "No electronic surveillance."
    },
    {
      "@id": "concept:crimes-legislation-amendment-serious-and-organised-crime-act-2010-sch-3-sec-14",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "14 Protection from criminal responsibility for certain ancillary",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/crimes-legislation-amendment-serious-and-organised-crime-act-2010#sch-3-sec-14"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "crimes-legislation-amendment-serious-and-organised-crime-act-2010.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "crimes-legislation-amendment-serious-and-organised-crime-act-2010.pdf, p.164",
      "values:originalText": "conduct\n(1)\nThis item applies if:\n\n(a) a person engaged in conduct (the ancillary conduct), whether\nbefore, on or after commencement, that related to conduct\n(the related conduct) that:\n\n(i) was engaged in before, on or after commencement by\nanother person; and\n\n(ii) constituted an offence for which a person would, but for\nitem 12, be criminally responsible; and\n\n(b) engaging in the ancillary conduct was or is an ancillary\noffence (within the meaning of the Criminal Code) in\nrelation to the offence constituted by the related conduct.\n(2)\nDespite any law of the Commonwealth, the person who engaged in the\nancillary conduct is not criminally responsible for the ancillary offence\nif, at the time the person engaged in the ancillary conduct, he or she\nbelieved the related conduct was being engaged in, or would be engaged\nin, by a participant in an operation authorised before commencement\nunder a State controlled operations law.\n(3)\nExpressions used in this item have the same meanings as in the State\ncontrolled operations law under which the person believed the\ncontrolled conduct was being engaged in.",
      "skos:definition": "conduct\n(1)\nThis item applies if:\n\n(a) a person engaged in conduct (the ancillary conduct), whether\nbefore, on or after commencement, that related to conduct\n(the related conduct) that:\n\n(i) was engaged in before, on or after commencement by\nanother person; and\n\n(ii) constituted an offence for which a person would, but for\nitem 12, be criminally responsible; and\n\n(b) engaging in the ancillary conduct was or is an ancillary\noffence (within the meaning of the Criminal Code) in\nrelation to the offence constituted by the related conduct.\n(2)\nDespite any law of the Commonwealth, the person who engaged in the\nancillary conduct is not criminally responsible for the ancillary offence\nif, at the time the person engaged in the ancillary conduct, he or she\nbelieved the related conduct was being engaged in, or would be engaged\nin, by a participant in an operation authorised before commencement\nunder a State controlled operations law.\n(3)\nExpressions used in this item have the same meanings as in the State\ncontrolled operations law under which the person believed the\ncontrolled conduct was being engaged in.",
      "cml:asserts": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:crimes-legislation-amendment-serious-and-organised-crime-act-2010-sch-3-sec-14-norm"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:crimes-legislation-amendment-serious-and-organised-crime-act-2010-sch-3-sec-14-logic-deontic-1"
        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "78dcb4703d72493e74afccab6efac06f7e0773ad025171e13b53fc450155d2b0",
      "skos:note": "Protection from criminal responsibility for certain ancillary conduct"
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/crimes-legislation-amendment-serious-and-organised-crime-act-2010#sch-3-sec-14",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "14 Protection from criminal responsibility for certain ancillary",
      "values:kind": "section",
      "cof:pageNumber": 164,
      "values:originalText": "conduct\n(1)\nThis item applies if:\n\n(a) a person engaged in conduct (the ancillary conduct), whether\nbefore, on or after commencement, that related to conduct\n(the related conduct) that:\n\n(i) was engaged in before, on or after commencement by\nanother person; and\n\n(ii) constituted an offence for which a person would, but for\nitem 12, be criminally responsible; and\n\n(b) engaging in the ancillary conduct was or is an ancillary\noffence (within the meaning of the Criminal Code) in\nrelation to the offence constituted by the related conduct.\n(2)\nDespite any law of the Commonwealth, the person who engaged in the\nancillary conduct is not criminally responsible for the ancillary offence\nif, at the time the person engaged in the ancillary conduct, he or she\nbelieved the related conduct was being engaged in, or would be engaged\nin, by a participant in an operation authorised before commencement\nunder a State controlled operations law.\n(3)\nExpressions used in this item have the same meanings as in the State\ncontrolled operations law under which the person believed the\ncontrolled conduct was being engaged in."
    },
    {
      "@id": "concept:crimes-legislation-amendment-serious-and-organised-crime-act-2010-sch-3-sec-14-norm",
      "@type": "values:Obligation",
      "cml:modality": {
        "@id": "cml:Deontic"
      },
      "values:partOf": {
        "@id": "concept:crimes-legislation-amendment-serious-and-organised-crime-act-2010-sch-3-sec-14"
      },
      "values:deonticStatus": {
        "@id": "values:HeuristicDerived"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "values:borneBy": {
        "@id": "values:State"
      },
      "skos:scopeNote": "borne by: State"
    },
    {
      "@id": "concept:crimes-legislation-amendment-serious-and-organised-crime-act-2010-sch-3-sec-14-logic-deontic-1",
      "@type": "cml:LogicApplication",
      "cml:modality": {
        "@id": "cml:Deontic"
      },
      "cml:operator": "Obligation",
      "cml:logicSummary": "Obligation to protect from criminal responsibility",
      "cml:executionSurface": "modalities::logic::deontic",
      "cml:confidence": {
        "@value": 1.0,
        "@type": "xsd:decimal"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:premiseText": "State must provide protection",
      "cml:conclusionText": "Person is not criminally responsible for ancillary conduct"
    },
    {
      "@id": "concept:crimes-legislation-amendment-serious-and-organised-crime-act-2010-sch-3-sec-15",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "15 Evidence of authorities",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/crimes-legislation-amendment-serious-and-organised-crime-act-2010#sch-3-sec-15"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "crimes-legislation-amendment-serious-and-organised-crime-act-2010.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "crimes-legislation-amendment-serious-and-organised-crime-act-2010.pdf, p.164",
      "values:originalText": "A document purporting to be an authority granted under a State\ncontrolled operations law:\n\n(a) is admissible in any legal proceedings; and\nComLaw Authoritative Act C2012C00115\n\nAmendments relating to controlled operations, assumed identities and witness identity\nprotection  Schedule 3\nProvisions relating to pre-commencement authorisations under State controlled\noperations law  Part 2\n\nCrimes Legislation Amendment (Serious and Organised Crime) Act 2010\n\n(b) in the absence of evidence to the contrary, is proof in any\nproceedings (not being criminal or disciplinary proceedings\nagainst a law enforcement officer) that the person granting\nthe authority was satisfied of the facts he or she was required\nto be satisfied of to grant the authority.",
      "skos:definition": "A document purporting to be an authority granted under a State\ncontrolled operations law:\n\n(a) is admissible in any legal proceedings; and\nComLaw Authoritative Act C2012C00115\n\nAmendments relating to controlled operations, assumed identities and witness identity\nprotection  Schedule 3\nProvisions relating to pre-commencement authorisations under State controlled\noperations law  Part 2\n\nCrimes Legislation Amendment (Serious and Organised Crime) Act 2010\n\n(b) in the absence of evidence to the contrary, is proof in any\nproceedings (not being criminal or disciplinary proceedings\nagainst a law enforcement officer) that the person granting\nthe authority was satisfied of the facts he or she was required\nto be satisfied of to grant the authority.",
      "cml:asserts": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:crimes-legislation-amendment-serious-and-organised-crime-act-2010-sch-3-sec-15-norm"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:crimes-legislation-amendment-serious-and-organised-crime-act-2010-sch-3-sec-15-logic-deontic-1"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:crimes-legislation-amendment-serious-and-organised-crime-act-2010-sch-3-sec-15-logic-alleninterval-2"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:crimes-legislation-amendment-serious-and-organised-crime-act-2010-sch-3-sec-15-logic-ltl-3"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:crimes-legislation-amendment-serious-and-organised-crime-act-2010-sch-3-sec-15-logic-diffusion-4"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:crimes-legislation-amendment-serious-and-organised-crime-act-2010-sch-3-sec-15-logic-argumentation-5"
        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "0325dd52edb46af6a6adee56d3ac8e3cf5908cef0ee42ac071c4fe0cb2d5f65b",
      "skos:note": "A document purporting to be an authority granted under a State controlled operations law is admissible in any legal proceedings."
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/crimes-legislation-amendment-serious-and-organised-crime-act-2010#sch-3-sec-15",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "15 Evidence of authorities",
      "values:kind": "section",
      "cof:pageNumber": 164,
      "values:originalText": "A document purporting to be an authority granted under a State\ncontrolled operations law:\n\n(a) is admissible in any legal proceedings; and\nComLaw Authoritative Act C2012C00115\n\nAmendments relating to controlled operations, assumed identities and witness identity\nprotection  Schedule 3\nProvisions relating to pre-commencement authorisations under State controlled\noperations law  Part 2\n\nCrimes Legislation Amendment (Serious and Organised Crime) Act 2010\n\n(b) in the absence of evidence to the contrary, is proof in any\nproceedings (not being criminal or disciplinary proceedings\nagainst a law enforcement officer) that the person granting\nthe authority was satisfied of the facts he or she was required\nto be satisfied of to grant the authority."
    },
