    {
      "@id": "concept:crimes-legislation-amendment-serious-and-organised-crime-act-2010-sch-4-sec-166-ss-6",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "166(6) Crimes Legislation Amendment (Serious and Organised Crime) Act",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/crimes-legislation-amendment-serious-and-organised-crime-act-2010#sch-4-sec-166-ss-6"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "crimes-legislation-amendment-serious-and-organised-crime-act-2010.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "crimes-legislation-amendment-serious-and-organised-crime-act-2010.pdf, p.170",
      "values:originalText": "(6) A person cannot be found guilty of an offence because of the\noperation of this section if, before the conduct constituting any of\nthe physical elements of the joint offence concerned was engaged\nin, the person:\nComLaw Authoritative Act C2012C00115\n\nOther amendments  Schedule 4\nJoint commission  Part 1\n\nCrimes Legislation Amendment (Serious and Organised Crime) Act 2010\n\n(a) terminated his or her involvement; and\n\n(b) took all reasonable steps to prevent that conduct from being\nengaged in.\nPerson may be found guilty even if another party not prosecuted\netc.",
      "skos:definition": "(6) A person cannot be found guilty of an offence because of the\noperation of this section if, before the conduct constituting any of\nthe physical elements of the joint offence concerned was engaged\nin, the person:\nComLaw Authoritative Act C2012C00115\n\nOther amendments  Schedule 4\nJoint commission  Part 1\n\nCrimes Legislation Amendment (Serious and Organised Crime) Act 2010\n\n(a) terminated his or her involvement; and\n\n(b) took all reasonable steps to prevent that conduct from being\nengaged in.\nPerson may be found guilty even if another party not prosecuted\netc.",
      "values:partOf": {
        "@id": "concept:crimes-legislation-amendment-serious-and-organised-crime-act-2010-sch-4-sec-166"
      },
      "cml:asserts": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:crimes-legislation-amendment-serious-and-organised-crime-act-2010-sch-4-sec-166-ss-6-norm"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:crimes-legislation-amendment-serious-and-organised-crime-act-2010-sch-4-sec-166-ss-6-logic-deontic-1"
        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "bd17477117562a269bf11bb6929d69992b2a5dad14d76ac79e48681e67dd5da7",
      "skos:note": "A person cannot be found guilty of an offence if they terminated their involvement and took reasonable steps to prevent the conduct."
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/crimes-legislation-amendment-serious-and-organised-crime-act-2010#sch-4-sec-166-ss-6",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "166(6) Crimes Legislation Amendment (Serious and Organised Crime) Act",
      "values:kind": "subsection",
      "cof:pageNumber": 170,
      "values:originalText": "(6) A person cannot be found guilty of an offence because of the\noperation of this section if, before the conduct constituting any of\nthe physical elements of the joint offence concerned was engaged\nin, the person:\nComLaw Authoritative Act C2012C00115\n\nOther amendments  Schedule 4\nJoint commission  Part 1\n\nCrimes Legislation Amendment (Serious and Organised Crime) Act 2010\n\n(a) terminated his or her involvement; and\n\n(b) took all reasonable steps to prevent that conduct from being\nengaged in.\nPerson may be found guilty even if another party not prosecuted\netc."
    },
    {
      "@id": "concept:crimes-legislation-amendment-serious-and-organised-crime-act-2010-sch-4-sec-166-ss-6-norm",
      "@type": "values:Obligation",
      "cml:modality": {
        "@id": "cml:Deontic"
      },
      "values:partOf": {
        "@id": "concept:crimes-legislation-amendment-serious-and-organised-crime-act-2010-sch-4-sec-166-ss-6"
      },
      "values:deonticStatus": {
        "@id": "values:HeuristicDerived"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "values:borneBy": {
        "@id": "values:State"
      },
      "skos:scopeNote": "borne by: State"
    },
    {
      "@id": "concept:crimes-legislation-amendment-serious-and-organised-crime-act-2010-sch-4-sec-166-ss-6-logic-deontic-1",
      "@type": "cml:LogicApplication",
      "cml:modality": {
        "@id": "cml:Deontic"
      },
      "cml:operator": "Cannot",
      "cml:logicSummary": "Prohibition on being found guilty",
      "cml:executionSurface": "modalities::logic::deontic",
      "cml:confidence": {
        "@value": 1.0,
        "@type": "xsd:decimal"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:premiseText": "Terminated involvement and prevention steps taken",
      "cml:conclusionText": "Guilty verdict not possible"
    },
    {
      "@id": "concept:crimes-legislation-amendment-serious-and-organised-crime-act-2010-sch-4-sec-166-ss-7",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "166(7) Crimes Legislation Amendment (Serious and Organised Crime) Act",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/crimes-legislation-amendment-serious-and-organised-crime-act-2010#sch-4-sec-166-ss-7"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "crimes-legislation-amendment-serious-and-organised-crime-act-2010.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "crimes-legislation-amendment-serious-and-organised-crime-act-2010.pdf, p.170",
      "values:originalText": "(7) A person may be found guilty of an offence because of the\noperation of this section even if:\n\n(a) another party to the agreement has not been prosecuted or has\nnot been found guilty; or\n\n(b) the person was not present when any of the conduct\nconstituting the physical elements of the joint offence was\nengaged in.\nSpecial liability provisions apply",
      "skos:definition": "(7) A person may be found guilty of an offence because of the\noperation of this section even if:\n\n(a) another party to the agreement has not been prosecuted or has\nnot been found guilty; or\n\n(b) the person was not present when any of the conduct\nconstituting the physical elements of the joint offence was\nengaged in.\nSpecial liability provisions apply",
      "values:partOf": {
        "@id": "concept:crimes-legislation-amendment-serious-and-organised-crime-act-2010-sch-4-sec-166"
      },
      "cml:asserts": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:crimes-legislation-amendment-serious-and-organised-crime-act-2010-sch-4-sec-166-ss-7-norm"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:crimes-legislation-amendment-serious-and-organised-crime-act-2010-sch-4-sec-166-ss-7-logic-deontic-1"
        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "8338932c98225d5328c437dae73d1f663bfef70ad811a9929c1bc7a2f53550d9",
      "skos:note": "A person may be found guilty of an offence despite another party not being prosecuted or present."
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/crimes-legislation-amendment-serious-and-organised-crime-act-2010#sch-4-sec-166-ss-7",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "166(7) Crimes Legislation Amendment (Serious and Organised Crime) Act",
